m","date":"2026-07-07T18:45:05Z"},"message":"feat(sdk): add NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra harness profile (#4192)\n\nDeep Agents now includes a built-in harness profile for NVIDIA Nemotron\n3 Ultra model specs across NVIDIA/ChatNVIDIA, Baseten, Fireworks,\nOpenRouter, Nebius, and Together. The profile adds prompt guidance,\ntool-call compatibility repairs, loop-control nudges, and final-answer\nguards for agentic workloads without changing other models on those\nproviders.\n\n---\n\n- Add Nemotron-specific system-prompt suffix for observed agent\nbehaviors: tool grounding, loop control, domain-vs-filesystem tool\nselection, state-changing actions, final-answer completeness, follow-up\ndefaults, and context compaction.\n- Override the `read_file` tool description to make pagination\nexpectations explicit for whole-file reads.\n- Add tool-call and provider-compatibility repair middleware:\n`NemotronToolCallShim` rewrites `path` to `file_path`, supplies a\ndefault `read_file` limit, and normalizes empty tool results;\n`ChatNVIDIAMessageCompatibilityMiddleware` mirrors LangChain tool-call\nmetadata into the shape ChatNVIDIA expects.\n- Add execution-repair middleware for common Nemotron 3 Ultra outputs:\n`NemotronTextToolCallParser` converts available text-form tool calls\ninto structured tool calls, `NemotronReasoningTagCleanupMiddleware`\npreserves leaked `<think>` blocks as reasoning metadata,\n`ToolRetryMiddleware` retries filesystem tools once, and\n`ModelRateLimitRetryMiddleware` retries likely provider 429s with short\nbackoff.\n- Add progress, policy, follow-up, entity-resolution, and final-answer\nguards that nudge or retry once for repeated tool loops, wrong\ntool-family selection, redundant follow-up questions, unresolved entity\nIDs, and vague final answers after successful mutation tools.\n\n## Caveats\n\n- The `read_file` continuation notice is intentionally heuristic:\nexactly-at-limit output is treated as potentially incomplete, even\nthough a file can end exactly on that boundary.\n- The progress and guard middleware can add one extra model turn, or\nreturn a fallback from gathered tool results after the configured\nbudgets are exceeded, rather than continuing indefinitely.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"c0933e0d4cca8768aa211b27e311fd9fe021cfaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c0933e0d4cca8768aa211b27e311fd9fe021cfaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d5a60ece7379c37c81edcef2cd6c2811ddc90c9a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTUkxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAapIQAGPJ2DubE4dQmOmme7FaVULr\njc/EkD8T4ugmcmjnHXVwt6cJfn0GYBNuNyLuj5OdWrFJ7J536KJRSCmPR5eofCdt\nN9q36/stmdawXO5vKIuc4tApey5+ZXDh1eXIx+UE2V07Id7YHs1k5QJ4zObnIyzv\n2wfnOMwhc+cNtXE/GNpLGugbAdB2i5Nf4MRnozEkgBqMnY7XJReTKp7lSnhgEeZI\n5v1QaY3Zw3aw3K1Ew1Re+ipnDGs8AgR6yG3yy+FH6uKkBvasWj9BIlkCJyzpT1U+\n6IzuI7nTxAUPOigFJyW4ApVM6KB0c+uYVAGd1PgkW0XosL+VAOYGmAB4NE5EXEjd\nu13K4GXr/7ABAieBTyLTY+jMCHXwYe/L7dVdC9/De+ypQnrx9bJNfR/zMnP5j08G\nrrUe3vjCpkSVjxIUgJ93wHDun2CJARoK8nNUiXlMKcHUtVNAPLPZ+oFnkip6Nbak\nVL+SFsro0mVJ3DJhQz2uyIjqgR93V73RHEq6OclgOyrxl6dZOdcym+GrQ5D20fqd\nFW4Z5ZWvC4w6xfKR80OYT116JSu9S9NqaFt99fFn3NPpBuMI0hHQwz3rYC0UeiNl\nbRuPwuY1Gb4xp+VUoNl3Wq2k074tATT6Qyrq94RSlUaJfQkSjCpHrIgZHs/cgQpp\n3HFxHftjpWwbXHfsJ5MS\n=afZ3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c0933e0d4cca8768aa211b27e311fd9fe021cfaf\nparent 35199ab22b2111474d1f46b3ad7cc677d82ed46b\nauthor Srimanth Tangedipalli <srimanth.tangedipalli@langchain.dev> 1783449905 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783449905 -0400\n\nfeat(sdk): add NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra harness profile (#4192)\n\nDeep Agents now includes a built-in harness profile for NVIDIA Nemotron\n3 Ultra model specs across NVIDIA/ChatNVIDIA, Baseten, Fireworks,\nOpenRouter, Nebius, and Together. The profile adds prompt guidance,\ntool-call compatibility repairs, loop-control nudges, and final-answer\nguards for agentic workloads without changing other models on those\nproviders.\n\n---\n\n- Add Nemotron-specific system-prompt suffix for observed agent\nbehaviors: tool grounding, loop control, domain-vs-filesystem tool\nselection, state-changing actions, final-answer completeness, follow-up\ndefaults, and context compaction.\n- Override the `read_file` tool description to make pagination\nexpectations explicit for whole-file reads.\n- Add tool-call and provider-compatibility repair middleware:\n`NemotronToolCallShim` rewrites `path` to `file_path`, supplies a\ndefault `read_file` limit, and normalizes empty tool results;\n`ChatNVIDIAMessageCompatibilityMiddleware` mirrors LangChain tool-call\nmetadata into the shape ChatNVIDIA expects.\n- Add execution-repair middleware for common Nemotron 3 Ultra outputs:\n`NemotronTextToolCallParser` converts available text-form tool calls\ninto structured tool calls, `NemotronReasoningTagCleanupMiddleware`\npreserves leaked `<think>` blocks as reasoning metadata,\n`ToolRetryMiddleware` retries filesystem tools once, and\n`ModelRateLimitRetryMiddleware` retries likely provider 429s with short\nbackoff.\n- Add progress, policy, follow-up, entity-resolution, and final-answer\nguards that nudge or retry once for repeated tool loops, wrong\ntool-family selection, redundant follow-up questions, unresolved entity\nIDs, and vague final answers after successful mutation tools.\n\n## Caveats\n\n- The `read_file` continuation notice is intentionally heuristic:\nexactly-at-limit output is treated as potentially incomplete, even\nthough a file can end exactly on that boundary.\n- The progress and guard middleware can add one extra model turn, or\nreturn a fallback from gathered tool results after the configured\nbudgets are exceeded, rather than continuing indefinitely.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-07T18:45:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d5a60ece7379c37c81edcef2cd6c2811ddc90c9a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d5a60ece7379c37c81edcef2cd6c2811ddc90c9a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d5a60ece7379c37c81edcef2cd6c2811ddc90c9a/comments","author":{"login":"srimanthtangedipalli-eng","id":280118819,"node_id":"U_kgDOELJGIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/280118819?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/srimanthtangedipalli-eng","html_url":"https://github.com/srimanthtangedipalli-eng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/srimanthtangedipalli-eng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/srimanthtangedipalli-eng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/srimanthtangedipalli-eng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/srimanthtangedipalli-eng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/srimanthtangedipalli-eng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/srimanthtangedipalli-eng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/srimanthtangedipalli-eng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/srimanthtangedipalli-eng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/srimanthtangedipalli-eng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https:/