ally at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T23:01:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5c47bdbdda889693fa060bc30b6b486d0f0e0bcf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5c47bdbdda889693fa060bc30b6b486d0f0e0bcf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5c47bdbdda889693fa060bc30b6b486d0f0e0bcf/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0289dd0a190e5060e631e840da115dd59c64cf5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0289dd0a190e5060e631e840da115dd59c64cf5c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0289dd0a190e5060e631e840da115dd59c64cf5c"}]},{"sha":"0289dd0a190e5060e631e840da115dd59c64cf5c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDAyODlkZDBhMTkwZTUwNjBlNjMxZTg0MGRhMTE1ZGQ1OWM2NGNmNWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Kennedy","email":"65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-06T22:29:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T22:29:38Z"},"message":"feat(talon): add Fleet zip import command (#4493)\n\nAdds `deepagents-talon import-fleet` so Fleet zip exports can be\nmaterialized into a normal Talon local assistant directory. The importer\nwrites prompts, skills, subagent prompts, and MCP setup handoff notes\nwhile rejecting unsafe zip paths, symlinks, missing root prompts,\nmalformed tool manifests, and unsafe subagent names.\n\nThis is useful when an assistant starts in Fleet but needs to run\nlocally through Talon channels, cron, and local MCP configuration. For\nexample, the `crowbar.zip` sample can be imported into a `crowbar`\nassistant and then run with Telegram:\n\n```bash\nuv run --directory libs/talon --extra media deepagents-talon import-fleet \\\n  examples/talon/crowbar.zip \\\n  --assistant-id crowbar\n\nAGENT_ASSISTANT_ID=crowbar AGENT_MODEL=<provider>:<model-id> \\\n  uv run --directory libs/talon --extra media deepagents-talon --telegram\n```\n\nFleet `tools.json` remains import input only. When Fleet MCP tools are\npresent, Talon writes `.mcp.json.setup` as operator guidance;\n`.mcp.json` remains the runtime MCP config file.\n\n## Release note\n\nTalon now supports `deepagents-talon import-fleet <fleet-export.zip>` to\nimport Fleet zip exports into a local Talon agent directory, including\nMCP setup notes and local subagent prompt loading.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","tree":{"sha":"817d60f31cf55a3457341b8872ff06c4e17af7f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/817d60f31cf55a3457341b8872ff06c4e17af7f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0289dd0a190e5060e631e840da115dd59c64cf5c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTCxSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkFwQAGlo1z24zoiWvTwdESCAoeSb\nmSpN6fsEIfYzd8tFwrEJV23/8hYjzXGugrwIAIQC1ruJ3SOrGkZQY8zSwtZTEGGd\njJNfbtIzfkqotYzwlYmuNkj9WLJaYCZz7vuTTt9o2DL+yIyLTjqZ4LPyfkrNsKAg\nDFIZLNs5wU46wJ5vZw1MCpUpbSKIxddIp5G9t1fbp6UyL1CAAr2Qiwq1Fnjitmr2\nCM0Jdm276L2fazyrCyVCxW9f3RGJA9U2mtpZvM9vUXDVZRdVTNL4qrp8q9yK+4ke\nNPdnmOObLmFRoJ2RaVk8YvR1l1dV3w7RGsaRSFRAGD36J0XDhSKz0Ts8PfNlRsdE\nOlTwn4yEpZP+9/fFVb3eA5tHXspXNuJ5GtlJ5LfotviQr90bkVmgWoa52DqxdjP4\n8FNJNRisWI+AfWwFM2RvoHW6LUa0w5j/7C0FUROTl4KMHreGDvdeoeWuaYGNBrbS\n/0oz58VgaRstoV127VwHTiez+L4BHllZA+3XI/0LciBwS/mxQk5rR42ge+FDVXO/\nTClbCjhVGl3lxiTNzb40gk1BJot4wf0Mm8MuMOm0sIjkX+DWHvvS8U83W/YtN7Tk\nefMN35lritJAih0oKAE6I5/gPGF5qYxCcb352qQWGqQz/Woxn9pMRR3Nwrh29G1R\nne/cS1pzJgD5g6gLZIeP\n=QcIJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 817d60f31cf55a3457341b8872ff06c4e17af7f9\nparent d62534c86b87a91aca16c6bfb71209232d69a6ec\nauthor John Kennedy <65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com> 1783376978 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783376978 +0000\n\nfeat(talon): add Fleet zip import command (#4493)\n\nAdds `deepagents-talon import-fleet` so Fleet zip exports can be\nmaterialized into a normal Talon local assistant directory. The importer\nwrites prompts, skills, subagent prompts, and MCP setup handoff notes\nwhile rejecting unsafe zip paths, symlinks, missing root prompts,\nmalformed tool manifests, and unsafe subagent names.\n\nThis is useful when an assistant starts in Fleet but needs to run\nlocally through Talon channels, cron, and local MCP configuration. For\nexample, the `crowbar.zip` sample can be imported into a `crowbar`\nassistant and then run with Telegram:\n\n```bash\nuv run --directory libs/talon --extra media deepagents-talon import-fleet \\\n  examples/talon/crowbar.zip \\\n  --assistant-id crowbar\n\nAGENT_ASSISTANT_ID=crowbar AGENT_MODEL=<provider>:<model-id> \\\n  uv run --directory libs/talon --extra media deepagents-talon --telegram\n```\n\nFleet `tools.json` remains import input only. When Fleet MCP tools are\npresent, Talon writes `.mcp.json.setup` as operator guidance;\n`.mcp.json` remains the runtime MCP config file.\n\n## Release note\n\nTalon now supports `deepagents-talon import-fleet <fleet-export.zip>` to\nimport Fleet zip exports into a local Talon agent directory, including\nMCP setup notes and local subagent prompt loading.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T22:29:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0289dd0a190e5060e631e840da115dd59c64cf5c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0289dd0a190e5060e631e840da115dd59c64cf5c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0289dd0a190e5060e631e840da115dd59c64cf5c/comments","author":{"login":"jkennedyvz","id":65985482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTg1NDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65985482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz","html_url":"https://github.com/jkennedyvz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d62534c86b87a91aca16c6bfb71209232d69a6ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d62534c86b87a91aca16c6bfb71209232d69a6ec","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d62534c86b87a91aca16c6bfb71209232d69a6ec"}]},{"sha":"d62534c86b87a91aca16c6bfb71209232d69a6ec","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ2MjUzNGM4NmI4N2E5MWFjYTE2YzZiZmI3MTIwOTIzMmQ2OWE2ZWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T22:29:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T22:29:36Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): accept list format for skill `allowed-tools` (#4140)\n\n`SkillsMiddleware` now accepts YAML lists and comma-separated strings\nfor the `allowed-tools` SKILL.md frontmatter field.\n\n---\n\nSKILL.md `allowed-tools` is commonly authored as a YAML list, but the\nparser only accepted string values and warned for every list-valued\nskill. The parsed value is display-only, so list-valued input should be\naccepted instead of treated as noisy metadata. This accepts YAML lists,\nskips non-string or blank list items, trims kept entries, and continues\nwarning only for unsupported scalar values.\n\nThis also makes description and compatibility truncation warnings more\nactionable by including the field name, file path, actual length, and\nconfigured limit.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/20213c86-9ee8-55a4-53ca-733e3aca91b7)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3b48904f3ff43bba5e0cae3c5bf8f1beb1175e62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3b48904f3ff43bba5e0cae3c5bf8f1beb1175e62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d62534c86b87a91aca16c6bfb71209232d69a6ec","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTCxQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAf4gQAAcIHMubHNCvYP3pcyGxHbxv\nJL39AZEFNKk4VpYrJCOq2JNaZhLfFj82G1PzpqQuXuTVar/TVItG+pJ5+Cta2tfr\nG0uJ8aklW1V5nqRqJuUB3xKsjtwj9DW1EwPjM4Ij4vO5MK+C02yO6E+Kmh+Hsd2E\nWtpIS3kIb4KUJMQHCLrI+Se/cWWmE3XXDDFZ+DmENBo58oRcNpczwJ5ESrwjl67J\niP7FUF+c9utKVl5RKOCHGmVqvgrTDSM8oiKpQshejbawG7NXn6ysFF/QTfwi6qc4\n7xTpBzoewq5PiHL3iXCD3kOjI8mHrinXuVaAKYRklllH6U++wHgOBvk/Mq6SNomm\nmqN4zm6IkNaIlNbYyoXN9iiIX0X6qIBRWHupeSNd1Nn2ZkDPCzzjgcTyxDnrHRgk\nszJZyZWxZjNYq0VOOArCQotCrnJ3s0C3CNEvPTvIyypia45bFYhNP6Iq7Ifx3Mp2\nWbkuNPcsihbszik4ZedojT8fVieUPR/Z1F+DiTccIEVWAb+q2cyLXt5FTZxbGfaB\nE9B07lUTF0oH4jjQt/5OGr1LpxjdkLM91Dp72kct/zCTdUp5grY86tsOB1Rw/Yff\nwhjLqDklZYRlcVpc8XBR0iOPvbhS19jaRiYGxDdJuW3zq0qFoMkmES+x7G1vj11a\nE0nezUbW5TwsNmHiVGox\n=4hFH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3b48904f3ff43bba5e0cae3c5bf8f1beb1175e62\nparent 2f5f5b85793d944167a42e8d5b8e0a11bb1e3932\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783376976 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783376976 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): accept list format for skill `allowed-tools` (#4140)\n\n`SkillsMiddleware` now accepts YAML lists and comma-separated strings\nfor the `allowed-tools` SKILL.md frontmatter field.\n\n---\n\nSKILL.md `allowed-tools` is commonly authored as a YAML list, but the\nparser only accepted string values and warned for every list-valued\nskill. The parsed value is display-only, so list-valued input should be\naccepted instead of treated as noisy metadata. This accepts YAML lists,\nskips non-string or blank list items, trims kept entries, and continues\nwarning only for unsupported scalar values.\n\nThis also makes description and compatibility truncation warnings more\nactionable by including the field name, file path, actual length, and\nconfigured limit.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/20213c86-9ee8-55a4-53ca-733e3aca91b7)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T22:29:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d62534c86b87a91aca16c6bfb71209232d69a6ec","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d62534c86b87a91aca16c6bfb71209232d69a6ec","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d62534c86b87a91aca16c6bfb71209232d69a6ec/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2f5f5b85793d944167a42e8d5b8e0a11bb1e3932","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2f5f5b85793d944167a42e8d5b8e0a11bb1e3932","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2f5f5b85793d944167a42e8d5b8e0a11bb1e3932"}]},{"sha":"2f5f5b85793d944167a42e8d5b8e0a11bb1e3932","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJmNWY1Yjg1NzkzZDk0NDE2N2E0MmU4ZDViOGUwYTExYmIxZTM5MzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T22:24:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T22:24:57Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): make skill truncation warnings actionable (#4141)\n\nSkill description/compatibility truncation warnings now explain the\nlimit, the impact, and how to fix the SKILL.md frontmatter.\n\n---\n\nThe `SkillsMiddleware` truncation warnings (e.g. `Description exceeds\n1024 characters in .../SKILL.md, truncating`) only named the limit, so\nusers couldn't tell why they were warned or how to fix it. The messages\nnow report the actual field length, the Agent Skills spec limit, the\nimpact (only the truncated text reaches the model when it decides\nwhether to use the skill), and exactly which SKILL.md frontmatter field\nto shorten.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d7d1b4e8-caeb-43ec-48f5-35dd5b55e661)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"deb02a606913aa34b5f7ec177c7552e18e49b542","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/deb02a606913aa34b5f7ec177c7552e18e49b542"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2f5f5b85793d944167a42e8d5b8e0a11bb1e3932","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTCs5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACOUQAK0+EAX3lsYr6aG2xyKAN5tQ\n1nhiFJmbZUsx/4R4Ree8iN0ew03bU5xsRSS83ax8dQyXiUWm3v33Mr74EbNutVb0\n69G0C/Tj6sPibACc341PgxcKH/vYWSsCvrUA4afU8vdwNxVSu3+P2gVw358lQzEm\nxEOLxseJwDRHLrfA++g6UM7DU3+hRQZIA7nktrValdmruLvqiYTJ7N2zZUCesIcT\nUyJ93fJwP76wHMSEI7n81MvyiwIm1roO5kDeeyE/SaRNMjCCljZb85NNdVkdRc8v\naEatkCuaY74ULPbkGMp4XH2VR8lqB+0bLZzH8nS96MP70zE+RYrx6D+neQ8PWQK5\nh0ROqLjHsNQLALegVuPr/HGHxXXoTTsoHBjk4x2ikrEO3l/iwHChToSDDF7CYs7H\n0mrAKtiUZowr/69Bk9uJJh2Q3b7uF34GIai/93DpYpF/acadVDcCFC9j0Rqf4ObO\nmrFxeppL0STOK01L17HkjaIZh+dYTvSJ3VijVTTr6WtP2f0M13JdDn7NQkjk+29x\nm0HaEDgzQSBtRY3CxjFZeBIqrKkrQnnowj2K1a3O8z9ohiWvglhGZLt1OZ/DxCev\nlCwiCzkKCaFfocQv5Iq4pTdXMGe7acJftcxlOSaWf/OHCOEckjER9vaz2/oXzYm0\nsPez1fviw73//3gZWPke\n=mQJS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree deb02a606913aa34b5f7ec177c7552e18e49b542\nparent 699e439699723e477a621f95eef87a7d76aac5f5\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783376697 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783376697 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): make skill truncation warnings actionable (#4141)\n\nSkill description/compatibility truncation warnings now explain the\nlimit, the impact, and how to fix the SKILL.md frontmatter.\n\n---\n\nThe `SkillsMiddleware` truncation warnings (e.g. `Description exceeds\n1024 characters in .../SKILL.md, truncating`) only named the limit, so\nusers couldn't tell why they were warned or how to fix it. The messages\nnow report the actual field length, the Agent Skills spec limit, the\nimpact (only the truncated text reaches the model when it decides\nwhether to use the skill), and exactly which SKILL.md frontmatter field\nto shorten.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d7d1b4e8-caeb-43ec-48f5-35dd5b55e661)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T22:24:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2f5f5b85793d944167a42e8d5b8e0a11bb1e3932","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2f5f5b85793d944167a42e8d5b8e0a11bb1e3932","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2f5f5b85793d944167a42e