#4522)\n\nBumps the `deepagents-code` SDK pin to the latest `deepagents` alpha so\nreleased `dcode` installs pick up the newer prerelease SDK.","verified_at":"2026-07-06T15:44:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e2a2151b79b49d5010eda9abaa817b1d0d9821af","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e2a2151b79b49d5010eda9abaa817b1d0d9821af","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e2a2151b79b49d5010eda9abaa817b1d0d9821af/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d77e4f299368d1350e465249384527e045373ee0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d77e4f299368d1350e465249384527e045373ee0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d77e4f299368d1350e465249384527e045373ee0"}]},{"sha":"d77e4f299368d1350e465249384527e045373ee0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ3N2U0ZjI5OTM2OGQxMzUwZTQ2NTI0OTM4NDUyN2UwNDUzNzNlZTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T15:10:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T15:10:42Z"},"message":"docs(repo): document alpha release lockfile steps (#4521)\n\nAlpha release instructions now call out the lockfile refresh required\nafter package version bumps, including the Python version mapping used\nby the repo’s lock-check. The manual release flow also includes a `gh\nworkflow run` example so maintainers can dispatch prerelease builds\nwithout relying on the Actions UI.\n\n## Changes\n- Add a lockfile regeneration step for packages with `uv.lock`, with\nguidance to use Python 3.14 for `acp` and 3.12 for every other package.\n- Update the commit staging example to include package lockfiles when\npresent.\n- Add a GitHub CLI example for dispatching the package release workflow\nfrom an alpha branch.\n- Renumber the manual alpha release verification and cleanup steps after\nthe new lockfile guidance.","tree":{"sha":"2fe8a8979eb41c6079f43971ae3d94adbda78301","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2fe8a8979eb41c6079f43971ae3d94adbda78301"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d77e4f299368d1350e465249384527e045373ee0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS8VyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ6EQAKamRgXA/L+oWOItaRvF/z7v\nzOjeQt5bJP9N2zn8IUyO8Cd4VqhsKQR9/UVwkgZlv/bM5qegSHEhadqbI+zCNvHi\nuhKf3orXg4mQ2Ixzsu+UzXZpyS7w+LiRaLaMrY1ZmqJQJSE6yXUt5RQuk4TOJLP1\noKaIFa+xPSPmszjVjsoY0yxYA+mtk9OP+RIhFfusR3vYfTKHd+wRQDPqbZeuEhEt\n/h2SEy/r8wz64EyQSvAdUeTodAKyFpvEVa5RbQAfrHt/ZpjD+qepuExkx6Nuev7p\nIPXw1L7idI7SRlvvHMvcCliEmQ75AS3N24ks4EygiFtd3FNCAu5vtH9nru2k55fK\njO2U8EsV1VCm1nVPprtYFhfbFkFvK6nDh8RjTpFS9z8IA9m1bgHtHtcweUiiggSk\n96digmoTmKWHUJl6hy5QoBEHdaNwTkffEcvnZJ69VIkAhx5/mTfKrvY81f2Bvvo1\n6I525OXIm16MuuZw5QP8eVfXEjLvwhbYpqHgMAtwJsEbndAXccb3KcgcrjbN8d8Y\ne1ioh90+QwfD8jnejYviUzQixvEY5iqA3X2GvKGBlPaeZDT5UUxAlnsLWvrLPyVN\n2Tzzw8gK4EvcRjp+9g7fw8fe3KaB88wtjW1Kk6B9nWZtT1rQ4XAeIV2KRzO03T87\ndk4htuiTSg1FLMZxI/kZ\n=UhMD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2fe8a8979eb41c6079f43971ae3d94adbda78301\nparent aaa22a9340cb3d2c8e9ce1a921957d0a9121da20\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783350642 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783350642 -0400\n\ndocs(repo): document alpha release lockfile steps (#4521)\n\nAlpha release instructions now call out the lockfile refresh required\nafter package version bumps, including the Python version mapping used\nby the repo’s lock-check. The manual release flow also includes a `gh\nworkflow run` example so maintainers can dispatch prerelease builds\nwithout relying on the Actions UI.\n\n## Changes\n- Add a lockfile regeneration step for packages with `uv.lock`, with\nguidance to use Python 3.14 for `acp` and 3.12 for every other package.\n- Update the commit staging example to include package lockfiles when\npresent.\n- Add a GitHub CLI example for dispatching the package release workflow\nfrom an alpha branch.\n- Renumber the manual alpha release verification and cleanup steps after\nthe new lockfile guidance.","verified_at":"2026-07-06T15:10:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d77e4f299368d1350e465249384527e045373ee0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d77e4f299368d1350e465249384527e045373ee0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d77e4f299368d1350e465249384527e045373ee0/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aaa22a9340cb3d2c8e9ce1a921957d0a9121da20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aaa22a9340cb3d2c8e9ce1a921957d0a9121da20","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aaa22a9340cb3d2c8e9ce1a921957d0a9121da20"}]},{"sha":"aaa22a9340cb3d2c8e9ce1a921957d0a9121da20","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFhYTIyYTkzNDBjYjNkMmM4ZTljZTFhOTIxOTU3ZDBhOTEyMWRhMjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T14:40:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T14:40:20Z"},"message":"feat(code): selective per-server project MCP trust (#4507)\n\nAdd `[mcp].enabled_project_servers` / `disabled_project_servers` (and\nenv equivalents) to selectively pre-approve or reject individual project\nMCP servers by name from user-level config.\n\n---\n\nMirrors Claude Code's `enabledMcpjsonServers` /\n`disabledMcpjsonServers`: a user can pre-approve or reject specific\nproject MCP servers (from a repo's `.mcp.json`) by name via a new\n`[mcp]` `config.toml` table (`enabled_project_servers` /\n`disabled_project_servers`) or the\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ENABLED_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS` / `..._DISABLED_...` env\nvars — without the interactive fingerprint prompt and without trusting\nthe whole config. Reject wins over approval and over full trust.\n\nThe allow/deny lists are read **only** from the user-level\n`~/.deepagents/config.toml` and process env (via the new\n`model_config.load_mcp_server_trust_lists`), never from `.mcp.json` or\nany repo-committed file, so a committed config cannot self-approve its\nown servers. The untrusted path changes from \"drop all\" to \"drop all\nexcept allowlisted\", and only allowlisted (or fully trusted) names\nsurvive into the merged config — so the remote-SSRF /\nheader-exfiltration gate stays intact.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0b9a59e3-2c90-47ce-65f9-efac2532321a)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0b9a59e3-2c90-47ce-65f9-efac2532321a/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"89e46ee8492729d819e5fae9c36441f3c5175fa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/89e46ee8492729d819e5fae9c36441f3c5175fa6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/aaa22a9340cb3d2c8e9ce1a921957d0a9121da20","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS75UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsBgQAAI47vkGIz2gNJ2mjxuXTf2W\nDkQoU3FZz8EcmUxGl65mx4qBjXvTsstYZ0Tqln3Mf/CJgQLjvpzoF0s1JJ3O5CSI\nO6kP24tHdMNFvn9hG5CocVGd450zmrxcEnvcna4oYZRqFgF2u5vk0u3M4/CAsKJC\nXs8nUU9Ezl1H9dT9rhGlY4UA45M9DHyUfYzIWIwJucDcaAzDuwEnK8YUuLPxzjMm\nXX9lqzLvcyPq5OT/8s/C+va2CXZvQkwcGBHwCl0UbXryI2lhExzF0R5FFFVEbtQ1\nRiyQyCUh8m2ogWtow0lu9pjKq9h6DEmUSoHNv5pjZuPWe5RkbTggptJEZmkwjXfj\nmL02OEnB29crDIYNbnsMYfrA4TsmAfcr+f58UqsGHt0zxnjQSfnKbMvi1cKyY5XD\np38ipYvcmXtJ4G0Mx1HSy+3WYDDt0Q6ZDGQrzi1wNqSSHnZkKjUtek/rBy2JzGCl\nznTFs6HU9adyoqIlcPlLQPIuzQEpQbD3CsdecwJ5SchhERKFuSNxLA0rMiGGI/Sj\nZyQm9B7jLzRY0zsdXATHgUuCi8T6BrTOXeielq3w7/dfYLqhBX95MDB6Mytr9VPz\nUxkS/qKlCgqfB1z8ivBtviGCaHNFw1SP/w/SvbUjU2wBIY88mg4B9Nqe5RlWqELj\n3FNlPSP1gNNfYjGE9e7j\n=poZ3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 89e46ee8492729d819e5fae9c36441f3c5175fa6\nparent 5d1c3928f7ca0ea97f28fd4d34ae1a4ee885e888\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783348820 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783348820 -0400\n\nfeat(code): selective per-server project MCP trust (#4507)\n\nAdd `[mcp].enabled_project_servers` / `disabled_project_servers` (and\nenv equivalents) to selectively pre-approve or reject individual project\nMCP servers by name from user-level config.\n\n---\n\nMirrors Claude Code's `enabledMcpjsonServers` /\n`disabledMcpjsonServers`: a user can pre-approve or reject specific\nproject MCP servers (from a repo's `.mcp.json`) by name via a new\n`[mcp]` `config.toml` table (`enabled_project_servers` /\n`disabled_project_servers`) or the\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_ENABLED_PROJECT_MCP_SERVERS` / `..._DISABLED_...` env\nvars — without the interactive fingerprint prompt and without trusting\nthe whole config. Reject wins over approval and over full trust.\n\nThe allow/deny lists are read **only** from the user-level\n`~/.deepagents/config.toml` and process env (via the new\n`model_config.load_mcp_server_trust_lists`), never from `.mcp.json` or\nany repo-committed file, so a committed config cannot self-approve its\nown servers. The untrusted path changes from \"drop all\" to \"drop all\nexcept allowlisted\", and only allowlisted (or fully trusted) names\nsurvive into the merged config — so the remote-SSRF /\nheader-exfiltration gate stays intact.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0b9a59e3-2c90-47ce-65f9-efac2532321a)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0b9a59e3-2c90-47ce-65f9-efac2532321a/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T14:40:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aaa22a9340cb3d2c8e9ce1a921957d0a9121da20","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aaa22a9340cb3d2c8e9ce1a921957d0a9121da20","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aaa22a9340cb3d2c8e9ce1a921957d0a9121da20/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5d1c3928f7ca0ea97f28fd4d34ae1a4ee885e888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5d1c3928f7ca0ea97f28fd4d34ae1a4ee885e888","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5d1c3928f7ca0ea97f28fd4d34ae1a4ee885e888"}]},{"sha":"5d1c3928f7ca0ea97f28fd4d34ae1a4ee885e888","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDVkMWMzOTI4ZjdjYTBlYTk3ZjI4ZmQ0ZDM0YWUxYTRlZTg4NWU4ODg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T14:20:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T14:20:29Z"},"message":"fix(code): re-apply theme preference on `/reload` (#4514)\n\n`/reload` now picks up a theme default saved in another session and\nswitches to it.\n\n---\n\n`/reload` (in `libs/code`) rebuilt the theme *registry*\n(`theme.reload_registry()` + `_register_custom_themes()`) but never\nre-evaluated which theme should be *active* — it never re-ran\n`_load_theme_preference()` or reassigned `self.theme`. So a per-terminal\ndefault (`[ui.terminal_themes][TERM_PROGRAM]`) or global default saved\nby another session was ignored until the app restarted. This re-resolves\nthe preference after the registry reload and applies it (with\nterminal-background sync + CSS refresh), matching startup resolution\norder (env → terminal default → `[ui].theme` → default). Re-applying the\non-disk preference is the intended `/reload` semantic, so it\ndeliberately overrides an unsaved in-session `/theme` choice.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7edbf211-076a-afd0-c0a8-76c44c422e00)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"960afb027ff06caec07d14c362d87e7dbf8881d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/960afb027ff06caec07d14c362d87e7dbf8881d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5d1c3928f7ca0ea97f28fd4d34ae1a4ee885e888","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS7mtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEDcQADwXi/heDrZSy8+y6+kkYqUp\nQAvWjND681vQ7IybH3U0puSPB3A0tz9I8D+ypUKDGX1xek/NmgEvR/oDTLJijXjx\noxXzZymOz5B2Y5plLQlJAzrtItvjoFHoP0dDncUC6ynKSeDJCOTziL0tFu7TNb+D\nQU5YSHQ/zLkDqGmNjxW6UFQJZmFiaMuZb5E3OfYqGc+ENYsBGc4dgjO4qpBe3Tpb\nvxQ4sJEvzqYrcCB+GaJmwuWqfnMWNxKbJCn6RXM4wknjnC+l70cs5r0IsHH2fHf7\nosxg8ftT1R/8VdbgSsLTbMOa8YAtH5kWqdVtZ+ZSpKY81XCqk36IjldoTvbqM15u\nfjJsTCkOChrtXgKbNVfkjXSF7HBbUCMYWo9UZseKW14XteRdKpUynwMO4e2N65bp\nPkwZehc/HcMlv9uEwTgnQDtwlOzYbkkY/5k3ix5PCR/wLG7C844ytcoGPWza4Fxk\nuzq+TsWD8wuTun+uhzSnrbDuXFinV3j5qZl1BupS49fEskar7V4iTj8A98MNnEEM\nifpVL3pRvNRVG+YLqUhRQokAuhmTxKezNKXzzhDmD35j3sYN8FCu5gB3qh8kk1mZ\nLczmALMxyh/PPwluP0wDAkHr1f8TuVbuGSshVBUgCIlgR2urkIi9gYRrY5tKV5+A\nMYgq9YTSja80C87ijX/6\n=lCm3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 960afb027ff06caec07d14c362d87e7dbf8881d8\nparent a4431e4339348431e91533cb2b177259ab94b083\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783347629 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783347629 -0400\n\nfix(code): re-apply theme preference on `/reload` (#4514)\n\n`/reload` now picks up a theme default saved in another session and\nswitches to it.\n\n---\n\n`/reload` (in `libs/code`) rebuilt the theme *registry*\n(`theme.reload_registry()` + `_register_custom_themes()`) but never\nre-evaluated which theme should be *active* — it never re-ran\n`_load_theme_preference()` or reassigned `self.theme`. So a per-terminal\ndefault (`[ui.terminal_themes][TERM_PROGRAM]`) or global default saved\nby another session was ignored until the app restarted. This re-resolves\nthe preference after the registry reload and applies it (with\nterminal-background sync + CSS refresh), matching startup resolution\norder (env → terminal default → `[ui].theme` → default). Re-applying the\non-disk preference is the intended `/reload` semantic, so it\ndeliberately overrides an unsaved in-session `/theme` choice.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/7edbf211-076a-afd0-c0a8-76c44c422e00)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T14:20:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5d1c3928f7ca0ea97f28fd4d34ae1a4ee885e888","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5d1c3928f7ca0ea97f28fd4d34ae1a4ee885e888","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5d1c3928f7ca0ea97f28fd4d34ae1a4ee885e888/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a4431e4339348431e91533cb2b177259ab94b083","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a4431e4339348431e91533cb2b177259ab94b083","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a4431e4339348431e91533cb2b177259ab94b083"}]},{"sha":"a4431e4339348431e91533cb2b177259ab94b083","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE0NDMxZTQzMzkzNDg0MzFlOTE1MzNjYjJiMTc3MjU5YWI5NGIwODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T14:17:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T14:17:58Z"},"message":"feat(code): in-the-moment trust prompt for symlinked skills (#4200)\n\nSkills whose `SKILL.md` resolves outside trusted directories (e.g. via a\nsymlink) can now be approved in the moment via a trust prompt, instead\nof requiring a quit-and-relaunch to edit config. Approved directories\nare persisted to `~/.deepagents/.state/skill_trust.json` and can be\naudited or revoked with `dcode skills trust list|revoke|clear`.\n\n---\n\nToday, invoking a skill whose `SKILL.md` resolves (via symlink) outside\nevery trusted skill root fails hard with a `PermissionError`, and the\nonly way to proceed is to quit, set `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRA_SKILLS_DIRS`\n/ `[skills].extra_allowed_dirs`, and relaunch. This adds an\nin-the-moment approval flow modeled on the existing project-level MCP\ntrust screen.\n\nWhen containment fails, the TUI shows a `SkillTrustScreen` naming the\nskill and the resolved target directory. Allowing reads the skill\nimmediately, persists the resolved target directory to a new trust store\nat `~/.deepagents/.state/skill_trust.json` (managed by\n`skills/trust.py`, mirroring `mcp_trust.py`), and extends the in-session\ncontainment allowlist. Denying is safe and is remembered for the rest of\nthe session so the user is not re-nagged. The non-interactive (`-x`)\npath keeps the existing hard-fail + hint.\n\nTrust is keyed by the resolved target directory — the canonical path\nshown to the user at approval time, stored as-is and never re-resolved.\nTwo distinct post-approval symlink swaps are caught by two distinct\nlayers, so neither grants access the user never approved:\n\n- Re-pointing the *discovery* symlink (the `SKILL.md` path) at a new\ntarget is caught by containment enforcement in `load_skill_content`: the\nnew target is not on the allowlist, so the read is refused and the user\nis re-prompted. The stored trust entry — the original resolved target —\nis untouched.\n- Replacing the *stored* directory itself (or one of its parents) with a\nsymlink is caught by the `resolve()`-to-self re-verification in\n`load_trusted_skill_dirs`, which drops the stale entry rather than\nfollowing the injected symlink to a directory the user never approved.\n\nPersisted approvals join the containment roots in\n`discover_skills_and_roots`, so they apply on subsequent launches.\n`skills trust list|revoke|clear` lets users audit and revoke approved\ndirectories; the declarative `extra_allowed_dirs` / env allowlist still\nworks unchanged as the permanent path.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b71e7066e83cb0df0e402c22e277e97937f66270","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b71e7066e83cb0df0e402c22e277e97937f66270"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a4431e4339348431e91533cb2b177259ab94b083","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS7kWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAG5AQAGWv2xhbtFsVRbclLz0M7E60\n3rhRV44+kSQcfypCU1NpjiHuMQFPWxf3ir98eBgg4GvzRcq1M6LJsQl9j/OJCTqG\nqBFu52LohU9+zhgF1EBl0zHIP6c4RwJI8SoncNVl3Hhs/2C3euGKAZpCpZU3cdam\nYHJQCVTzB0LIfF5HQMPhKnflVj+zDRfuAigxpaE3kC9VM9mJBjYbYNF7U4wZEZEk\na7YZmlc4G4DwgzkGA61Kt/WrbRQpYnaY9OjojAihWG08TE1n6+xC8RKT3qWLDcJE\nEGY5fo9h8BMQlj5idctnH6lgbRfWx+PqsrRF978UB9D0paVo25hqkE6G71tUL9Ep\n6K7F8+j8vBLH41Pdgj9WU98Aff/aUIhd9l3Yuybm09tOaukR/OjnybbH87sxxYqH\nYN2VgCo7XSK/Q9pqnFr5gQHtFufY3eHF/TdeXd5rkslBck6UptZI+xbK9ARb1/4K\n7xU72eJvgdkg9QT3Qf8mE35IDrfwrMQpBwNP/j/h/jZ7Ce+OLsu5geU7jXUon1ud\nWJAM4aHiFPpfJZ3ey4G8euYFJTQwJOeEDASIlwrJ2Z+dYwUqBo1u+blm3n/sv5yU\nn7uyE1KXDwYVhvJEKHqATDXsIwuUyb7W6bToCBAk+uOiZr1xhjBY7sLco5ZqU4KP\n5Y7Z2Jy+IFGghh/0Xwsv\n=IwG0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b71e7066e83cb0df0e402c22e277e97937f66270\nparent d73f36ebaeaaa3c22d60e994bb29d55595c16a36\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783347478 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783347478 -0400\n\nfeat(code): in-the-moment trust prompt for symlinked skills (#4200)\n\nSkills whose `SKILL.md` resolves outside trusted directories (e.g. via a\nsymlink) can now be approved in the moment via a trust prompt, instead\nof requiring a quit-and-relaunch to edit config. Approved directories\nare persisted to `~/.deepagents/.state/skill_trust.json` and can be\naudited or revoked with `dcode skills trust list|revoke|clear`.\n\n---\n\nToday, invoking a skill whose `SKILL.md` resolves (via symlink) outside\nevery trusted skill root fails hard with a `PermissionError`, and the\nonly way to proceed is to quit, set `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRA_SKILLS_DIRS`\n/ `[skills].extra_allowed_dirs`, and relaunch. This adds an\nin-the-moment approval flow modeled on the existing project-level MCP\ntrust screen.\n\nWhen containment fails, the TUI shows a `SkillTrustScreen` naming the\nskill and the resolved target directory. Allowing reads the skill\nimmediately, persists the resolved target directory to a new trust store\nat `~/.deepagents/.state/skill_trust.json` (managed by\n`skills/trust.py`, mirroring `mcp_trust.py`), and extends the in-session\ncontainment allowlist. Denying is safe and is remembered for the rest of\nthe session so the user is not re-nagged. The non-interactive (`-x`)\npath keeps the existing hard-fail + hint.\n\nTrust is keyed by the resolved target directory — the canonical path\nshown to the user at approval time, stored as-is and never re-resolved.\nTwo distinct post-approval symlink swaps are caught by two distinct\nlayers, so neither grants access the user never approved:\n\n- Re-pointing the *discovery* symlink (the `SKILL.md` path) at a new\ntarget is caught by containment enforcement in `load_skill_content`: the\nnew target is not on the allowlist, so the read is refused and the user\nis re-prompted. The stored trust entry — the original resolved target —\nis untouched.\n- Replacing the *stored* directory itself (or one of its parents) with a\nsymlink is caught by the `resolve()`-to-self re-verification in\n`load_trusted_skill_dirs`, which drops the stale entry rather than\nfollowing the injected symlink to a directory the user never approved.\n\nPersisted approvals join the containment roots in\n`discover_skills_and_roots`, so they apply on subsequent launches.\n`skills trust list|revoke|clear` lets users audit and revoke approved\ndirectories; the declarative `extra_allowed_dirs` / env allowlist still\nworks unchanged as the permanent path.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T14:17:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a4431e4339348431e91533cb2b177259ab94b083","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a4431e4339348431e91533cb2b177259ab94b083","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a4431e4339348431e91533cb2b177259ab94b083/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d73f36ebaeaaa3c22d60e994bb29d55595c16a36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d73f36ebaeaaa3c22d60e994bb29d55595c16a36","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d73f36ebaeaaa3c22d60e994bb29d55595c16a36"}]},{"sha":"d73f36ebaeaaa3c22d60e994bb29d55595c16a36","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ3M2YzNmViYWVhYWEzYzIyZDYwZTk5NGJiMjlkNTU1OTVjMTZhMzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T14:14:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T14:14:37Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump `langchain-google-genai` to 4.2.7 (#4518)\n\nUpdates the Deep Agents Code Google GenAI dependency floor to 4.2.7 and\nrefreshes package locks that record the workspace metadata. This keeps\nthe required dependency and optional `google-genai` extra in sync across\nthe affected uv lockfiles.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Bump both the required `langchain-google-genai` dependency and the\n`google-genai` optional extra for Deep Agents Code from `>=4.2.6` to\n`>=4.2.7`.\n- Refresh the `uv.lock` metadata for Deep Agents Code, evals, and talon\nso their package metadata and resolved `langchain-google-genai` artifact\npoint at 4.2.7.","tree":{"sha":"e6e8b88286e1e0f04ce07fc0fbb9582369d71ef7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e6e8b88286e1e0f04ce07fc0fbb9582369d71ef7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d73f36ebaeaaa3c22d60e994bb29d55595c16a36","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS7hNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArEEQAE2JsNOvdCc96QAVcRNntea0\nzs3B+xCtxHcKDP+SM0aIwDLOzHN7q1yAirBFSpx8v+IrBgjn6SsSjdnBKaN93Omk\nn44I2fTyS+C1tolTRn4GrjZEM1xrrhFGvwbbGUowMxHtuYLFQvv7i1GHg47cwj7c\n/WQ1WRrEH0DTb0dsN6//DICYQZaFlSx7nhbKrQxZTMBkwS4gz+NFmlYgU06cUjMR\noyISU264TWBfwbyyckv8VTFpfJZ6EXXcKwxkOW+LaFJIu3PoD6hPv6tpGPXq1xZt\n7SSJSMNQfQzkD+r+wCaXcriE+Sdl5wzVqRaoTSvB3DhN9SMZga/Aha75kdQSKrbg\nd2LIdyZeXQI0JeCAAKothS6BpfW+/ypRtkPCc7qCua9G8AhYEsYogi5Rgy4ozhEZ\nz4QolYGX+VNmSgydnqwzmbzqF2jiEe3minvUAuNpjw3ud7AV3wHz51bOKSfW/s1h\n8N4X8uoFFVDNhP1zr3SxOsdKaQ/zcADroVQx0hStemtv57r9wxojKhfjxKiekAUs\ni6J21hS2qHAigkxVdSg7frhii+nDiE1xVqblc2jOmAxvQ1f8vFXRtSeJUxXhIFJx\nwG+2imQtPnMKX/A55tbdnq+ZfMhQEU4oES3i0ZXQMuOe4MoI1biqej9jlYrJ1TpY\nlp1DElwv1Ioytt9+Rv1Q\n=O9lZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e6e8b88286e1e0f04ce07fc0fbb9582369d71ef7\nparent f2b26a8915fb70c26d32af6e8240442e5e6118e6\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783347277 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783347277 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump `langchain-google-genai` to 4.2.7 (#4518)\n\nUpdates the Deep Agents Code Google GenAI dependency floor to 4.2.7 and\nrefreshes package locks that record the workspace metadata. This keeps\nthe required dependency and optional `google-genai` extra in sync across\nthe affected uv lockfiles.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Bump both the required `langchain-google-genai` dependency and the\n`google-genai` optional extra for Deep Agents Code from `>=4.2.6` to\n`>=4.2.7`.\n- Refresh the `uv.lock` metadata for Deep Agents Code, evals, and talon\nso their package metadata and resolved `langchain-google-genai` artifact\npoint at 4.2.7.","verified_at":"2026-07-06T14:14:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d73f36ebaeaaa3c22d60e994bb29d55595c16a36","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d73f36ebaeaaa3c22d60e994bb29d55595c16a36","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d73f36ebaeaaa3c22d60e994bb29d55595c16a36/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f2b26a8915fb70c26d32af6e8240442e5e6118e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f2b26a8915fb70c26d32af6e8240442e5e6118e6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f2b26a8915fb70c26d32af6e8240442e5e6118e6"}]},{"sha":"f2b26a8915fb70c26d32af6e8240442e5e6118e6","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGYyYjI2YTg5MTVmYjcwYzI2ZDMyYWY2ZTgyNDA0NDJlNWU2MTE4ZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Deep Agent","email":"agent@deepagents.dev","date":"2026-07-06T07:38:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"Deep Agent","email":"agent@deepagents.dev","date":"2026-07-06T07:39:33Z"},"message":"fix(talon): materialize agents under home","tree":{"sha":"f0d114142b5b1810f4268aab895781c144d9d066","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f0d114142b5b1810f4268aab895781c144d9d066"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f2b26a8915fb70c26d32af6e8240442e5e6118e6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f2b26a8915fb70c26d32af6e8240442e5e6118e6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f2b26a8915fb70c26d32af6e8240442e5e6118e6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f2b26a8915fb70c26d32af6e8240442e5e6118e6/comments","author":null,"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"aa0ae36b00df6411a9200610a9075ef2dc28b1af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aa0ae36b00df6411a9200610a9075ef2dc28b1af","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aa0ae36b00df6411a9200610a9075ef2dc28b1af"}]},{"sha":"aa0ae36b00df6411a9200610a9075ef2dc28b1af","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFhMGFlMzZiMDBkZjY0MTFhOTIwMDYxMGE5MDc1ZWYyZGMyOGIxYWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T07:21:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T07:21:35Z"},"message":"fix(code): strip media placeholders from model-facing message text (#4462)\n\n- Display-only `[image N]`/`[video N]` placeholders no longer appear in\nthe model-facing message text or LangSmith trace; only the structured\nmedia block is sent.\n- Manually typing `[image N]`/`[video N]` text that looks like a\nplaceholder no longer triggers atomic deletion on backspace — it edits\ncharacter by character like ordinary text.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user attaches an image or video in the Deep Agents Code TUI, a\ndisplay-only `[image N]` or `[video N]` placeholder appears in the input\narea. The placeholder is purely visual — the actual media travels as a\nstructured content block alongside the text. Two bugs caused that\ndisplay convention to leak into model-facing behavior:\n\n1. **Tracing/model leak:** `create_multimodal_content` copied the raw\ninput text verbatim into the message text block, so the canonical\n`HumanMessage` sent to the model and serialized to LangSmith contained\nthe display-only `[image 1]` as if the user had typed it. It now strips\nonly the exact placeholder tokens bound to media actually attached to\nthat message (via `strip_media_placeholders`), leaving look-alike\nliteral text intact and requiring no escaping mechanism.\n\n2. **Editing false positive:** `ChatTextArea._find_placeholder_span`\ntreated any text matching the placeholder regex as an atomic token, so\nmanually typing `[image 2]` meant a single backspace deleted the whole\ntoken. It now validates each regex match against real state — the media\ntracker for image/video placeholders and `_pasted_contents` for paste\nplaceholders — so only tokens bound to real attachments delete\natomically while typed look-alikes edit character by character.\n\nDisambiguating a display token from a user-typed duplicate of the same\nstring (e.g. attaching an image that gets `[image 1]`, then the user\nalso types `[image 1]` in the same message) requires tracking the exact\ncharacter span of each display token, not just its text. `ImageData` and\n`VideoData` now carry a `placeholder_span` that the tracker updates\nthrough edits via `sync_to_text` (using a diff-based span mapper) and\nre-maps at submit time through text transforms — whitespace trimming,\npaste expansion, prefix prepending — that shift offsets. `add_media`\nalso skips placeholder IDs already present in the draft so a literal\n`[image 1]` in the text doesn't cause a newly attached image to reuse\nthe same ID.\n\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0fc423a2-7100-74d7-2a83-4ea855c9d4bb)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cc4ef65bd93af9e21bedbdb846a5e9964e9d8177","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/cc4ef65bd93af9e21bedbdb846a5e9964e9d8177"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/aa0ae36b00df6411a9200610a9075ef2dc28b1af","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS1d/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ60QAEL7JBXQx0dk7lEPUYg4fPIw\nzcjCd3Pv7nXK+yntx+5oJdcrbQoHqOr2nCglxoBDoPe10Ou2e2qT1IW+13sSuz0r\nnvxFaydtpG63/mKNN4HY+jwkXet1pft2nSHOp/4ScDaUtpWSB+53efebVuaWFLtN\nze6mJmfYRH3wvGGTaNQTBhonp4kjfe3rTgCi+crN7m5pbH3GcJdbjU7VHWAma4GC\nqXd9Gd3hzm2vxNrpV98fz3kuiuEKX8ctdKNLYmKezrvOjUL8FX8ClAiPpERSXkkQ\nB20cgTYhyFOCFnxU2NwNtYPeieBw/cbUmC+aeTxRVUcvPkrqrlsA19C0ftDl8d/Z\nMU8SkjWQwr+Bw3Um9/H0FGkpMXj89XD2Q8Cw74lgNQUlW6QAhTY/VInzOfZfFkjj\nG1ub1G1GrzjNCHNnuhpNvOz8TNWf910lViSOR4W6vM7kfM+Pet0M1vV1E9qDqoFj\nnBkt8fmH04TaPetKoGSgH5Lp+kHdpR82OLBJUB10BYXnubvlHht5eEq+99ldZsyP\nivNBfA9a5q6PbHUa3pyZzFkbRWbBOorV2WctHj5jckMBK/1QXle9cTIdNkctCfXY\nFbK//r/xGLrQ1kn1Nn13iv7Xn9Way6YjsJzXL5VIs8zoTTw4PihgJSIhfr9aX5M6\nf4OS7It3aeAWTpVLUsKR\n=DDAB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cc4ef65bd93af9e21bedbdb846a5e9964e9d8177\nparent 9d4d7ba4eb337359f39e8ffffe7ba95f44b64cf0\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783322495 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783322495 -0400\n\nfix(code): strip media placeholders from model-facing message text (#4462)\n\n- Display-only `[image N]`/`[video N]` placeholders no longer appear in\nthe model-facing message text or LangSmith trace; only the structured\nmedia block is sent.\n- Manually typing `[image N]`/`[video N]` text that looks like a\nplaceholder no longer triggers atomic deletion on backspace — it edits\ncharacter by character like ordinary text.\n\n---\n\nWhen a user attaches an image or video in the Deep Agents Code TUI, a\ndisplay-only `[image N]` or `[video N]` placeholder appears in the input\narea. The placeholder is purely visual — the actual media travels as a\nstructured content block alongside the text. Two bugs caused that\ndisplay convention to leak into model-facing behavior:\n\n1. **Tracing/model leak:** `create_multimodal_content` copied the raw\ninput text verbatim into the message text block, so the canonical\n`HumanMessage` sent to the model and serialized to LangSmith contained\nthe display-only `[image 1]` as if the user had typed it. It now strips\nonly the exact placeholder tokens bound to media actually attached to\nthat message (via `strip_media_placeholders`), leaving look-alike\nliteral text intact and requiring no escaping mechanism.\n\n2. **Editing false positive:** `ChatTextArea._find_placeholder_span`\ntreated any text matching the placeholder regex as an atomic token, so\nmanually typing `[image 2]` meant a single backspace deleted the whole\ntoken. It now validates each regex match against real state — the media\ntracker for image/video placeholders and `_pasted_contents` for paste\nplaceholders — so only tokens bound to real attachments delete\natomically while typed look-alikes edit character by character.\n\nDisambiguating a display token from a user-typed duplicate of the same\nstring (e.g. attaching an image that gets `[image 1]`, then the user\nalso types `[image 1]` in the same message) requires tracking the exact\ncharacter span of each display token, not just its text. `ImageData` and\n`VideoData` now carry a `placeholder_span` that the tracker updates\nthrough edits via `sync_to_text` (using a diff-based span mapper) and\nre-maps at submit time through text transforms — whitespace trimming,\npaste expansion, prefix prepending — that shift offsets. `add_media`\nalso skips placeholder IDs already present in the draft so a literal\n`[image 1]` in the text doesn't cause a newly attached image to reuse\nthe same ID.\n\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0fc423a2-7100-74d7-2a83-4ea855c9d4bb)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T07:21:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aa0ae36b00df6411a9200610a9075ef2dc28b1af","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aa0ae36b00df6411a9200610a9075ef2dc28b1af","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aa0ae36b00df6411a9200610a9075ef2dc28b1af/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9d4d7ba4eb337359f39e8ffffe7ba95f44b64cf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9d4d7ba4eb337359f39e8ffffe7ba95f44b64cf0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9d4d7ba4eb337359f39e8ffffe7ba95f44b64cf0"}]},{"sha":"9d4d7ba4eb337359f39e8ffffe7ba95f44b64cf0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlkNGQ3YmE0ZWIzMzczNTlmMzllOGZmZmZlN2JhOTVmNDRiNjRjZjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T06:45:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T06:45:32Z"},"message":"hotfix(code): fix branch display test truncating at default terminal width (#4512)\n\nThe `test_branch_display_with_feature_branch` test did not specify a\nterminal size, so Textual defaulted to 80×24. The `BranchLabel` widget\ntruncates branch names from the right with an ellipsis when they\noverflow the allocated width — at 80 columns, `feat/new-feature` (17\nchars with icon) was truncated to `↗ feat/new-featu…`, failing the\nsubstring assertion.\n\nAdd `size=(120, 24)` to `run_test()` so the full branch name fits.","tree":{"sha":"50ea97ea66280b648d44f0cde9068b1eab391900","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/50ea97ea66280b648d44f0cde9068b1eab391900"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9d4d7ba4eb337359f39e8ffffe7ba95f44b64cf0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS08MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp5sQAF575g7B+AgmJnwlO7UgOoNy\n9cUXDpK69EHGZEa6MxTzWchUMznqmMCgm4soOE6+mZY5tBmpy1xBYGVt5d+Ms7zW\npEJox8KiKUV+nFfD1fN4RAr/tG4Lml9pJYxf9aC3iqZWbOFMYYh1sGJfmP18Gn6U\nUe83J5B3pR1d6RY0jR6ZjDY0JIEDXIwQpO1gfxNqHiIFrnMxBQSDvT4FHJByfB7V\nX8I/Pn8XjbK8GpS/yzQ9v6hI/hsklxrDrbDwrj65wmvexLjA6g6zP4uKm0q7XQ5J\n00+0t0HQaRRrIr6sbfOO1wu8bSUmptgop1XrwECD3kPqvETLvX7hj/5NDgx2gN0u\nvP7IZvemOhsPz//i66ctzMcy3GLUn8FEdr8a8bufGIRltfW4WzrEf3oQHiFPsYga\nfRGe57tc3yrMaHyTcCZSPLYuPrwZXr4WoWmQSBau4fE6fCl4E6ZZFKiZqi32m3La\nQY05iHON9PMUZVqsqwXgjK/DbVXsCjn+s1kpFm567IuV5E1HftbbYBHD5rvy05Zz\n/Bw1OCqrZvmA/RDPagXmIA3hB00h0rcMT/JAry4ZkZ4BZgEpQ+6CkrJvbjrt/TMJ\n6UTLkpfQ4Kkl/3rdl/7VjKKHHwrbgXoat+5p1dJpnOWKIQ2OcbzNZ02iKNKczbhg\nGoqR4lp2AqwNec6GC8xu\n=Fevd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 50ea97ea66280b648d44f0cde9068b1eab391900\nparent 0dd2e7afe17f90156f1fcd8dabf0f8db56484534\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783320332 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783320332 -0400\n\nhotfix(code): fix branch display test truncating at default terminal width (#4512)\n\nThe `test_branch_display_with_feature_branch` test did not specify a\nterminal size, so Textual defaulted to 80×24. The `BranchLabel` widget\ntruncates branch names from the right with an ellipsis when they\noverflow the allocated width — at 80 columns, `feat/new-feature` (17\nchars with icon) was truncated to `↗ feat/new-featu…`, failing the\nsubstring assertion.\n\nAdd `size=(120, 24)` to `run_test()` so the full branch name fits.","verified_at":"2026-07-06T06:45:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9d4d7ba4eb337359f39e8ffffe7ba95f44b64cf0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9d4d7ba4eb337359f39e8ffffe7ba95f44b64cf0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9d4d7ba4eb337359f39e8ffffe7ba95f44b64cf0/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0dd2e7afe17f90156f1fcd8dabf0f8db56484534","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0dd2e7afe17f90156f1fcd8dabf0f8db56484534","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0dd2e7afe17f90156f1fcd8dabf0f8db56484534"}]},{"sha":"0dd2e7afe17f90156f1fcd8dabf0f8db56484534","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBkZDJlN2FmZTE3ZjkwMTU2ZjFmY2Q4ZGFiZjBmOGRiNTY0ODQ1MzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-06T06:33:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T06:33:42Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.32 (#4511)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.32](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.31...deepagents-code==0.1.32)\n(2026-07-06)\n\n### Features\n\n* Simplify welcome banner to compact box\n([#4482](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4482))\n([b7f46e9](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b7f46e931807f86476c9c2d661dcd4e9623c10a2))\n* Add LangSmith base URL to `/auth`\n([#4228](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4228))\n([88d167f](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/88d167f9ceec1cfadd7c3feac6f63c0da7c893f1))\n* `tool.use` and `tool.result` hook events\n([#3954](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3954))\n([ba1979d](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ba1979d64c3ed5e96ebc896197bc8f97f6f84bac))\n* Fall back to folder name for subagents\n([#4504](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4504))\n([9db3db5](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9db3db5f31a93fb8598a5dc5bedf4fe61fe92c94))\n* Report tracing gateway in `dcode doctor`\n([#4466](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4466))\n([a912427](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a9124275504bc1af5f76dfdd9a6c558c98eea92d))\n* Gate paste auto-collapse behind `display.collapse_pastes`\n([#4473](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4473))\n([ff5dd56](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ff5dd564a3a590e7d2d521b20df495b5e1512e12))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Keep footer branch visible and ellipsized instead of hiding when\nnarrow ([#4506](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4506))\n([ccf30c3](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ccf30c342e5ead677aafd196d8f1ddd2bdf95196))\n* Remove MCP OAuth success page message shift\n([#4463](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4463))\n([69bb06c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/69bb06c0680fa6d37b917deb6b70927c3eff9c09))\n* Prevent `UnicodeEncodeError` crash in non-interactive mode on legacy\nWindows consoles\n([#4478](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4478))\n([b1b16cd](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b1b16cd114d4ee4f077cf5824a0176cd94ebd851))\n\n### Performance Improvements\n\n* Make `threads list` faster on large session databases\n([#4005](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4005))\n([85ca01a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/85ca01a43b002c2bdb4205f48fac5fa6f66a3276))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"56a396f2f473542b836d30fa540df9f2e3ad8bce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/56a396f2f473542b836d30fa540df9f2e3ad8bce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0dd2e7afe17f90156f1fcd8dabf0f8db56484534","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS0xGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhroQADRqar6wuknEs+IdeJ6YPanH\nREVdKMeV/J+ifRDSX2ZdzTEfVHSXeAxN51owhrv6jaRabhXEUk8ckSSZQenGxoZ2\ndxPqEa44W9IMIoRayp0dbJHorat1pdmgyWQj0r57MlX92rD2TPNDdf+I33/7J1c8\nq5pbObohjnsmaRtkpDsazHOwiLYUY4JXR2wdodPOcJ5AaB/anpRBYdYYy4OStsY3\npAO2VjDHs/iXFmFlawD0uta6xhAdYczZg6GMBl+Jk/j8vblFLzqS63azIB4vUfjQ\n9x0zKfAbl7A9JyAbr9fZXIJiPKcsWb9sGzHQnlzNMNcFCwpzK6t5dGfhkNW+3