a93fb8598a5dc5bedf4fe61fe92c94))\n* Report tracing gateway in `dcode doctor`\n([#4466](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4466))\n([a912427](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a9124275504bc1af5f76dfdd9a6c558c98eea92d))\n* Gate paste auto-collapse behind `display.collapse_pastes`\n([#4473](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4473))\n([ff5dd56](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ff5dd564a3a590e7d2d521b20df495b5e1512e12))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Keep footer branch visible and ellipsized instead of hiding when\nnarrow ([#4506](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4506))\n([ccf30c3](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ccf30c342e5ead677aafd196d8f1ddd2bdf95196))\n* Remove MCP OAuth success page message shift\n([#4463](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4463))\n([69bb06c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/69bb06c0680fa6d37b917deb6b70927c3eff9c09))\n* Prevent `UnicodeEncodeError` crash in non-interactive mode on legacy\nWindows consoles\n([#4478](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4478))\n([b1b16cd](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b1b16cd114d4ee4f077cf5824a0176cd94ebd851))\n\n### Performance Improvements\n\n* Make `threads list` faster on large session databases\n([#4005](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4005))\n([85ca01a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/85ca01a43b002c2bdb4205f48fac5fa6f66a3276))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T06:33:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0dd2e7afe17f90156f1fcd8dabf0f8db56484534","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0dd2e7afe17f90156f1fcd8dabf0f8db56484534","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0dd2e7afe17f90156f1fcd8dabf0f8db56484534/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ccf30c342e5ead677aafd196d8f1ddd2bdf95196","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ccf30c342e5ead677aafd196d8f1ddd2bdf95196","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ccf30c342e5ead677aafd196d8f1ddd2bdf95196"}]},{"sha":"ccf30c342e5ead677aafd196d8f1ddd2bdf95196","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNjZjMwYzM0MmU1ZWFkNjc3YWFmZDE5NmQ4ZjFkZGQyYmRmOTUxOTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T05:59:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T05:59:11Z"},"message":"fix(code): keep footer branch visible and ellipsized instead of hiding when narrow (#4506)\n\nThe status-bar footer now keeps the git branch visible at any terminal\nwidth, truncating it with a trailing ellipsis (`…`) instead of\nhard-clipping it or hiding it outright.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, in `libs/code`:\n\n- The branch rendered in an auto-width widget that overflowed its\ncollapsible container and was hard-clipped with no visual cue.\n- `on_resize` hid the branch entirely below 100 cols (70 with\n`HIDE_CWD`), so on a narrow-ish terminal the branch name simply\ndisappeared.\n\nNow:\n\n- `.status-branch` uses a flexible width with `text-overflow: ellipsis`,\nso a too-long branch truncates with a trailing `…` while short names\nstill render in full.\n- The width-based hide is removed: the branch stays visible and\nellipsizes down as the terminal narrows. The `HIDE_GIT_BRANCH` env\noverride still hides it entirely, and the cwd still hides below 70 cols\nto reclaim space (model > cwd priority is unchanged).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/c0006e5f-a4dc-52aa-2fbf-f7979af72ffb)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"94222eb9dfa6c97a7ed327fb375a31d1d67f5078","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/94222eb9dfa6c97a7ed327fb375a31d1d67f5078"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ccf30c342e5ead677aafd196d8f1ddd2bdf95196","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS0QvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPZUQAK10GMsDDycVXLt7uBlEeGY6\nti1Y/yulTEvIGkMbR5K0m95ImB94WWeYkWrG63NiqZR/9Bc2Kxv+ISmzWiwmODVO\nwCSXAIywHg3o8PM82EMG1g4j6sWerGb5Mh+06J1Gr26db7YvLpXDttSP/55xaIJN\niJnZAZFBKfPBtiN/+3KQqLCpSToMktnsyAL2JR4HCCD9uupt1bRynHpG3Z9F8oIF\n7pETJa0J8YDfxykMQys0zkuLRO1hASPg4el2741filpNZAE1uTtLdZ5r74fhXN7F\nihdMuF4vNloCrb9Q2d4Xw3VJhE7i//ENj5ELo8l6EFl++9CWSgLPan/Cy5hg7H+z\na2gj69ipdcOj3j3RdM8B/+nxuIpuzM1PXmX5sy6PZ81+oghgFxBELbyJd40gnyXf\n1PvZOKJxgGB3RuduqVCuutMDrMoTVDe+CsqTXTVck1z+4uNvlEy4i+xYW8sWNzeV\nHeRPbyRGWhsFQkrcGIns+KiIT/kiOYlPGAgOejaab6GrHNh44JR6AFlTk95KZKx2\ndhcsRWaAgDXTtu1qPDsm7/S0+ckJ0XSW6BG0uSlIBngPStz3Q0RUNi6W47R7GJw9\nSBKkEq7HEhO0gfev0bGUsJlofw9+/t1DqiISKQDYDqeJkTAv8n7/RH045uGKaw1B\nQwcLJoF1BIVM2aXpAeZx\n=rCIX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 94222eb9dfa6c97a7ed327fb375a31d1d67f5078\nparent 88d167f9ceec1cfadd7c3feac6f63c0da7c893f1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783317551 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783317551 -0400\n\nfix(code): keep footer branch visible and ellipsized instead of hiding when narrow (#4506)\n\nThe status-bar footer now keeps the git branch visible at any terminal\nwidth, truncating it with a trailing ellipsis (`…`) instead of\nhard-clipping it or hiding it outright.\n\n---\n\nPreviously, in `libs/code`:\n\n- The branch rendered in an auto-width widget that overflowed its\ncollapsible container and was hard-clipped with no visual cue.\n- `on_resize` hid the branch entirely below 100 cols (70 with\n`HIDE_CWD`), so on a narrow-ish terminal the branch name simply\ndisappeared.\n\nNow:\n\n- `.status-branch` uses a flexible width with `text-overflow: ellipsis`,\nso a too-long branch truncates with a trailing `…` while short names\nstill render in full.\n- The width-based hide is removed: the branch stays visible and\nellipsizes down as the terminal narrows. The `HIDE_GIT_BRANCH` env\noverride still hides it entirely, and the cwd still hides below 70 cols\nto reclaim space (model > cwd priority is unchanged).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/c0006e5f-a4dc-52aa-2fbf-f7979af72ffb)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T05:59:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ccf30c342e5ead677aafd196d8f1ddd2bdf95196","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ccf30c342e5ead677aafd196d8f1ddd2bdf95196","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ccf30c342e5ead677aafd196d8f1ddd2bdf95196/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"88d167f9ceec1cfadd7c3feac6f63c0da7c893f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/88d167f9ceec1cfadd7c3feac6f63c0da7c893f1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/88d167f9ceec1cfadd7c3feac6f63c0da7c893f1"}]},{"sha":"88d167f9ceec1cfadd7c3feac6f63c0da7c893f1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg4ZDE2N2Y5Y2VlYzFjZmFkZDdjM2ZlYWM2ZjYzYzBkYTdjODkzZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"open-swe[bot]","email":"215916821+open-swe[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-06T05:53:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T05:53:44Z"},"message":"feat(code): add LangSmith base URL to `/auth` (#4228)\n\nConfigure the LangSmith tracing region/endpoint (US, EU, or a custom\nURL) directly from `/auth` and `dcode auth set langsmith --base-url`.\n\n---\n\nFollowing #4193 (LangSmith tracing in `/auth`), this lets users\nconfigure the LangSmith **endpoint** through `/auth` instead of\nexporting `LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT` by hand — motivated by EU-region users at\n`https://eu.api.smith.langchain.com`.\n\nThe stored LangSmith credential's `base_url` is now applied to\n`LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT` (clearing the `LANGCHAIN_ENDPOINT` alternate) with\nthe same precedence as the stored project: an explicit env value stays\nauthoritative at startup, and the immediate `/auth` save replaces it.\n\n- The `/auth` prompt gains a region selector (`RadioSet`): **United\nStates (default)** / **Europe** / **Custom…**, where Custom reveals a\nfree-text URL field for self-hosted/proxy endpoints.\n- `dcode auth set` gains `--base-url`, accepting the `us`/`eu`\nshorthands or a full URL (a non-interactive flag can't render a radio).\n- Both surfaces validate that a custom endpoint is an `http(s)` URL, so\na key is never paired with a non-HTTP, attacker-shaped endpoint.\n\nRegion aliases normalize to canonical URLs on input, so `auth.json`\nalways stores a real URL (US stores blank → SaaS default). At startup a\nstored key without an endpoint never clears an existing env\n`LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT`, so self-hosted setups keep working.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4f2446ed-36cc-d8e7-a098-3df2bbcf650d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <61371264+mdrxy@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"31fe5784f7c988d3c3b80c6441f644b9fcc476a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/31fe5784f7c988d3c3b80c6441f644b9fcc476a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/88d167f9ceec1cfadd7c3feac6f63c0da7c893f1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS0LoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAawQAFJuLQDe0/WpMTwt558RL7m8\n7owcEs4gC9I0DhV3P6ocJKyeoCsS37/h4bHJIcyWRc2140VySbnsbga8H3Dn7V8e\nGpzCqYI1gelbZJmIDShcPExT8REkUIbYrTbjig+tGBA76muqS+kS8XH/TgL3+aGA\nrpEjtKGB+yJ4MJXhMQL3fp4R6ew6Fb+GW7dzWcikG7t3xQIpH0FZCaxzmua8Hd8u\ncINOcxKjsMkGWg0PAdLgXIU5saWh+8k3lDsQH6jsZy5RwawJuTEJ6LZde2ZU5byv\n7bQ5qN5eOs5KClsWdoa9Gl6fERPKkc24tKpeg6hw3EQlPClfMB+nT2XzLMW3hua8\nWJ+ObfDRiItWBg+AyziFj8IaqD/66zH8iH9PCUP1pVIhwcVLWejseNE4OhiXDJSV\n18wyIaIA15sU9x77Fj6pnTPc7fYX5L33JfqP/NwQ33t2/NIxwXcQ/TEhzlZ3ltC2\nVIgNO74BboZ3xbAvDjF0uJQaCMjZ3/6Jtl9TS3Kmtcn7povaZCqsR8IBhNrfke4h\noMgvG3fpbusZhclhZgGJMJg+jcC/A41kxYkqvIMxi0Q4MuKJiTJRA+TM6gGiVcUg\nRi7x1njZfn8WsJtjuNC1oaXutAYehEr1hOVbxj3vMbyaV24XgdYzjh/IqkgvRv5O\npmBa2ThJyPBsJiRuyZ8W\n=j0+W\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 31fe5784f7c988d3c3b80c6441f644b9fcc476a7\nparent 85ca01a43b002c2bdb4205f48fac5fa6f66a3276\nauthor open-swe[bot] <215916821+open-swe[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1783317224 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783317224 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add LangSmith base URL to `/auth` (#4228)\n\nConfigure the LangSmith tracing region/endpoint (US, EU, or a custom\nURL) directly from `/auth` and `dcode auth set langsmith --base-url`.\n\n---\n\nFollowing #4193 (LangSmith tracing in `/auth`), this lets users\nconfigure the LangSmith **endpoint** through `/auth` instead of\nexporting `LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT` by hand — motivated by EU-region users at\n`https://eu.api.smith.langchain.com`.\n\nThe stored LangSmith credential's `base_url` is now applied to\n`LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT` (clearing the `LANGCHAIN_ENDPOINT` alternate) with\nthe same precedence as the stored project: an explicit env value stays\nauthoritative at startup, and the immediate `/auth` save replaces it.\n\n- The `/auth` prompt gains a region selector (`RadioSet`): **United\nStates (default)** / **Europe** / **Custom…**, where Custom reveals a\nfree-text URL field for self-hosted/proxy endpoints.\n- `dcode auth set` gains `--base-url`, accepting the `us`/`eu`\nshorthands or a full URL (a non-interactive flag can't render a radio).\n- Both surfaces validate that a custom endpoint is an `http(s)` URL, so\na key is never paired with a non-HTTP, attacker-shaped endpoint.\n\nRegion aliases normalize to canonical URLs on input, so `auth.json`\nalways stores a real URL (US stores blank → SaaS default). At startup a\nstored key without an endpoint never clears an existing env\n`LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT`, so self-hosted setups keep working.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4f2446ed-36cc-d8e7-a098-3df2bbcf650d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <61371264+mdrxy@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T05:53:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/88d167f9ceec1cfadd7c3feac6f63c0da7c893f1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/88d167f9ceec1cfadd7c3feac6f63c0da7c893f1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/88d167f9ceec1cfadd7c3feac6f63c0da7c893f1/comments","author":{"login":"open-swe[bot]","id":215916821,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODN6hFQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1395372?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/open-swe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"85ca01a43b002c2bdb4205f48fac5fa6f66a3276","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/85ca01a43b002c2bdb4205f48fac5fa6f66a3276","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/85ca01a43b002c2bdb4205f48fac5fa6f66a3276"}]},{"sha":"85ca01a43b002c2bdb4205f48fac5fa6f66a3276","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDg1Y2EwMWE0M2IwMDJjMmJkYjQyMDVmNDhmYWM1ZmE2ZjY2YTMyNzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T05:29:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T05:29:18Z"},"message":"perf(code): make `threads list` fast on large session databases (#4005)\n\nMakes `dcode threads list` fast on large session databases.\n\nOn a real profile (~12 GB `sessions.db`, 196k checkpoints, 1,505\nthreads) `threads list` took **~60 s**. Profiling showed the cost was\n**not** where it looked — it was the top-level listing query, not the\nper-thread message counts.\n\n## Root cause\n\nLangGraph's `SqliteSaver` stores each checkpoint's full state blob\n**inline in the same `checkpoints` row** as the small `metadata` field.\nThe listing query only reads `metadata` (latest `updated_at`,\n`agent_name`, `git_branch`, `cwd` per thread), but with no covering\nindex SQLite full-scans the table — dragging **11.8 GB of state blobs**\nthrough I/O just to read **234 MB of metadata**. That scan alone\nmeasured **59.6 s**.\n\n## Fix 1 — covering index (primary win)\n\nAdd an idempotent `idx_dcode_threads_list` covering index carrying\nexactly the expressions the `list_threads` `GROUP BY` reads. The planner\nnow answers from the index alone (`SCAN … USING INDEX\nidx_dcode_threads_list`) and never touches the blob-bearing rows.\n\nMeasured on the real DB above:\n\n| | Query time | Plan |\n|---|---|---|\n| Before | **59.6 s** | full scan via PK autoindex (drags 12 GB) |\n| After | **~0.04 s** | index-only scan (~50 MB index) |\n\n- One-time build (~40–60 s, a single table scan) on the first `threads\nlist` for an existing DB; near-zero for new/small DBs.\n- Adds ~50 MB. Index creation is non-fatal on failure (read-only DB /\nlock contention) — the query falls back to the previous scan and logs.\n\n## Fix 2 — linear message-count reconstruction (secondary)\n\nFor delta-channel threads whose latest checkpoint doesn't inline\n`messages`, the count is rebuilt from the `writes` table. The old path\ndeserialized each write in its own `run_in_executor` hop and folded\ndeltas one at a time through `add_messages` — O(n²) per thread. Now each\nchunk is decoded and reduced in a single worker-thread hop, and the\ncommon append/clear history folds in one linear `add_messages` pass.\nSpecific delete-by-ID deltas and any reducer error fall back to the\nexact sequential fold, so displayed counts are unchanged. A 4,000-write\nthread now counts in ~30 ms instead of seconds.\n\n## Robustness & docs\n\n- Per-thread fault isolation: a single malformed thread yields a missing\ncount instead of failing the whole list load.\n- Tightened docstrings: the delete-by-ID fallback is documented as\nconservative (batch and sequential folds agree on the *count* in\npractice; the sequential fold just guarantees it), not a demonstrated\ndivergence.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8fd34dcdebf9f7557cbf9323302e0f9fd37c4a4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8fd34dcdebf9f7557cbf9323302e0f9fd37c4a4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/85ca01a43b002c2bdb4205f48fac5fa6f66a3276","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSz0uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArPwQAA1XTFA92xp6jCeFloqKSGLP\nlr65NJ/Kt0QSDy0kwsPLrHQAhv0dZaNPVoCjzLqJwmLTlWSJFIgHzz9VxU8SkY8n\nk04V0fTPKpz+zZ7kPSpz00OGc0+7aULewtNE9ryZqlnQf3O2hT2ONRvdCBJQucvQ\nmo/UotidF5UZCx4SaR79dmxixHz4yaj6VwCncRpHURkeYKlb47nhyrvViEY1fg3v\n2PDwfyJlHNECCktBD1/mYuuCb+2oznG7CijWSFJU91bLmk4ZDxlg5VVFvoJSso/c\nx1aHUP+pthvyF31fzkk+7QL3JNUQL3N+/SFJp6yV+bgeEbW++YbQodzASks+38j8\nt2hPcJgUsL0mUhFdef1+yMkUzFi62TsMzTzTU5WNg0+CF2O3zYt4RO8uKYl9sgWy\nm9rNUVKrOaK7Nd9QhpBaMN/FglhbqmyYQ94soAQ81QBoQW8nq97thfZ76UT59w4Z\nzpvHJFDGvnBVkNgCFR9NJM53i1lHvrkCY8kt61PG5nKeCgO/wXaK/vxx9DKiBfIy\nGf7jIWRSLgOsQMp7r7Lar/4Js6QPuV6xZJGWu8crwYjxd72TY2pwY8H7NVjx/8/Z\ncjXLHi/84FoW56c5/XBjHsJnkmsnPyZolHIwvRskSd4W5s8w0ZwK6IWVqpTGsBgm\nmFgS9h7nntDBNTLzKQhz\n=ue9e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8fd34dcdebf9f7557cbf9323302e0f9fd37c4a4a\nparent ff5dd564a3a590e7d2d521b20df495b5e1512e12\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783315758 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783315758 -0400\n\nperf(code): make `threads list` fast on large session databases (#4005)\n\nMakes `dcode threads list` fast on large session databases.\n\nOn a real profile (~12 GB `sessions.db`, 196k checkpoints, 1,505\nthreads) `threads list` took **~60 s**. Profiling showed the cost was\n**not** where it looked — it was the top-level listing query, not the\nper-thread message counts.\n\n## Root cause\n\nLangGraph's `SqliteSaver` stores each checkpoint's full state blob\n**inline in the same `checkpoints` row** as the small `metadata` field.\nThe listing query only reads `metadata` (latest `updated_at`,\n`agent_name`, `git_branch`, `cwd` per thread), but with no covering\nindex SQLite full-scans the table — dragging **11.8 GB of state blobs**\nthrough I/O just to read **234 MB of metadata**. That scan alone\nmeasured **59.6 s**.\n\n## Fix 1 — covering index (primary win)\n\nAdd an idempotent `idx_dcode_threads_list` covering index carrying\nexactly the expressions the `list_threads` `GROUP BY` reads. The planner\nnow answers from the index alone (`SCAN … USING INDEX\nidx_dcode_threads_list`) and never touches the blob-bearing rows.\n\nMeasured on the real DB above:\n\n| | Query time | Plan |\n|---|---|---|\n| Before | **59.6 s** | full scan via PK autoindex (drags 12 GB) |\n| After | **~0.04 s** | index-only scan (~50 MB index) |\n\n- One-time build (~40–60 s, a single table scan) on the first `threads\nlist` for an existing DB; near-zero for new/small DBs.\n- Adds ~50 MB. Index creation is non-fatal on failure (read-only DB /\nlock contention) — the query falls back to the previous scan and logs.\n\n## Fix 2 — linear message-count reconstruction (secondary)\n\nFor delta-channel threads whose latest checkpoint doesn't inline\n`messages`, the count is rebuilt from the `writes` table. The old path\ndeserialized each write in its own `run_in_executor` hop and folded\ndeltas one at a time through `add_messages` — O(n²) per thread. Now each\nchunk is decoded and reduced in a single worker-thread hop, and the\ncommon append/clear history folds in one linear `add_messages` pass.\nSpecific delete-by-ID deltas and any reducer error fall back to the\nexact sequential fold, so displayed counts are unchanged. A 4,000-write\nthread now counts in ~30 ms instead of seconds.\n\n## Robustness & docs\n\n- Per-thread fault isolation: a single malformed thread yields a missing\ncount instead of failing the whole list load.\n- Tightened docstrings: the delete-by-ID fallback is documented as\nconservative (batch and sequential folds agree on the *count* in\npractice; the sequential fold just guarantees it), not a demonstrated\ndivergence.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T05:29:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/85ca01a43b002c2bdb4205f48fac5fa6f66a3276","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/85ca01a43b002c2bdb4205f48fac5fa6f66a3276","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/85ca01a43b002c2bdb4205f48fac5fa6f66a3276/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ff5dd564a3a590e7d2d521b20df495b5e1512e12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ff5dd564a3a590e7d2d521b20df495b5e1512e12","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ff5dd564a3a590e7d2d521b20df495b5e1512e12"}]},{"sha":"ff5dd564a3a590e7d2d521b20df495b5e1512e12","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZmNWRkNTY0YTNhNTkwZTdkMmQ1MjFiMjBkZjQ5NWI1ZTE1MTJlMTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T05:10:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T05:10:09Z"},"message":"feat(code): gate paste auto-collapse behind `display.collapse_pastes` (#4473)\n\nAdd `display.collapse_pastes` (`[ui].collapse_pastes` /\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_COLLAPSE_PASTES`) to toggle auto-collapsing of large\nchat-input pastes.\n\n---\n\nThe CLI always collapsed large chat-input pastes into compact `[Pasted\ntext #N]` placeholders. This adds a `display.collapse_pastes` config\noption (env `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_COLLAPSE_PASTES` / `[ui].collapse_pastes`\nin `config.toml`, default enabled) so users can turn the behavior off\nand have pasted text inserted verbatim. The `ChatInput`/`ChatTextArea`\npaste paths now consult the resolved setting before collapsing.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e782ab75-8eb0-1100-d501-1f872b11c286)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"62faec3d65c1b94922c82351bc379d195934dc28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/62faec3d65c1b94922c82351bc379d195934dc28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ff5dd564a3a590e7d2d521b20df495b5e1512e12","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSzixCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJfMQADEyG/HJPd6NsMjvPx/RiQdh\nOhst7t4Z3vg1JDl8lsw+xwHSnQqhEHSYYKZM2e9Hun7hVQ58tUUnppmH/0Cb3opO\n7034VTsg92v524qTcOVhjPfoIIg8Q6aObmEVNnBRHaRX9/vAQxpjCvIirH12FhwG\n3b8NVA5uwms2lPX7phYmiTJxpkZAB6w0tYXygZKkWKbdKAPpv/x2cmMgwZEDbPOq\nrvZVZf5hq2YZDmBNVDcbt96Q/eFk1XJmSe+jl2bl4kam2e6nVkSlg2r9G02u0lnv\nCVeX3Alwy2qw+JqM1OjDivPJONoTScCFaVxB+2SeOho7a7FrGCCaDpUZpvfGQDDv\nppeZkpNncOVoCd77nK4YhtPW3EiCAzYdxyMaoJ9jcgy6+PfHSNW85W5Awvd2M+MX\nxYk1rhzCwnaHcT5L3NK4hCazi0MvIuwtG/SX2BcdENJUovxXX20mDb39QKqM0CSV\nUQmH6j9c0Y0eXuDzovvdSQX7fgA3e8YxKFYix8RBdrIDK95RW/2jhF69TL/kbmmT\nRNxMQ0QD+p26TomFIzMLhYN2gN48VmWKFuzuwSjwIU+5g/hgy8zdDSqL2MmMqLp6\ni9yWQR8MCtCPNrSgJva+2Q4lDv1kN4vHoMNpXD+bF4sDiW3feHmtxG9lCx9utKmI\nEsCI+L+LZJ+SN31W1dUx\n=sM08\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 62faec3d65c1b94922c82351bc379d195934dc28\nparent 7b24e149b2a397330ce74aa36ce43586d04d6b1f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783314609 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783314609 -0400\n\nfeat(code): gate paste auto-collapse behind `display.collapse_pastes` (#4473)\n\nAdd `display.collapse_pastes` (`[ui].collapse_pastes` /\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_COLLAPSE_PASTES`) to toggle auto-collapsing of large\nchat-input pastes.\n\n---\n\nThe CLI always collapsed large chat-input pastes into compact `[Pasted\ntext #N]` placeholders. This adds a `display.collapse_pastes` config\noption (env `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_COLLAPSE_PASTES` / `[ui].collapse_pastes`\nin `config.toml`, default enabled) so users can turn the behavior off\nand have pasted text inserted verbatim. The `ChatInput`/`ChatTextArea`\npaste paths now consult the resolved setting before collapsing.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e782ab75-8eb0-1100-d501-1f872b11c286)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T05:10:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ff5dd564a3a590e7d2d521b20df495b5e1512e12","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ff5dd564a3a590e7d2d521b20df495b5e1512e12","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ff5dd564a3a590e7d2d521b20df495b5e1512e12/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7b24e149b2a397330ce74aa36ce43586d04d6b1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7b24e149b2a397330ce74aa36ce43586d04d6b1f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7b24e149b2a397330ce74aa36ce43586d04d6b1f"}]},{"sha":"7b24e149b2a397330ce74aa36ce43586d04d6b1f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdiMjRlMTQ5YjJhMzk3MzMwY2U3NGFhMzZjZTQzNTg2ZDA0ZDZiMWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Kennedy","email":"65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-06T04:49:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T04:49:10Z"},"message":"chore(talon): remove legacy Fleet direct-run startup path (#4492)\n\nCloses JKB-6\n\n---\n\nRemove the old Fleet direct-run/export-library runtime path from Talon\nso the runtime only serves the local materialized-agent layout. This\nlands the import implementation on a cleaned local-runtime surface\ninstead of carrying the legacy Fleet path forward.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`deepagents_talon/fleet.py`** deleted entirely:\n`FleetAgentComponents`, `load_fleet_agent_components`,\n`StaticSkillsLoader` wiring, and the Fleet MCP-surface logging helpers.\n- **`__main__._agent_runtime`** no longer branches on\n`config.fleet_dir`. The `reload_fleet_components` hook and\n`_runtime_components_from_fleet` helper are gone; `_agent_runtime` now\nonly serves the local MCP / echo path.\n- **`TalonConfig`** loses its `fleet_dir` field and stops reading\n`DEEPAGENTS_TALON_FLEET_DIR`, `AGENT_FLEET_DIR`, and `FLEET_DIR`. Those\nkeys are excluded from `config.env` via `_LEGACY_FLEET_ENV_KEYS` so they\ndon't leak into the runtime; setting them no longer invokes Fleet\nexport-library behavior.\n- **`DeepAgentRuntime`** drops the Fleet OAuth-reload mechanism: the\n`reload_agent_components` constructor param, `_reload_lock`, `reload()`,\n`_reload_after_auth_failure`, the MCP-auth-failure retry branch, and the\n`_structured_auth_failure_state` / `_is_mcp_auth_failure` /\n`_is_auth_failure` helpers plus their `_AUTH_*` / `_MCP_AUTH_*` /\n`_PROVIDER_AUTH_*` marker constants. MCP authorization failures now\nsurface as normal errors and are recovered through the normal local\n`deepagents-talon mcp login` flow after the operator configures\n`.mcp.json`.\n- **`fleet-deepagents-export`** removed from `pyproject.toml`\ndependencies; `uv.lock` regenerated.\n- Tests: deleted `tests/test_fleet.py` and\n`tests/test_import_compat.py`; added\n`test_from_env_drops_legacy_fleet_dir_env` covering all three legacy env\nkeys; removed the four Fleet-reload runtime tests, the\n`AuthFailingGraph` helper, and `reload_agent_components` references.\n- README: replaced the \"Fleet Exports\" how-to with migration guidance\npointing at `deepagents-talon import-fleet`, added an \"MCP\nAuthorization\" section, and dropped Fleet references from the Telegram\nand Tool Approval sections.\n\n## Reviewer notes\n\nThe `RuntimeAgentComponents` dataclass stays exported from\n`deepagents_talon.__init__` — it's still a public type even though\n`runtime.py` no longer constructs it internally. `_status_code` is also\nretained because `_is_retryable` uses it for retryable HTTP-status\ndetection.\n\nRemaining Fleet references are limited to README migration guidance, the\n`deepagents-talon import-fleet` pointer, an incidental\n`FLEET_OAUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN` string in a backend env-sanitization test (an\narbitrary secret-named env var, not Fleet code), and historical\nCHANGELOG entries managed by release-please — all per the issue's\nallow-list.\n\n## Test plan\n\n`make test` (190 passed), `make lint` (ruff check + format clean), `make\ntype` (ty clean) in `libs/talon`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","tree":{"sha":"fb2ae3d6d56f83245c711ff672553f6ca89cde74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/fb2ae3d6d56f83245c711ff672553f6ca89cde74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7b24e149b2a397330ce74aa36ce43586d04d6b1f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSzPGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoSIQAFOAfaEhsLaEXuwotpWXsNS5\nBra2EAvoRPyTKjBRr5JhkVDcuYVHzDdni2NbGbvz3lwhXRFAVzqvTmSBSgad6jm4\nCGMyachvr0lhOvBr1dyAgl+FXljEE1azQP1vVpFBkKzjVHqJJw1tMSAEfs7KVYK0\n9bzbOQuanUKTzC2G6D4KMkNJK2VInAr4+EZMfFq7P+ncDKE1zP7c4pjJ5NmE0BKm\nHMkrNTETDuskUkCYdA4Zn4fDCkA1wcsfXe/drZEBTme/4+sCbQbvS6nW1L9Aczm0\nhRRsKjnjVtzXwfegslYzzIExYn9CPhdbAAhpr7cAi6nosYMjBBS5CVW1gpNZkDiF\n3DzgJIKE8Xxhi5VH3N3LAXDO71L3EHYHIX1HtjK8r5r+b2o9iBl+Iwfn1/2Sx2Fw\nD4tV7bZwqRfZqhksrA2+ExeF4xYRrYt3gVF/3mgJ1zHXWV+NG7e8bvz7zqzBF3xF\nY9DOzB5/H2GZPpGv47fjQDuyaf8yDJtbmTSvQuVUxXw1Rab61upvsbh11GIxBV9w\nv2JOHK4IKUoguT37kCI+vg0H+Al0Baq3hrLtadPN467jIATXnoVYe7WTh7dXYj4h\n9GUnncVZ5pin1u1dejL2niF/Tq6CLhzvJ9cBLhQZBxO4+ZaMzd4T7GEFQB2c5s0p\n9C07/WQV/qH+rPD0jy5A\n=uyvU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fb2ae3d6d56f83245c711ff672553f6ca89cde74\nparent a9124275504bc1af5f76dfdd9a6c558c98eea92d\nauthor John Kennedy <65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com> 1783313350 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783313350 -0400\n\nchore(talon): remove legacy Fleet direct-run startup path (#4492)\n\nCloses JKB-6\n\n---\n\nRemove the old Fleet direct-run/export-library runtime path from Talon\nso the runtime only serves the local materialized-agent layout. This\nlands the import implementation on a cleaned local-runtime surface\ninstead of carrying the legacy Fleet path forward.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`deepagents_talon/fleet.py`** deleted entirely:\n`FleetAgentComponents`, `load_fleet_agent_components`,\n`StaticSkillsLoader` wiring, and the Fleet MCP-surface logging helpers.\n- **`__main__._agent_runtime`** no longer branches on\n`config.fleet_dir`. The `reload_fleet_components` hook and\n`_runtime_components_from_fleet` helper are gone; `_agent_runtime` now\nonly serves the local MCP / echo path.\n- **`TalonConfig`** loses its `fleet_dir` field and stops reading\n`DEEPAGENTS_TALON_FLEET_DIR`, `AGENT_FLEET_DIR`, and `FLEET_DIR`. Those\nkeys are excluded from `config.env` via `_LEGACY_FLEET_ENV_KEYS` so they\ndon't leak into the runtime; setting them no longer invokes Fleet\nexport-library behavior.\n- **`DeepAgentRuntime`** drops the Fleet OAuth-reload mechanism: the\n`reload_agent_components` constructor param, `_reload_lock`, `reload()`,\n`_reload_after_auth_failure`, the MCP-auth-failure retry branch, and the\n`_structured_auth_failure_state` / `_is_mcp_auth_failure` /\n`_is_auth_failure` helpers plus their `_AUTH_*` / `_MCP_AUTH_*` /\n`_PROVIDER_AUTH_*` marker constants. MCP authorization failures now\nsurface as normal errors and are recovered through the normal local\n`deepagents-talon mcp login` flow after the operator configures\n`.mcp.json`.\n- **`fleet-deepagents-export`** removed from `pyproject.toml`\ndependencies; `uv.lock` regenerated.\n- Tests: deleted `tests/test_fleet.py` and\n`tests/test_import_compat.py`; added\n`test_from_env_drops_legacy_fleet_dir_env` covering all three legacy env\nkeys; removed the four Fleet-reload runtime tests, the\n`AuthFailingGraph` helper, and `reload_agent_components` references.\n- README: replaced the \"Fleet Exports\" how-to with migration guidance\npointing at `deepagents-talon import-fleet`, added an \"MCP\nAuthorization\" section, and dropped Fleet references from the Telegram\nand Tool Approval sections.\n\n## Reviewer notes\n\nThe `RuntimeAgentComponents` dataclass stays exported from\n`deepagents_talon.__init__` — it's still a public type even though\n`runtime.py` no longer constructs it internally. `_status_code` is also\nretained because `_is_retryable` uses it for retryable HTTP-status\ndetection.\n\nRemaining Fleet references are limited to README migration guidance, the\n`deepagents-talon import-fleet` pointer, an incidental\n`FLEET_OAUTH_ACCESS_TOKEN` string in a backend env-sanitization test (an\narbitrary secret-named env var, not Fleet code), and historical\nCHANGELOG entries managed by release-please — all per the issue's\nallow-list.\n\n## Test plan\n\n`make test` (190 passed), `make lint` (ruff check + format clean), `make\ntype` (ty clean) in `libs/talon`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T04:49:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7b24e149b2a397330ce74aa36ce43586d04d6b1f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7b24e149b2a397330ce74aa36ce43586d04d6b1f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7b24e149b2a397330ce74aa36ce43586d04d6b1f/comments","author":{"login":"jkennedyvz","id":65985482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTg1NDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65985482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz","html_url":"https://github.com/jkennedyvz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a9124275504bc1af5f76dfdd9a6c558c98eea92d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a9124275504bc1af5f76dfdd9a6c558c98eea92d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a9124275504bc1af5f76dfdd9a6c558c98eea92d"}]},{"sha":"a9124275504bc1af5f76dfdd9a6c558c98eea92d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE5MTI0Mjc1NTA0YmMxYWY1Zjc2ZGZkZDlhNmM1NThjOThlZWE5MmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T04:48:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T04:48:00Z"},"message":"feat(code): report tracing gateway in `dcode doctor` (#4466)\n\n`dcode doctor` now shows a `Gateway` line under Tracing indicating\nwhether traces route through the LangSmith managed gateway.\n\n---\n\nBrian asked to know, at a glance, whether `dcode` is tracing to the\nLangSmith managed gateway or to a custom dev/staging endpoint. This adds\na `Gateway` line under the Tracing section of `dcode doctor` (shown when\ntracing is enabled): `yes` when traces route through the LangSmith\nmanaged/SaaS gateway (`*.smith.langchain.com`, including the default\n`https://api.smith.langchain.com` when no custom endpoint is set), `no`\nfor a self-hosted/dev/staging endpoint. The existing `Endpoint` line\nalready surfaces the custom URL itself.\n\nAssumption worth confirming: \"gateway\" is defined as any host under\n`smith.langchain.com` (matches the codebase's existing gateway-host\nconvention). If LangChain's internal dev/staging uses a subdomain of\n`smith.langchain.com`, it would read as `yes` — happy to narrow it if\nthat's not the intended cut.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/61952749-6cc0-a57e-8fe4-c151d099735e)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2dd6cbd3eb1332501663aa92086d3aea6888c9e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2dd6cbd3eb1332501663aa92086d3aea6888c9e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a9124275504bc1af5f76dfdd9a6c558c98eea92d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSzOACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMwkQACF3uo7+B3i9ZWkR8sYQT0Zw\nVryeLNpV9Fzv1PTFOUjQD+5sU3WTva+mSmufPGHEIsmcrRvwbQ7Bwo83A/XBr0PK\nDJg1wkwaknKptgXe4lXx8jc5j+vaYDFCwZp0Y4rLePueRygjy8eQbM45Kl+WoOSz\ne5pNHYTexFttpnn7qP4R7ahvbFsG8F5ORgHfqdY6TUedbAri1ClLfcYhYCOyk2q6\nJjkVDlN5ZqoUHuZUOGFDeR2NIM2g3fc1U1rwCx4Utk4s8/vMlKBlIGuQTvQPKPmY\n+1SnxKDxFDREnTQjx/vADFMl1HylvNU3R7NzmWGx2Tvge3xpkFy7raVR9Lmq+15L\ngRYpuumR/YEFplTkDD24anbrRHGSGoXg63sXGuMCkh/lvnIfc5leX2VPlfc3UMJ1\nlBGYeV1LvNCqJr8l7tsARbzfW0J24nNA5sFLPG03RJzcENBZRo7RvSeV/ruRKUpb\nouaIOPcZjkqcLfc5HiKPaMZqGgblSw3cOo/kM1qOXSH82X9rZduJOTMM4+a3ECQ1\ntQw0IyjJnpr7jdSdE+7GcId6piQO7LribTOmyMgKB11r6e5s5hNQv1N79pyBxCKC\nyRTV9wIG6a5iVlz2Z46OUQMHHw0g7okGxzbPm+3+TjgCdxCLAVgmKJWCJYLhaIxX\nb+V3rkGT9+pb7ODq3458\n=VUp5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2dd6cbd3eb1332501663aa92086d3aea6888c9e2\nparent b1b16cd114d4ee4f077cf5824a0176cd94ebd851\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783313280 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783313280 -0400\n\nfeat(code): report tracing gateway in `dcode doctor` (#4466)\n\n`dcode doctor` now shows a `Gateway` line under Tracing indicating\nwhether traces route through the LangSmith managed gateway.\n\n---\n\nBrian asked to know, at a glance, whether `dcode` is tracing to the\nLangSmith managed gateway or to a custom dev/staging endpoint. This adds\na `Gateway` line under the Tracing section of `dcode doctor` (shown when\ntracing is enabled): `yes` when traces route through the LangSmith\nmanaged/SaaS gateway (`*.smith.langchain.com`, including the default\n`https://api.smith.langchain.com` when no custom endpoint is set), `no`\nfor a self-hosted/dev/staging endpoint. The existing `Endpoint` line\nalready surfaces the custom URL itself.\n\nAssumption worth confirming: \"gateway\" is defined as any host under\n`smith.langchain.com` (matches the codebase's existing gateway-host\nconvention). If LangChain's internal dev/staging uses a subdomain of\n`smith.langchain.com`, it would read as `yes` — happy to narrow it if\nthat's not the intended cut.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/61952749-6cc0-a57e-8fe4-c151d099735e)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T04:48:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a9124275504bc1af5f76dfdd9a6c558c98eea92d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a9124275504bc1af5f76dfdd9a6c558c98eea92d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a9124275504bc1af5f76dfdd9a6c558c98eea92d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b1b16cd114d4ee4f077cf5824a0176cd94ebd851","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b1b16cd114d4ee4f077cf5824a0176cd94ebd851","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b1b16cd114d4ee4f077cf5824a0176cd94ebd851"}]},{"sha":"b1b16cd114d4ee4f077cf5824a0176cd94ebd851","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGIxYjE2Y2QxMTRkNGVlNGYwNzdjZjU4MjRhMDE3NmNkOTRlYmQ4NTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mohamed Amine NAJI","email":"122235965+Superstos@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-06T04:27:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T04:27:12Z"},"message":"fix(code): prevent `UnicodeEncodeError` crash in non-interactive mode on legacy Windows consoles (#4478)\n\nFixes #4476\n\n---\n\nOn Windows, when stdout is a legacy console using a locale code page\n(e.g. cp1252), `dcode -n` crashes before producing any output: the first\n`console.print()` containing a Unicode glyph (`âœ“ Server ready`,\n`non_interactive.py`) raises `UnicodeEncodeError` through rich's legacy\nWindows renderer. The error handler then crashes the same way trying to\nprint the error, so the run dies with a wall of tracebacks â€” or, when\noutput is redirected, looks like a silent hang.\n\nRepro (Windows, cp1252 console, v0.1.22-0.1.31):\n```\ndcode -n \"say hi\" --no-mcp\nUnicodeEncodeError: 'charmap' codec can't encode character 'âœ“' in position 0\n```\n\n## Fix\n\nReconfigure `sys.stdout`/`sys.stderr` with `errors=\"replace\"` at\n`run_non_interactive` entry. Unencodable characters degrade to `?`\ninstead of killing the run; the stream encoding itself is untouched.\nStreams without `reconfigure` (e.g. `StringIO` in tests) are left as-is.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"394d23e521e7b04b3e321945b8ec1895f3c65afc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/394d23e521e7b04b3e321945b8ec1895f3c65afc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b1b16cd114d4ee4f077cf5824a0176cd94ebd851","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSy6gCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuFIQAHaSeuTQJzrPFfY7163QLSvy\nsfNbhTzwAnR3iTWJRHE+eIaWGqubhhdLwAbnw/ACa7VkgvcvmGrVsHTeqHIQhD3s\nZnmMfhaXH8ksXC3lP8usjCG59Jq+CvpLSnPqOcmeQNitf3H/+6CLXR6w119ZiBU3\nnPziIBZa6TTg+EG2GHYutSyGdilgALQ8Bj+gHUZPO8XLZYnkNK1A9ehEGefanfSM\nc3BFPh7vetXWGYNy9+eK135uz9ujp0PSPga8H2KPMkBT4x1zs/durY7G9F5d0qGi\nhr2II8XqewJpUnXHo0cctuGnunZuj35SHEqvJFn2WjCokVLuvpotIu06zbJOcWrE\n+CZk2ErfuEHw8Z5NEATz8jD7ES1V4NA2sJ6cXtzoQumab2ON2kXArdICfA60TirV\nrckgbbx+gfhnjIFR9Hnce1GdT2ze8TFk1BXtMe0jBbixW5L96i1aRD61kDv9o2an\nMb6iItylLt7Q/BggFKGfBu7Jk0nB7RwJW7GwqsBy9svkG6VJ0tKfcnr9+Ehh4pRv\n8LnbalHk7n0VtQfAtExWjUkzFhxB14JP36RLu4lfw7Nm30ntfvyYGw6SX4GkJxt/\n2w/B7YWcBkTLPqKnO8zenL6oXB405eFKox7eMFCremxa8zrMhCrEKSaUPxkUqSeu\np8DH4L2Nce+wdTX1dxdP\n=peVy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 394d23e521e7b04b3e321945b8ec1895f3c65afc\nparent b7f46e931807f86476c9c2d661dcd4e9623c10a2\nauthor Mohamed Amine NAJI <122235965+Superstos@users.noreply.github.com> 1783312032 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783312032 -0400\n\nfix(code): prevent `UnicodeEncodeError` crash in non-interactive mode on legacy Windows consoles (#4478)\n\nFixes #4476\n\n---\n\nOn Windows, when stdout is a legacy console using a locale code page\n(e.g. cp1252), `dcode -n` crashes before producing any output: the first\n`console.print()` containing a Unicode glyph (`âœ“ Server ready`,\n`non_interactive.py`) raises `UnicodeEncodeError` through rich's legacy\nWindows renderer. The error handler then crashes the same way trying to\nprint the error, so the run dies with a wall of tracebacks â€” or, when\noutput is redirected, looks like a silent hang.\n\nRepro (Windows, cp1252 console, v0.1.22-0.1.31):\n```\ndcode -n \"say hi\" --no-mcp\nUnicodeEncodeError: 'charmap' codec can't encode character 'âœ“' in position 0\n```\n\n## Fix\n\nReconfigure `sys.stdout`/`sys.stderr` with `errors=\"replace\"` at\n`run_non_interactive` entry. Unencodable characters degrade to `?`\ninstead of killing the run; the stream encoding itself is untouched.\nStreams without `reconfigure` (e.g. `StringIO` in tests) are left as-is.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T04:27:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b1b16cd114d4ee4f077cf5824a0176cd94ebd851","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b1b16cd114d4ee4f077cf5824a0176cd94ebd851","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b1b16cd114d4ee4f077cf5824a0176cd94ebd851/comments","author":{"login":"Superstos","id":122235965,"node_id":"U_kgDOB0ksPQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122235965?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Superstos","html_url":"https://github.com/Superstos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Superstos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Superstos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Superstos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Superstos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Superstos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Superstos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Superstos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Superstos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Superstos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b7f46e931807f86476c9c2d661dcd4e9623c10a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b7f46e931807f86476c9c2d661dcd4e9623c10a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b7f46e931807f86476c9c2d661dcd4e9623c10a2"}]},{"sha":"b7f46e931807f86476c9c2d661dcd4e9623c10a2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI3ZjQ2ZTkzMTgwN2Y4NjQ3NmM5YzJkNjYxZGNkNGU5NjIzYzEwYTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T03:51:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T03:51:46Z"},"message":"feat(code): simplify welcome banner to compact box (#4482)\n\nThe startup welcome banner was a large multi-section panel — ASCII art\ntitle, a \"Ready to code!\" subheader, a randomly selected tip, LangSmith\ntracing links (including replica projects), editable-install path, and\nMCP status. On a fresh launch with an empty chat, Textual's\nbottom-anchor behavior floated this panel to the bottom of the viewport,\nleaving dead space above it — unlike Claude Code, which greets the user\ntop-aligned.\n\nThis PR replaces the banner with a compact bordered box and fixes the\nviewport anchoring so the banner sits at the top on launch.\n\nThe new box shows `dcode` (bold) and the version tag. Rows below the\ntitle appear only when their data is present:\n\n    dcode  v0.1.0\n\n    tracing:   'shared-deepagents-code'\n    mcp:       42 tools\n\nThe model and working-directory rows are opt-in (`SPLASH_SHOW_MODEL` /\n`SPLASH_SHOW_CWD`, both off by default) — the model already lives in the\nstatus bar and the cwd in the prompt. The thread ID row appears only in\ndebug mode. MCP server warnings (unauthenticated, errored, awaiting\nreconnect) still surface as yellow alert lines inside the box, and the\neditable-install path shows for local installs.\n\nRemoved: rotating tips and the `build_welcome_footer()` helper, the\n\"Ready to code!\" subheader, replica tracing project display, and\n`HIDE_SPLASH_TIPS`. `set_idle()` / `set_connecting()` are now no-ops —\nthe status bar owns connection progress and failure messaging.\n\n`_ChatScroll.anchor()` no longer bottom-anchors at startup. The real\nanchor is deferred until chat content overflows the viewport, so the\nbanner stays pinned to the top on an empty chat and the chat follows the\nbottom once it fills up. Streaming, shell output, slash-command output,\nand thread-resume paths opt into bottom-follow as content arrives.\n\n`_sync_status_model` now updates the banner's model display (when\nenabled) in addition to the status bar, so `/model` switches are\nreflected everywhere. Cwd changes also flow through `update_cwd()`. Both\nlookups guard against `ScreenStackError` when the banner isn't mounted.\n\n## Release note\n\nThe startup welcome banner is now a compact bordered box instead of a\nmulti-section panel. Tips, the \"Ready to code!\" subheader, and replica\ntracing project lines have been removed. The banner stays top-aligned in\nan empty chat instead of floating to the bottom. Two new opt-in settings\n— `SPLASH_SHOW_MODEL` and `SPLASH_SHOW_CWD` (env:\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SPLASH_SHOW_MODEL` / `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SPLASH_SHOW_CWD`)\n— control whether the active model and working directory appear as rows\nin the banner.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"212c7e6a696be7b827f3539df713247cf567f21c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/212c7e6a696be7b827f3539df713247cf567f21c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b7f46e931807f86476c9c2d661dcd4e9623c10a2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSyZSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQrwQAIOa6m8y6iakFY8Gp25PDukp\nIOo8ZIjaruzxO2InhfE4GEA5uPINnjQVqc07NeuxmoV1r2o6blJki7QidJovAvKT\njCk98d2s8ySaUc/MKbgxcwenSU3wbxuZp7JchA4o1Plqku7tzsoiaSPZt9i9gf1n\nkUB9kS/EINUQiPe77pFVQHf3byYLSffxmEHhQvd65888lxSwUHPWxdjS/saYvKBK\nqD1tZYS4VReNcJooeoNCSr+qCDB2m/eVV6vZ0zan4FkROdlsbIWwtNKB2U+N+ybW\n7gfEevdNp55oqzz7U8zWLlYCKouEiUFNPFhNrYu2kUzd+Y+ZO00W1wi2pZs8n+ai\nMP01psfGvWOn8z/N6IegEhvTZ38xWlabXqG4BK7w8wbRTbAsz+6Ed6s8uH9zw4r9\nvMB2NyZFU43mDurwNoytSIfHs+s86WSq9l5NYZbOChL/Q3BE221sLCTfmwRRNYSO\nKgRUmKFTF6uq+2amaE4ZQemd9VaCv3ZL1c+drgrex0yD4Dlx2s6E7qQSm1M4/SHl\nk9lLxN1uflwgEQu/BeFzVq0RWnxK7e8QfcDhxq5drBuEcWeh1vE7C1g56juXPehA\nUnnKMoxklGv67htMYFAT5e6O/WyGzplUnUF2gk1BPfin16lgrPVEf81IJ0wPgtki\nXjYa5GY8H3JuTGH+cbBF\n=2raj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 212c7e6a696be7b827f3539df713247cf567f21c\nparent 69bb06c0680fa6d37b917deb6b70927c3eff9c09\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1783309906 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783309906 -0400\n\nfeat(code): simplify welcome banner to compact box (#4482)\n\nThe startup welcome banner was a large multi-section panel — ASCII art\ntitle, a \"Ready to code!\" subheader, a randomly selected tip, LangSmith\ntracing links (including replica projects), editable-install path, and\nMCP status. On a fresh launch with an empty chat, Textual's\nbottom-anchor behavior floated this panel to the bottom of the viewport,\nleaving dead space above it — unlike Claude Code, which greets the user\ntop-aligned.\n\nThis PR replaces the banner with a compact bordered box and fixes the\nviewport anchoring so the banner sits at the top on launch.\n\nThe new box shows `dcode` (bold) and the version tag. Rows below the\ntitle appear only when their data is present:\n\n    dcode  v0.1.0\n\n    tracing:   'shared-deepagents-code'\n    mcp:       42 tools\n\nThe model and working-directory rows are opt-in (`SPLASH_SHOW_MODEL` /\n`SPLASH_SHOW_CWD`, both off by default) — the model already lives in the\nstatus bar and the cwd in the prompt. The thread ID row appears only in\ndebug mode. MCP server warnings (unauthenticated, errored, awaiting\nreconnect) still surface as yellow alert lines inside the box, and the\neditable-install path shows for local installs.\n\nRemoved: rotating tips and the `build_welcome_footer()` helper, the\n\"Ready to code!\" subheader, replica tracing project display, and\n`HIDE_SPLASH_TIPS`. `set_idle()` / `set_connecting()` are now no-ops —\nthe status bar owns connection progress and failure messaging.\n\n`_ChatScroll.anchor()` no longer bottom-anchors at startup. The real\nanchor is deferred until chat content overflows the viewport, so the\nbanner stays pinned to the top on an empty chat and the chat follows the\nbottom once it fills up. Streaming, shell output, slash-command output,\nand thread-resume paths opt into bottom-follow as content arrives.\n\n`_sync_status_model` now updates the banner's model display (when\nenabled) in addition to the status bar, so `/model` switches are\nreflected everywhere. Cwd changes also flow through `update_cwd()`. Both\nlookups guard against `ScreenStackError` when the banner isn't mounted.\n\n## Release note\n\nThe startup welcome banner is now a compact bordered box instead of a\nmulti-section panel. Tips, the \"Ready to code!\" subheader, and replica\ntracing project lines have been removed. The banner stays top-aligned in\nan empty chat instead of floating to the bottom. Two new opt-in settings\n— `SPLASH_SHOW_MODEL` and `SPLASH_SHOW_CWD` (env:\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SPLASH_SHOW_MODEL` / `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SPLASH_SHOW_CWD`)\n— control whether the active model and working directory appear as rows\nin the banner.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T03:51:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b7f46e931807f86476c9c2d661dcd4e9623c10a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b7f46e931807f86476c9c2d661dcd4e9623c10a2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b7f46e931807f86476c9c2d661dcd4e9623c10a2/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"69bb06c0680fa6d37b917deb6b70927c3eff9c09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/69bb06c0680fa6d37b917deb6b70927c3eff9c09","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/69bb06c0680fa6d37b917deb6b70927c3eff9c09"}]},{"sha":"69bb06c0680fa6d37b917deb6b70927c3eff9c09","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY5YmIwNmMwNjgwZmE2ZDM3YjkxN2RlYjZiNzA5MjdjM2VmZjljMDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T03:51:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T03:51:15Z"},"message":"fix(code): remove MCP OAuth success page message shift (#4463)\n\nThe MCP OAuth loopback callback success page rewrote its message text\n~1.5s after load (after a best-effort `window.close()`), producing a\nvisible text \"shift\" on the page. Since the static message (\"MCP\nauthorization complete. You can close this tab and return to your\nterminal.\") already reads correctly whether or not the tab closes, this\ndrops the DOM `textContent` rewrite (and the now-unused\n`id=\"oauth-message\"`) and keeps only the best-effort `window.close()`.\nThe message no longer changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Complete an MCP OAuth login where the browser is OS-opened (normal\ncase) and confirm the success page text stays constant (no shift) and\nthe tab does not falsely disappear.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/bcb41636-7d5a-faf8-0728-553ffa8c14e9)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a32f9f6b84c1318a3b4105e71781fc28b0d06188","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a32f9f6b84c1318a3b4105e71781fc28b0d06188"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/69bb06c0680fa6d37b917deb6b70927c3eff9c09","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSyYzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPVUQAJBg/UVXBPfqfD5I7MxDZpPj\nfID+fLdxp5ScGheQ1U0aQ9eB4M0d6YsqgxRETI4U7PlXelmiQZR+woSdlA8zG46L\nPGsBFaCfl2lUDCqa9EhepXRvlj3qv/mf+i8h5+FxqT2Gq0uuOOAI9mTYlffVG0s8\nw850tOjzECq4ci3regqU4JFZVxnAbn7or+eqmPBssy+0eDOfYDTcr8+1twggjz83\nY9SaPfGL4jgJQcDPSXD4vAZ/lVl3XdB+0v1064SItsDxWOTIIbhW7cSk84gki1l+\n9NPXIf7GEmqv+mj0Ksr2uFPnb3itW9Qy3HSk8LWiNm3ogZFCJoT2oie5As1bf3Jy\n5dnczOWt0WMrfKR2GzY9rnkGjRsx+neWkgoeW7EGiT9dg3jiEQYW6mSpw3QEoqY+\nPtC9Z/hg2RxchqWF85LrN5EPzjlOGUAWibCcXh1x1JA7rhlkvaboh+OuUXGc4EDD\nve+edDwM/x3WxVkRI8MVqrBbz/2W/OWs218yhJIQqoftb0ENXVokFzDY5qW3ITiY\n2nKsg6HV0lc8sKuPB54bp4pEPrkCMbC3BYM6QtL6GnPczXojnZFlgN3/OLBfwV2M\nddxkBM1Go+yldhKDl/IVexcA8D2myo5YxdVb0CfV23/yxcm8A+/kbDApfTwKCOfH\nTXOaIvbsJqsUTkXYfeOm\n=uZdQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a32f9f6b84c1318a3b4105e71781fc28b0d06188\nparent cd21d57969b4255eeaeb5b390d52694ee4575748\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783309875 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783309875 -0400\n\nfix(code): remove MCP OAuth success page message shift (#4463)\n\nThe MCP OAuth loopback callback success page rewrote its message text\n~1.5s after load (after a best-effort `window.close()`), producing a\nvisible text \"shift\" on the page. Since the static message (\"MCP\nauthorization complete. You can close this tab and return to your\nterminal.\") already reads correctly whether or not the tab closes, this\ndrops the DOM `textContent` rewrite (and the now-unused\n`id=\"oauth-message\"`) and keeps only the best-effort `window.close()`.\nThe message no longer changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Complete an MCP OAuth login where the browser is OS-opened (normal\ncase) and confirm the success page text stays constant (no shift) and\nthe tab does not falsely disappear.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/bcb41636-7d5a-faf8-0728-553ffa8c14e9)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T03:51:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/69bb06c0680fa6d37b917deb6b70927c3eff9c09","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/69bb06c0680fa6d37b917deb6b70927c3eff9c09","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/69bb06c0680fa6d37b917deb6b70927c3eff9c09/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cd21d57969b4255eeaeb5b390d52694ee4575748","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cd21d57969b4255eeaeb5b390d52694ee4575748","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cd21d57969b4255eeaeb5b390d52694ee4575748"}]},{"sha":"cd21d57969b4255eeaeb5b390d52694ee4575748","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNkMjFkNTc5NjliNDI1NWVlYWViNWIzOTBkNTI2OTRlZTQ1NzU3NDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-06T03:39:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T03:39:19Z"},"message":"chore(code): remove /theme labels/keys tip from welcome footer (#4505)\n\nRemoves the rotating welcome-footer tip \"In /theme, press N to toggle\nlabels/keys, T to set for the current terminal\" from the `_TIPS` list in\nthe code TUI welcome widget, as requested.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/9df0d7d8-bcf8-d9e8-aa9e-7f2c850129de)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab0514ee546e6d9c2358d3f1ec11882f9a964a52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ab0514ee546e6d9c2358d3f1ec11882f9a964a52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/cd21d57969b4255eeaeb5b390d52694ee4575748","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSyNnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwHoQAI67rrhceYWbZQjHW5EfRhOb\nacmh/UyFw1mrsoS/jqLm/7chLqxPGK+IPYyKIbqFl4cDmn9o8lz1YiW609ow6/bw\n265P9+YXoq4mGP2vKoojida4GfCwRq0D/Jv7qYA0Vas1/PODhaunhMmbCaLbiHk7\nEtJIIsZKEg2lvRIyvJ5tSEdyijDi4KFuHXTC+AFgXLN1MA0e1rnXwYEGQkPD0Ffi\nW1AHKcpVRfqGfAlp5ritKx+3FwjdTly+8hh0IrBb1qCp48IaYNXcMEg25pEL910B\n39fPFwCgfgKyVjM1tiHtIGDKm1qLfFifL2Kqmdf9RPtm450/y6jQrn1tmmGllomd\n+BMIkcRMwBYNWTHOBloIs20Jmm5TEhHpoxzPdhc3K8VmvsW4HIubNveHwICK/yew\ntDF0uFFLOu89XRw948mLzODEDVu1HeMvdic8E2H9rB0Zm/PN9YTnL7lnD3esziT5\n+qjjd3ANRNGGNqvZzsSxYCiln6nawuOpJSZax/+luycM3JETrN4BfEk2qYl0Ebx2\nEhxv13q0VxlfbnbqZP6vTkKQcdnUOh9p+GIJj3oDolmCEvpA+pqmCtlybkq02xTW\nA8TqdL8E/SB9hF1IgBhXd9FhNS4CPqf8G0S+q5TtwflDobyoLYlQHgFV019F+Wvk\niu5y70tPMolcb+5lDRog\n=q7V+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ab0514ee546e6d9c2358d3f1ec11882f9a964a52\nparent 9db3db5f31a93fb8598a5dc5bedf4fe61fe92c94\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783309159 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783309159 -0400\n\nchore(code): remove /theme labels/keys tip from welcome footer (#4505)\n\nRemoves the rotating welcome-footer tip \"In /theme, press N to toggle\nlabels/keys, T to set for the current terminal\" from the `_TIPS` list in\nthe code TUI welcome widget, as requested.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/9df0d7d8-bcf8-d9e8-aa9e-7f2c850129de)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T03:39:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cd21d57969b4255eeaeb5b390d52694ee4575748","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cd21d57969b4255eeaeb5b390d52694ee4575748","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cd21d57969b4255eeaeb5b390d52694ee4575748/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9db3db5f31a93fb8598a5dc5bedf4fe61fe92c94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9db3db5f31a93fb8598a5dc5bedf4fe61fe92c94","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9db3db5f31a93fb8598a5dc5bedf4fe61fe92c94"}]},{"sha":"9db3db5f31a93fb8598a5dc5bedf4fe61fe92c94","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDlkYjNkYjVmMzFhOTNmYjg1OThhNWRjNWJlZGY0ZmU2MWZlOTJjOTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Kennedy","email":"65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-06T03:36:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-06T03:36:42Z"},"message":"feat(code): fall back to folder name for subagents (#4504)\n\nAllows subagents defined under `agents/{name}/AGENTS.md` to load when\nthe YAML frontmatter omits `name`, using the containing folder name as\nthe implicit name. Explicit invalid `name` values still fail validation,\nand descriptions remain required.\n\n## Spec divergence\n\nThe Agent Skills specification (`deepagents.middleware.skills`) requires\n`name` in frontmatter and enforces that it matches the parent directory\nname exactly — no fallback. This PR relaxes that rule for subagents\nonly: `name` is optional, and the folder name is used when it's absent.\nSubagents are already uniquely identified by their folder, so requiring\na redundant `name` field adds friction without adding information. The\ndivergence is documented in the module and function docstrings in\n`subagents.py`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"5cd1585eb100c053aaece223bb66e538b133e095","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5cd1585eb100c053aaece223bb66e538b133e095"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9db3db5f31a93fb8598a5dc5bedf4fe61fe92c94","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSyLKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6BYQAHJKO1yi4A6lLm2LdukyySW5\nzM+kwcF++NfWnCBtlUDzE1YCdXAAhldtF3K3SP/0vQq0Wr1UthmhZ6YFJHgwm1Au\nIIcX1VW+JbH3hL7Ei2c2B5DuPYTfbsW0AaN9QiDmzQ2MY8FOF/16G8c/bWeKvmTF\neuoQplz4pORKqvvKu7Xwr1p3oGJ3wLvF6zZfvdziom0EIVw4sTt8xb5RSqFOXGZK\nAz6APf8FE+HDeH4kkqjbk9dkVXcsvv4+YdIqvcaKLqeSJE8yUlupFqYvW5YoFYtK\neBMFdRX5K4rK+LDgA2QMHgtNHpTfevWiDPMCY5ZzW3o8Nf7axeunGzNmk05BSzIe\nMqqeTLCqBQzi6zBshwh6cohJ9UmiHimJM1p9MmbKXEb35B+HvF8N/5HgUYx5nl54\nNAapY3sB0fvT8cgQCuN2Dzg4GftuzumNrFMevvgcnQ8Dt26JcdKAFHK2taopGy+t\nSPr9A7LpKLW7hNuTU2bGbDb98IfYcL+qJA/Jj7k9Ux5w7zudAXMWvxb2y3JsXek6\nY81xkEhxnTFq0eXBz/DfJ3uBKAElQGn9NzhG1AAIdGOFzc68BztZfXtYLFEdIzRj\noi+OMITAjsgmrSx9S6v+/XnVO/jHPJcA0M1Gwyt9gbZRcruKJ3KUKbgTEo+RI6zp\nVov3kxCDq+06lEJR81b1\n=SXeJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5cd1585eb100c053aaece223bb66e538b133e095\nparent ba1979d64c3ed5e96ebc896197bc8f97f6f84bac\nauthor John Kennedy <65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com> 1783309002 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783309002 -0400\n\nfeat(code): fall back to folder name for subagents (#4504)\n\nAllows subagents defined under `agents/{name}/AGENTS.md` to load when\nthe YAML frontmatter omits `name`, using the containing folder name as\nthe implicit name. Explicit invalid `name` values still fail validation,\nand descriptions remain required.\n\n## Spec divergence\n\nThe Agent Skills specification (`deepagents.middleware.skills`) requires\n`name` in frontmatter and enforces that it matches the parent directory\nname exactly — no fallback. This PR relaxes that rule for subagents\nonly: `name` is optional, and the folder name is used when it's absent.\nSubagents are already uniquely identified by their folder, so requiring\na redundant `name` field adds friction without adding information. The\ndivergence is documented in the module and function docstrings in\n`subagents.py`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-07-06T03:36:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9db3db5f31a93fb8598a5dc5bedf4fe61fe92c94","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9db3db5f31a93fb8598a5dc5bedf4fe61fe92c94","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9db3db5f31a93fb8598a5dc5bedf4fe61fe92c94/comments","author":{"login":"jkennedyvz","id":65985482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTg1NDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65985482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz","html_url":"https://github.com/jkennedyvz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ba1979d64c3ed5e96ebc896197bc8f97f6f84bac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ba1979d64c3ed5e96ebc896197bc8f97f6f84bac","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ba1979d64c3ed5e96ebc896197bc8f97f6f84bac"}]},{"sha":"ba1979d64c3ed5e96ebc896197bc8f97f6f84bac","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJhMTk3OWQ2NGMzZWQ1ZTk2ZWJjODk2MTk3YmM4Zjk3ZjZmODRiYWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ninaad R. Rao","email":"35262832+NinaadRao@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-05T23:24:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-05T23:24:51Z"},"message":"feat(code): `tool.use` and `tool.result` hook events (#3954)\n\nCloses #3953\n\n---\n\nAdds two hook events — `tool.use` (fires before a tool executes) and\n`tool.result` (fires after) — mirroring Claude Code's\nPreToolUse/PostToolUse hooks. They cover audit logging, notifications,\nguardrails, and latency tracking. Both events are wired into the two\nexecution surfaces — the interactive Textual TUI and the headless (`-p`)\nrunner — so hooks fire consistently regardless of how the agent is\ninvoked. The existing `tool.error` event is untouched and continues to\nfire alongside `tool.result` on failure, so existing hooks are\nunaffected.\n\n**Payloads**\n\n`tool.use` carries `tool_name`, `tool_id`, and the parsed `tool_args`.\n`tool.result` adds `tool_status` (`\"success\"` or `\"error\"`) and\n`tool_output` (the tool's returned content, truncated to a shared\n`HOOK_TOOL_OUTPUT_LIMIT`). The full schema and a worked example live in\nthe `hooks` module docstring.\n\n**Resolving streamed arguments**\n\nTool-call arguments arrive as JSON string fragments while the model\nstreams. Each in-progress call is tracked in a typed `_ToolCallBuffer`,\nand `_parse_tool_call_args` reassembles the fragments; `tool.use`\ndispatches only once the arguments parse into a complete value, so hooks\nreceive the real arguments rather than a partial or empty payload.\nArguments that look structurally complete but still fail to parse are\nlogged rather than silently dropped, so a missed hook is never\ninvisible.\n\n**Dispatch and delivery**\n\nBoth events are dispatched fire-and-forget on both surfaces, so a slow\nhook command never blocks the agent or stalls the UI. Because they run\nas background tasks, each surface drains any in-flight hook tasks before\nits event loop tears down — the headless runner before the process\nexits, and the TUI on app shutdown — so the final `tool.result` is never\ncancelled mid-flight and silently dropped. Both surfaces also emit\n`tool.result` for every executed tool, including a tool call whose\nresult arrives without a rendered widget, so audit consumers see the\nsame event stream in either mode. Rejected HITL approvals that abort a\nturn now emit terminal `tool.error`/`tool.result` events, so hook\nconsumers never observe an unterminated `tool.use` for a tool that did\nnot run.\n\n## Release note\n\nDeep Agents Code now emits `tool.use` and `tool.result` hook events (in\naddition to the existing `tool.error`), fired before and after each tool\ncall in both the interactive TUI and headless (`-p`) modes. Rejected\nHITL approvals also emit terminal hook events when the turn aborts, so\nevery `tool.use` is closed by a matching result or error event.\nConfigure them under `~/.deepagents/hooks.json`; see the `hooks` module\ndocstring for the payload schema.\n\nLinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ninaadrrao/\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"d36cd264bd4ea3f5a2c2fba834ee2fb572a7a648","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d36cd264bd4ea3f5a2c2fba834ee2fb572a7a648"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ba1979d64c3ed5e96ebc896197bc8f97f6f84bac","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSufDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuYwQAEihTlFvCOeJxM8xKKvtbe3q\n09uTc3jC0SFQ8NQTTIpO/WI2YKTBmA3inGRGFjgb+f7XTxFfFOEjSQqdPe3YgtwC\nJ/4pqKAS/AXwRwtZtS0vzr0EDdDZKay3XfedbUhCjsk+Qen6vfWCx2serVmLzzM+\nGgQIr5AzHAeWWTRdnE3O3ffTkEekieJnK5HLBYHvmrwZJGIEjsBDatG1TmjcgFhl\nvDBkeIC4m7JuujkMy9h7SAGf6rk1KSAySvWi2//UweDLQYf+YXijXLxD663h4jNP\n5VUvXQyJV1guAVWofCa6FI4urJzpav43UJnG69IFg5i5lSGtzpn+OCx62v6g2F+e\nlahYiz1PvVzyR5ZOmORFweEJwtmC9mYmtiF5C8HS7uJzht0N4fLKdzmQ0HvreaR9\nRT4TUov78fafha4cByFXiHPN0PKPnV2t7PJntifh6dOAFJRMX4U+refTG8QhyJdU\njx/VHXy4IOWmthzZOaNpYhszoPu89Y/vF/sx230Rt+cVVga3AcRZtPfhntnWoFG4\nzK7XNPiOdERMo3nz4ZOVunP31HqrG7oTYo7HfEL6wqPM+Yd8aLdu2gtn981wUlRX\nIiEHZAXG47IS26YW9EjrvkZgUGjHiCRcMTSzRhWK8yAIMUZXTMdQWrufRKw3fOSl\nO8qOhedcWppAUHjo2yDu\n=2++7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d36cd264bd4ea3f5a2c2fba834ee2fb572a7a648\nparent 59a665f339fd18aa47bc7bb7be7e685b6948e342\nauthor Ninaad R. Rao <35262832+NinaadRao@users.noreply.github.com> 1783293891 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783293891 -0400\n\nfeat(code): `tool.use` and `tool.result` hook events (#3954)\n\nCloses #3953\n\n---\n\nAdds two hook events — `tool.use` (fires before a tool executes) and\n`tool.result` (fires after) — mirroring Claude Code's\nPreToolUse/PostToolUse hooks. They cover audit logging, notifications,\nguardrails, and latency tracking. Both events are wired into the two\nexecution surfaces — the interactive Textual TUI and the headless (`-p`)\nrunner — so hooks fire consistently regardless of how the agent is\ninvoked. The existing `tool.error` event is untouched and continues to\nfire alongside `tool.result` on failure, so existing hooks are\nunaffected.\n\n**Payloads**\n\n`tool.use` carries `tool_name`, `tool_id`, and the parsed `tool_args`.\n`tool.result` adds `tool_status` (`\"success\"` or `\"error\"`) and\n`tool_output` (the tool's returned content, truncated to a shared\n`HOOK_TOOL_OUTPUT_LIMIT`). The full schema and a worked example live in\nthe `hooks` module docstring.\n\n**Resolving streamed arguments**\n\nTool-call arguments arrive as JSON string fragments while the model\nstreams. Each in-progress call is tracked in a typed `_ToolCallBuffer`,\nand `_parse_tool_call_args` reassembles the fragments; `tool.use`\ndispatches only once the arguments parse into a complete value, so hooks\nreceive the real arguments rather than a partial or empty payload.\nArguments that look structurally complete but still fail to parse are\nlogged rather than silently dropped, so a missed hook is never\ninvisible.\n\n**Dispatch and delivery**\n\nBoth events are dispatched fire-and-forget on both surfaces, so a slow\nhook command never blocks the agent or stalls the UI. Because they run\nas background tasks, each surface drains any in-flight hook tasks before\nits event loop tears down — the headless runner before the process\nexits, and the TUI on app shutdown — so the final `tool.result` is never\ncancelled mid-flight and silently dropped. Both surfaces also emit\n`tool.result` for every executed tool, including a tool call whose\nresult arrives without a rendered widget, so audit consumers see the\nsame event stream in either mode. Rejected HITL approvals that abort a\nturn now emit terminal `tool.error`/`tool.result` events, so hook\nconsumers never observe an unterminated `tool.use` for a tool that did\nnot run.\n\n## Release note\n\nDeep Agents Code now emits `tool.use` and `tool.result` hook events (in\naddition to the existing `tool.error`), fired before and after each tool\ncall in both the interactive TUI and headless (`-p`) modes. Rejected\nHITL approvals also emit terminal hook events when the turn aborts, so\nevery `tool.use` is closed by a matching result or error event.\nConfigure them under `~/.deepagents/hooks.json`; see the `hooks` module\ndocstring for the payload schema.\n\nLinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/ninaadrrao/\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-05T23:24:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ba1979d64c3ed5e96ebc896197bc8f97f6f84bac","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ba1979d64c3ed5e96ebc896197bc8f97f6f84bac","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ba1979d64c3ed5e96ebc896197bc8f97f6f84bac/comments","author":{"login":"NinaadRao","id":35262832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjYyODMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35262832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao","html_url":"https://github.com/NinaadRao","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/events{/privacy}","r