}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4cba72893fc4aae5b429d8c573c1a513d97ddf8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4cba72893fc4aae5b429d8c573c1a513d97ddf8a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4cba72893fc4aae5b429d8c573c1a513d97ddf8a"}]},{"sha":"4cba72893fc4aae5b429d8c573c1a513d97ddf8a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRjYmE3Mjg5M2ZjNGFhZTViNDI5ZDhjNTczYzFhNTEzZDk3ZGRmOGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-03T01:56:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-03T01:56:50Z"},"message":"fix(code): resolve `/threads` header link on mount, not after load (#4453)\n\nFixed the `/threads` switcher so the current thread's LangSmith link\nappears immediately instead of only after all threads finish loading.\n\n---\n\nThe `/threads` switcher renders the current thread ID as a clickable\nLangSmith hyperlink in its header, but when the picker opened with no\ncached rows the URL was only resolved after the full DB thread load\ncompleted — so the link appeared late. The URL depends solely on\n`current_thread` (known at construction), so this resolves it as soon as\nthe modal mounts, regardless of the thread list load.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Open `/threads` with no cached rows and confirm the header\nthread-ID hyperlink is clickable before the list finishes loading.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/93bf5c64-5965-c233-d4ad-68cf58a33229)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"aedf4ef885ea05d92284833f1be513bcfb56bb28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/aedf4ef885ea05d92284833f1be513bcfb56bb28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4cba72893fc4aae5b429d8c573c1a513d97ddf8a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRxbiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcnQQAF4viAVc+b6/W4SJvSXBwPx/\nxpkA4T4pcGTNE6QlCAKR6Imx47eOaCumhGK4ZeUVWeX6IY+BcMr8W3UhR/23Ebgb\nNcJ4fEgB+9/QDy9S10Xx99QQhnYZqNsnw16PywA+yBzQs7cOG0bub0Hs9n4LUYUZ\naL+SleT7IvTWUCRNgrwZxFmWLWeaw72618ibpiR1xCUx0lQzSLgcTqAcqw6+pqno\nrWouU5vTS1hnnePP+xh9q3/5O8Q2bzYqL4TYIIf73SMoOfaEAuxOKA3K7AstBvVl\n1tmxgQEshZxqHXmgZtVwlbC0ixbxsYyuOPgO7C68e+ehP0YO+2PgAKr8Dkdy6Ll6\nTDGX46URYgSqJzLWkZMLUIN4QWAi2Pwk+MetevPK1XroISg2QYd4W/ws4v2LOE6L\nDwzks8redKXoAupNCjgfTjK7ltva2JQNR3oU88F0bEbhaFZ3LwDxru5+ZMK6vEFg\nLyOcwYA05dRJx7Wa+gGNOQEShHQFWCILWkSRGVTt5Kp6xwwbVuim0EMQeCpHzluh\nyei3cBsrEYGfVWT8LyL+9YGp6rxrZUe9eUmMHKIgr9dzwHH00ZxBBiQ0U1m+jqAd\nPcn93j3NW6lpecubGHumIPgyZbdl2muc11XyQo5ogs3xO/5cqsKCsmVhSYuYvKM7\nD26NTnbT6OcDMrKdULu8\n=pe8H\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aedf4ef885ea05d92284833f1be513bcfb56bb28\nparent de2f7d2835485df905772e1c96e33d2c239d8e22\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783043810 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783043810 -0400\n\nfix(code): resolve `/threads` header link on mount, not after load (#4453)\n\nFixed the `/threads` switcher so the current thread's LangSmith link\nappears immediately instead of only after all threads finish loading.\n\n---\n\nThe `/threads` switcher renders the current thread ID as a clickable\nLangSmith hyperlink in its header, but when the picker opened with no\ncached rows the URL was only resolved after the full DB thread load\ncompleted — so the link appeared late. The URL depends solely on\n`current_thread` (known at construction), so this resolves it as soon as\nthe modal mounts, regardless of the thread list load.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Open `/threads` with no cached rows and confirm the header\nthread-ID hyperlink is clickable before the list finishes loading.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/93bf5c64-5965-c233-d4ad-68cf58a33229)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-03T01:56:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4cba72893fc4aae5b429d8c573c1a513d97ddf8a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4cba72893fc4aae5b429d8c573c1a513d97ddf8a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4cba72893fc4aae5b429d8c573c1a513d97ddf8a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"de2f7d2835485df905772e1c96e33d2c239d8e22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/de2f7d2835485df905772e1c96e33d2c239d8e22","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/de2f7d2835485df905772e1c96e33d2c239d8e22"}]},{"sha":"de2f7d2835485df905772e1c96e33d2c239d8e22","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRlMmY3ZDI4MzU0ODVkZjkwNTc3MmUxYzk2ZTMzZDJjMjM5ZDhlMjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-03T01:13:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-03T01:13:53Z"},"message":"fix(code): ensure unique message widget IDs on history load (#4454)\n\nFix intermittent \"Could not load history\" errors caused by duplicate\nmessage widget IDs when resuming or switching threads.\n\n---\n\nResume/thread-switch loads were intermittently failing with `Could not\nload history: Tried to insert a widget with ID 'msg-XXXX', but a widget\nalready exists...`. Message IDs were only 32 bits (`uuid4().hex[:8]`),\nso IDs could collide, and `_load_thread_history` had no defense against\nmounting a widget whose ID was already in the DOM (e.g. a re-entrant\nload over surviving widgets). This widens auto-generated\nmessage/assistant IDs to the full 128-bit uuid4 hex and makes the\nhistory mount skip any widget whose ID is already present, logging a\nwarning instead of aborting the load.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e6466f87-1dba-5949-34eb-29774cd3eaa6)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e42f92f462918cd46ed7e5c735c5667cbad2fc2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e42f92f462918cd46ed7e5c735c5667cbad2fc2b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/de2f7d2835485df905772e1c96e33d2c239d8e22","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRwzRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEA0QAHM9khhkUkIzZfycIuKGRpIV\n9OIOrcjwoO8MFX+3Qqi1nDag7jahD1yiW+Ii8RQkR0IcfB2/pwllJNi6pJuLBu6W\na8j7ffV0DmWLdmKAvkmi010DNiYVkvqx1TRg7PUNpP7SGGly2OUz29M7zBUdNDFk\ng32O2WlBU99JxKM0tYOoKRyYvsHE5kAM0bS96aGrjCd+QB6+j/+cIywhVHUJUJL4\n5lj2cmOZ9PYLFJ/UM+P4aTrrZnhstw9MpTHgn20KQDKvNxn+TTV7ZpTJbzQfSqDV\nzghYlogNKiGPZFRZnZ6/QRhI8Ld3ttow/rjxbdHHZbqw0kfS+L9FKT7bhSH+99AQ\nzEH9SgX77qG/6SqR0tHnaDiUwMbC1wF/16wbVPJDfFYaS7BDouHGEFeUEGfmfmNg\nOn/QMC1Y0J0v4MtrP/ORtjZcZ1MzcONckQn9ziTpY9ynR91BYq8SnRzGvFo4k3F6\nqVCE8Zq9vNngUWWHTTNySQI1RhyCK94/Wx7YpcEZvAWY9ki056D4aVFqc+9A67Gq\nlDQcSeclQcN8XYqtp5QmfxKqpEfzZSsZLf0A6qk8lG4SAEkaqldfPaE3Fhw60Mud\n2rBtZ89uPhHyTyoCwCq78nZdK7b3ID8ZBUtZoKPoE6fwvv8YdiqrrYqhwztL2fuM\nIj5kivjmsAcWJZLXtcQK\n=a1GI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e42f92f462918cd46ed7e5c735c5667cbad2fc2b\nparent 9293b190170a872b73d0d94e66479bcc5f7962c7\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783041233 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783041233 -0400\n\nfix(code): ensure unique message widget IDs on history load (#4454)\n\nFix intermittent \"Could not load history\" errors caused by duplicate\nmessage widget IDs when resuming or switching threads.\n\n---\n\nResume/thread-switch loads were intermittently failing with `Could not\nload history: Tried to insert a widget with ID 'msg-XXXX', but a widget\nalready exists...`. Message IDs were only 32 bits (`uuid4().hex[:8]`),\nso IDs could collide, and `_load_thread_history` had no defense against\nmounting a widget whose ID was already in the DOM (e.g. a re-entrant\nload over surviving widgets). This widens auto-generated\nmessage/assistant IDs to the full 128-bit uuid4 hex and makes the\nhistory mount skip any widget whose ID is already present, logging a\nwarning instead of aborting the load.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e6466f87-1dba-5949-34eb-29774cd3eaa6)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-03T01:13:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/de2f7d2835485df905772e1c96e33d2c239d8e22","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/de2f7d2835485df905772e1c96e33d2c239d8e22","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/de2f7d2835485df905772e1c96e33d2c239d8e22/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9293b190170a872b73d0d94e66479bcc5f7962c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9293b190170a872b73d0d94e66479bcc5f7962c7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9293b190170a872b73d0d94e66479bcc5f7962c7"}]},{"sha":"9293b190170a872b73d0d94e66479bcc5f7962c7","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDkyOTNiMTkwMTcwYTg3MmI3M2QwZDk0ZTY2NDc5YmNjNWY3OTYyYzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-03T01:13:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-03T01:13:07Z"},"message":"fix(code): restore caller's LangSmith API key in shell subprocess env (#4458)\n\nRelated: #4436\n\nFixed a credential leak where shell subprocesses spawned by Deep Agents\nCode inherited the agent's internal LangSmith API key override instead\nof the caller's original key. Subprocess environments now restore the\ncaller's `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` (and LangChain alias) to the value they had\nbefore bootstrap, or remove the key entirely if the caller never set\none.\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\nWhen a user launches Deep Agents Code with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_API_KEY` set, bootstrap bridges that prefixed\nvalue onto the canonical `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` so the LangSmith SDK picks\nit up for the agent's own tracing. This overwrites the caller's original\nkey in-process — fine for the agent itself, but the original value was\nnever saved. As a result, shell commands run by the agent (via\n`execute`) inherited the override key, and the caller's own credential\nwas irrecoverable in that subprocess environment.\n\nThis is the same data-loss footgun that `restore_user_tracing_env`\nalready guards for tracing *flags*. The fix applies the same\nsave/restore pattern to tracing API *keys*: snapshot the caller's keys\nduring `_ensure_bootstrap`, then restore them (or drop the propagated\nvalue if the caller had none) when preparing the shell subprocess\nenvironment in `create_cli_agent`.","tree":{"sha":"b5b2fe5afee0689374c4339efa19eb595a2eb915","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b5b2fe5afee0689374c4339efa19eb595a2eb915"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9293b190170a872b73d0d94e66479bcc5f7962c7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRwyjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATKkQABmxq6Zb3VJbS4i4mem3uwQa\n5qtiMtfblDEQ2pfI+/ZYwAER5f5ny3bw14CHfnk7D5tLutVaGEFv+Lgq96C/urgN\nsvcH79B+cXXfOq0n6jaT+/4FzS+9pa6PmtQc3JBnME47hb/lDQH9JgQgu/9ZPhtt\n95Mrx7OJmPElN+W8V5tmMg5B+dDuY3k9yb04FeEdmQbCw3rcvUovnGQpbirYX/GJ\n0IDjwMe3qP/CwiZ4kDmOJoTTGO7wUFu7PubknORHWPxn4oH39f+Y9jY/ljU1MVE4\nnGEyyCeooCkOcIRPkyEnTFdbHNPMoxyVi/blXAslWaHAEgTgrz8ZSEZ1OU9wwEjt\nwTdoLV87t2MNcOwdci3sNH6bfToO5N5gGc8/Jn2dEEcYup26svsx27/h1op8h31M\nG0n0bQ/6qWJQl76IfYc16q5fBH+6DnRhqgvN97bGg24r6CkR/4pcoYvDvV6qyehu\nC83ZcbKuX2v13M4HpipwEhG1LV87XEUTYJi7rlBwHKFR8MKkFkGfqzZc8U4JoaBe\n61Xz4D81oCnjblnKNCz3iThm/xEJgF7OwJO/eFbSYhM/wNrPqfDeFUPK6Rs7czk1\nyUv5QGf8zdGgRng0XDi/aXSEss46croIh/2ofPseSKXMU1gpbBVJ0VzVSnZl1slP\n9v1Td/clrl+J2PMwmNsA\n=Tzxr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b5b2fe5afee0689374c4339efa19eb595a2eb915\nparent 4cb47491b024991322b7c24062c58cbcdc26a727\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783041187 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783041187 -0400\n\nfix(code): restore caller's LangSmith API key in shell subprocess env (#4458)\n\nRelated: #4436\n\nFixed a credential leak where shell subprocesses spawned by Deep Agents\nCode inherited the agent's internal LangSmith API key override instead\nof the caller's original key. Subprocess environments now restore the\ncaller's `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` (and LangChain alias) to the value they had\nbefore bootstrap, or remove the key entirely if the caller never set\none.\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\nWhen a user launches Deep Agents Code with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_API_KEY` set, bootstrap bridges that prefixed\nvalue onto the canonical `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` so the LangSmith SDK picks\nit up for the agent's own tracing. This overwrites the caller's original\nkey in-process — fine for the agent itself, but the original value was\nnever saved. As a result, shell commands run by the agent (via\n`execute`) inherited the override key, and the caller's own credential\nwas irrecoverable in that subprocess environment.\n\nThis is the same data-loss footgun that `restore_user_tracing_env`\nalready guards for tracing *flags*. The fix applies the same\nsave/restore pattern to tracing API *keys*: snapshot the caller's keys\nduring `_ensure_bootstrap`, then restore them (or drop the propagated\nvalue if the caller had none) when preparing the shell subprocess\nenvironment in `create_cli_agent`.","verified_at":"2026-07-03T01:13:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9293b190170a872b73d0d94e66479bcc5f7962c7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9293b190170a872b73d0d94e66479bcc5f7962c7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9293b190170a872b73d0d94e66479bcc5f7962c7/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4cb47491b024991322b7c24062c58cbcdc26a727","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4cb47491b024991322b7c24062c58cbcdc26a727","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4cb47491b024991322b7c24062c58cbcdc26a727"}]},{"sha":"4cb47491b024991322b7c24062c58cbcdc26a727","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRjYjQ3NDkxYjAyNDk5MTMyMmI3YzI0MDYyYzU4Y2JjZGMyNmE3Mjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"nv-kasikritc","email":"kchantharuan@nvidia.com","date":"2026-07-02T23:47:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-02T23:47:51Z"},"message":"feat(sdk): add NVIDIA NIM app-origin attribution (#4455)\n\nFixes #4456\n\nDeep Agents now identifies requests made through the NVIDIA provider\nwith NVIDIA NIM's app-origin billing header.\n\n---\n\nAdds a built-in NVIDIA provider profile that sends\n`X-BILLING-INVOKE-ORIGIN: DeepAgents` through\n`ChatNVIDIA.default_headers`, while preserving explicit caller\noverrides.","tree":{"sha":"505a90e24d67a9dd5857b9ca7f1cd45b4c51e801","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/505a90e24d67a9dd5857b9ca7f1cd45b4c51e801"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4cb47491b024991322b7c24062c58cbcdc26a727","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRvinCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANXkQAHehN2rXBPCAedME+0wHnDka\nW7eGgbH4WrGXz5Gye+MLAX4Gn1BdViy4pGHpEHZB+1iekYtpZfVGmmrfZ0i/ybSH\nj2CduaAk5I26F4nUofCBniN13ij01xmLdJC5HfzcOWsBjXAayYFOC/3hPCgsLPKR\n5xkF0JDWxwcfGe8itZJhCm6PRxNEJTAmvLyfhYRES4b69KkN2MoP1A4n2voWWa7D\nCGaX/VX8u72IysqrxyLueOMZqMn9M/GERFTfijJHuL5rxpBtv8bCQeYNUcLasiHU\nFMSLqFsyflQaNXFVbyQhkAkCdYguvy5ggCOXfXVJPgTsz8vvWHS9YiF2HPVhQoyC\nOnAzlxqyzeEe5C7hD6lrNQhG+F1GQ6x40t6P+1RXBBpREQKGh4YSlw86jLOev5N2\n1PUZXo6s5YPTP6M4LLUCL2iQTmTIoahpgGPStTDwkQcqSH2nDMRLIpeEfRRgkMRT\nQ17++pB8lq64W/gpBUfhvGB5za4M2K6oWINGHoUQTl/UFsMdkMmfOmqUpWcRYzjb\n2GmCWRBGLI9Fbg0fAsDixZTjty7Hc6RkOfNu0YavXOfbBIHUOV9ZqYd6N1hgMmvy\nuHJgezBTfrUgjojq81HDSAs8bY/nb6jWsSllQ7Zh3Zs6e/R4kMBBIhEBx63cWiSn\nhFgAwYeeCG/Yy+jmIBqR\n=PoTp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 505a90e24d67a9dd5857b9ca7f1cd45b4c51e801\nparent ddcae5e0bd9aebc946be1d9fb3f5e35eeb690fa6\nauthor nv-kasikritc <kchantharuan@nvidia.com> 1783036071 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783036071 -0400\n\nfeat(sdk): add NVIDIA NIM app-origin attribution (#4455)\n\nFixes #4456\n\nDeep Agents now identifies requests made through the NVIDIA provider\nwith NVIDIA NIM's app-origin billing header.\n\n---\n\nAdds a built-in NVIDIA provider profile that sends\n`X-BILLING-INVOKE-ORIGIN: DeepAgents` through\n`ChatNVIDIA.default_headers`, while preserving explicit caller\noverrides.","verified_at":"2026-07-02T23:47:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4cb47491b024991322b7c24062c58cbcdc26a727","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4cb47491b024991322b7c24062c58cbcdc26a727","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4cb47491b024991322b7c24062c58cbcdc26a727/comments","author":{"login":"nv-kasikritc","id":169213847,"node_id":"U_kgDOChX_lw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169213847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nv-kasikritc","html_url":"https://github.com/nv-kasikritc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nv-kasikritc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nv-kasikritc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nv-kasikritc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nv-kasikritc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nv-kasikritc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nv-kasikritc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nv-kasikritc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nv-kasikritc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nv-kasikritc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ddcae5e0bd9aebc946be1d9fb3f5e35eeb690fa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ddcae5e0bd9aebc946be1d9fb3f5e35eeb690fa6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ddcae5e0bd9aebc946be1d9fb3f5e35eeb690fa6"}]},{"sha":"ddcae5e0bd9aebc946be1d9fb3f5e35eeb690fa6","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRkY2FlNWUwYmQ5YWViYzk0NmJlMWQ5ZmIzZjVlMzVlZWI2OTBmYTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-02T23:42:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-02T23:42:29Z"},"message":"fix(code): allow suppressing LangSmith key override warning (#4436)\n\nReword the LangSmith env var override warning and add\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SUPPRESS_ENV_OVERRIDE_WARNING` to silence it.\n\n---\n\nWhen both `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` and `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_API_KEY`\nare set to different values, bootstrap logs a warning. The old wording\nimplied the two variables can't coexist. This rewords it to explain the\noverride is expected (the prefixed value wins inside the Deep Agents\nCode process; the canonical shell var is left untouched for other tools)\nand adds an opt-in `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SUPPRESS_ENV_OVERRIDE_WARNING` flag\nto silence it — so users who intentionally keep `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` set\nfor other SDKs no longer need the `unset` alias workaround.\n\n### Why the warning exists (the footgun it guards against)\nThe precedence is silent: when both are set, the\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_`-prefixed value always wins and overwrites the\ncanonical one inside the process, with no other signal. The risk is that\na user thinks their traces are going to one place when they're actually\ngoing to another.\n\nUser story: months ago I exported `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_API_KEY`\n(pointing at my personal scratch workspace) while testing dcode, and\nit's still in my shell profile. Today I set `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` to my\nteam's shared workspace key, expecting dcode's traces to show up there\nfor a debugging session with a teammate. Without any warning, the stale\nprefixed key silently overrides it — my traces land in my personal\nworkspace, my teammate sees nothing, and I burn time wondering why.\nSending traces (which can contain prompts/tool output) to an unexpected\nLangSmith account is exactly the kind of quiet mistake that's hard to\nnotice and hard to debug.\n\nThe warning surfaces that mismatch so the override is a deliberate\nchoice rather than a silent surprise. The tradeoff is that it also nags\nusers who set both on purpose — which is why this PR both softens the\nwording and adds an explicit opt-out.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/5cb0013b-5a70-8f23-b828-aff0fd26c720)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f216b6112f8715d7c61816f65de355a36654f886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f216b6112f8715d7c61816f65de355a36654f886"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ddcae5e0bd9aebc946be1d9fb3f5e35eeb690fa6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRvdlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5m4QAEbp5IqDjA+W2ApBGIFDIJAX\nocNRFMZgZ2/D29BvLrNeD9keiUAY3VvYK/E7oWgcvp/WfnVlHXA1toa1Z/NDt7Pj\nwxkWfje5MtyC7NqjhOp6jsC+8D9U5Rz+boQebncgXQufM/TkijKFyJ5DMcaMfTSk\nC91PCewLTNLlw7pLGrxOLdxzLJRuPnySbKRMKbeegRA7H8WTEXsFe2OoZFOJE+y+\nUQBfBPvkemy8LlhQtUwXW6afCdsWw9ZzmdsqDZJNC5US6ob9c41H+LFE2XYkdLPV\netuxRNohxoHYArHJN0/KChq76wNuFhwbUivYEC/RKlPmywwT2RDW3q7pbcpLghgH\nQSfw4tmdDMF1tXCajNH8CwaEAYRG7oDmuh1NjCXs855L1u7OxX8JahcaXNCYTLbV\n4i9hgVnK8TLktE5zhAXZKS4Hi9ESPTNftTkS9E0jlj/Lr4c61n3yd4yJhdJDi95c\nuJgTJpSN9g+keOtBd5kZuTEodFxWpBUgtsqo2BceMxSZ/HcBNeRz3d3EQbZC5d8l\nfAzz04iiQGelbZq4bQjbxRMF0WSyPGbJyN0Ea28K/xu2HZF0WMNoQVxF8H7KDH8P\n9yzIWcBNxLWG0kz/niA88RFqAAewSeMEiNTRG/iyJXQS325yoQig7r5b99avQ3o3\nZLWaLORcZcY6U0TehJxo\n=9Pgt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f216b6112f8715d7c61816f65de355a36654f886\nparent b1dbf5e66ac81a9fd95abf6987ba058bb14a5edf\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783035749 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783035749 -0400\n\nfix(code): allow suppressing LangSmith key override warning (#4436)\n\nReword the LangSmith env var override warning and add\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SUPPRESS_ENV_OVERRIDE_WARNING` to silence it.\n\n---\n\nWhen both `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` and `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_API_KEY`\nare set to different values, bootstrap logs a warning. The old wording\nimplied the two variables can't coexist. This rewords it to explain the\noverride is expected (the prefixed value wins inside the Deep Agents\nCode process; the canonical shell var is left untouched for other tools)\nand adds an opt-in `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_SUPPRESS_ENV_OVERRIDE_WARNING` flag\nto silence it — so users who intentionally keep `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` set\nfor other SDKs no longer need the `unset` alias workaround.\n\n### Why the warning exists (the footgun it guards against)\nThe precedence is silent: when both are set, the\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_`-prefixed value always wins and overwrites the\ncanonical one inside the process, with no other signal. The risk is that\na user thinks their traces are going to one place when they're actually\ngoing to another.\n\nUser story: months ago I exported `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_API_KEY`\n(pointing at my personal scratch workspace) while testing dcode, and\nit's still in my shell profile. Today I set `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` to my\nteam's shared workspace key, expecting dcode's traces to show up there\nfor a debugging session with a teammate. Without any warning, the stale\nprefixed key silently overrides it — my traces land in my personal\nworkspace, my teammate sees nothing, and I burn time wondering why.\nSending traces (which can contain prompts/tool output) to an unexpected\nLangSmith account is exactly the kind of quiet mistake that's hard to\nnotice and hard to debug.\n\nThe warning surfaces that mismatch so the override is a deliberate\nchoice rather than a silent surprise. The tradeoff is that it also nags\nusers who set both on purpose — which is why this PR both softens the\nwording and adds an explicit opt-out.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/5cb0013b-5a70-8f23-b828-aff0fd26c720)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-02T23:42:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ddcae5e0bd9aebc946be1d9fb3f5e35eeb690fa6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ddcae5e0bd9aebc946be1d9fb3f5e35eeb690fa6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ddcae5e0bd9aebc946be1d9fb3f5e35eeb690fa6/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b1dbf5e66ac81a9fd95abf6987ba058bb14a5edf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b1dbf5e66ac81a9fd95abf6987ba058bb14a5edf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b1dbf5e66ac81a9fd95abf6987ba058bb14a5edf"}]},{"sha":"b1dbf5e66ac81a9fd95abf6987ba058bb14a5edf","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGIxZGJmNWU2NmFjODFhOWZkOTVhYmY2OTg3YmEwNThiYjE0YTVlZGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-02T23:04:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-02T23:04:42Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): improve grep literal guidance and sandbox glob routing (#4168)\n\n* `grep` now warns when a no-match pattern looks like a regex, since the\ntool only matches literal text.\n* The `grep` tool description and parameter docs now state up front that\nthe pattern is literal, with explicit do-nots and a pointer to `execute`\n+ `rg` for genuine regex.\n* Slash-containing globs (e.g. `src/**/*.py`) now work in sandbox\nbackends — previously they silently returned zero results because GNU\n`grep --include` only matches basenames.\n* The `grep` tool description is now reconciled at request time against\nthe backend's actual `execute` capability, so the `rg` fallback line\nappears only when `execute` is available.\n* Three new retrieval evals verify that a model recovers after a\nregex-style grep miss.\n* Default `grep` and `glob` timeouts are halved (grep 30s → 15s, glob\n10s → 5s backend / 20s → 10s middleware) so bad patterns and large trees\nfail faster.\n\n\n---\n\nThe `grep` tool matches *literal* text — `FilesystemBackend` shells out\nto ripgrep with `-F`, and the in-memory backends do a plain substring\ncheck. Models routinely reach for regex anyway (`|` alternation, `.*`,\nescapes like `\\.`), which is matched verbatim and silently returns \"No\nmatches found\" even when the content exists. This PR adds two\ncomplementary, non-breaking mitigations: a sharper tool description that\nsets expectations before the call, and a post-call hint that steers the\nmodel back to literal searches after a miss.\n\nIt also fixes a sandbox backend bug where slash-containing globs\nsilently returned nothing, makes the grep description self-adjust to the\nbackend's `execute` capability at request time, and halves the default\nwall-clock timeouts so that a pathological pattern or a huge tree fails\nfaster.\n\n### User-facing behavior changes\n\n* The `grep` tool description now leads with \"LITERAL text pattern\nacross files (NOT regex)\" and lists explicit do-nots: no `|`\nalternation, no `.*` wildcards, no `\\.` escapes. When the `execute` tool\nis active for the backend, it also points to `execute` with `rg` for\ngenuine regex needs; that line is dropped automatically when `execute`\nis unavailable, so the description never suggests a tool the model can't\ncall.\n+ Example: a model that previously called `grep(pattern=\"foo|bar\")` and\ngot \"No matches found\" should now read the tool description and run two\nseparate calls — `grep(pattern=\"foo\")` and `grep(pattern=\"bar\")` —\ninstead.\n* When `grep` returns no matches *and* the pattern carries strong regex\nsignals, the tool response now appends a one-line hint:\n  ```\nNote: grep matches literal text, not regex, so characters like `|`,\n`.*`, and `\\.` are searched verbatim. Search for the literal text you\nneed instead; for `|` alternation, run a separate search per\nalternative.\n  ```\nThe hint stays backend-agnostic (it never names the `execute` tool,\nwhich is not present in every configuration) and only appears on a\ngenuine no-match result. If the pattern happens to match literally (e.g.\na file contains `a = b|c`), or if matches existed but were all removed\nby read permissions, no hint is shown.\n* The `glob` parameter description on `GrepSchema` now clarifies that it\nis an in-tool file filter (not a call to the separate `glob` tool),\nspells out the matching semantics (a pattern without `/` matches the\nfile name at any depth; a pattern containing `/` matches the\nsearch-root-relative path, e.g. `src/**/*.py`), and notes that brace\nexpansion (e.g. `*.{ts,tsx}`) is not supported on all backends — the\nwcmatch-backed backends expand braces, but the Context Hub backend\ntreats them literally, so running a separate search per extension is the\nreliable choice.\n* The `output_mode` parameter description now spells out the exact\noutput shape for each mode instead of a terse one-liner:\n`files_with_matches` returns newline-separated paths, `content` returns\nmatching lines grouped by file under a `<path>:` header with indented\n`<line_number>: <line text>` lines (no surrounding context), and `count`\nreturns one `<path>: <match_count>` line per file.\n* Sandbox backends (`BaseSandbox`) now route slash-containing globs\nthrough an in-process Python glob instead of GNU `grep --include`.\nPreviously, a pattern like `src/**/*.py` was passed to `grep\n--include=src/**/*.py`, which only matches basenames and silently\nreturned zero results. The new `_GREP_PATH_GLOB_TEMPLATE` resolves the\nglob relative to the search root, reads matching files directly, and\nemits the same `path\\0line_num:text` record structure that\n`_parse_grep_output` already consumes, so the rest of the pipeline is\nunchanged. Basename-only globs (no `/`) continue through GNU `grep` for\nspeed.\n* The `grep` tool description is now a *placeholder* that is reconciled\nat request time. `_create_grep_tool` provisions the description assuming\n`execute` is available (so the `rg` fallback line is present).\n`_filter_unsupported_tools_and_apply_prompt` then checks whether\n`execute` is actually active for the backend and swaps in the\nwithout-`execute` variant via `_with_filtered_grep_description` when it\nisn't. The static description on `self.tools` is only provisional until\na request runs. The unsupported-tools logic was extracted into\n`_unsupported_tools_and_execution_state` and `_tool_name` helpers to\nsupport this.\n* Default filesystem tool timeouts are halved:\n  - `grep` sync phase: 30s → 15s\n- `grep` async wrapper: 65s → 35s (wraps two sync phases plus headroom)\n  - `glob` backend walk: 10s → 5s\n  - `glob` middleware deadline: 20s → 10s\n\nThe layering invariants are preserved: the backend glob budget stays\nbelow the middleware deadline (5s < 10s), and the async grep timeout\nstays above two sync phases (35s > 30s). `read_file` has no timeout\n(single direct read, no search or tree walk) and is unchanged.\n\n<details>\n<summary>How regex detection works</summary>\n\nDetection is deliberately conservative so common literal code searches\ndon't trigger false hints. The heuristic flags:\n\n- `|` — alternation, the most common regex reflex\n- `.*` or `.+` — wildcard quantifiers\n- Escaped metacharacters or character classes: `\\.` , `\\w`, `\\d`, `\\s`,\n`\\b`, etc.\n\nBare `.`, `(`, `)`, `[`, `]`, `?`, `^`, `$` are intentionally *not*\nflagged because they appear routinely in literal code searches:\n\n```\ndef __init__(self):    # ( ) : are literal\nself.tools              # . is literal\narr[0]                  # [ ] are literal\n```\n\n</details>\n\n### Motivation\n\nA silent \"No matches found\" for a regex-style pattern is a common\nfailure mode: the content exists, the model just asked for it the wrong\nway and gets no signal that the tool doesn't speak regex. The tool\ndescription fix addresses the problem before the call by making the\nliteral-only contract unmistakable. The hint addresses it after the call\nby catching the model when it still reaches for regex, steering it\ntoward separate literal searches instead of burning calls on regex\nvariants. (The `rg` escape hatch lives in the always-visible tool\ndescription rather than the hint, so the hint stays useful even on\nbackends without an `execute` tool.)\n\nThe sandbox glob fix addresses a quieter but equally confusible failure:\na model that passes `glob=\"src/**/*.py\"` to `grep` on a sandbox backend\ngot an empty result with no indication that the pattern was the problem\n— the files existed and the pattern was valid, but GNU `grep --include`\nonly matches basenames. The in-process glob route makes slash-containing\npatterns work as documented.\n\nThe dynamic description swap ensures the `rg` fallback line never\nappears for a backend that can't serve `execute`, preventing the model\nfrom being directed to a tool it can't call.\n\nThe timeout reduction addresses latency: the original values (30s grep,\n20s glob) were chosen independently based on each operation's cost\nprofile. Halving them lets the model receive a \"narrow your search\"\nsignal sooner, reducing wasted wall-clock time on pathological patterns\nor huge directory trees.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c857a6fe1b41862b361439e9cd22abfd46eb116","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9c857a6fe1b41862b361439e9cd22abfd46eb116"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b1dbf5e66ac81a9fd95abf6987ba058bb14a5edf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRu6KCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu8wQAFB4oc03cUiyEmD/06NH/ND9\n88Zv9/KKtk142BFni4PTyC+sJgm1ZQTu9J2sOzx5v/kDN8Xb+3wLjvJMRLd4ju5N\nI2p1oEr7exyBwG7oo43xlD2YNzxQMw6HKqStJCWKDjG/kKeoZaH2ISVKUkzPbFYd\ns8jC5sC0SHt/L5jYA/F0ZLk8uxrpi29SsCMUYqqgvrXQfk+Dr0/pNi4KJfteFzZs\nOQLU5IFqKGa9FyEjI3NAdcmkRKozy+/VzpuA05nPzalLjfBIXlcdyquxoiwfBUL+\nWSnuD20OCQGdqT1oxAamXxMs2GsjxA3qdog9kst9uS7YTxzuo3BVEE0WtEIrRbar\n1j10Dg7SwKJoncVGGdWN/0mz5V/iaULFseIbSLuDKvKokMFnw0eW4cZz3jisgH4V\nnoUjx1cKUU2qBmtUxt4qca/BAjDADtCTPs/mDLjTOxL0VnavuVo8B48kefdl+ntG\nQizMkAyvmDSf9wr3pSWIpV1ois1FEv4yWq09sPj2UQUhc6YNbD3bsYpSSLkwQh3g\n2IeJirT+juIEUwy40/26O0/Zwdj+9Z8g6kNn1OGipf3BXuRR4A4O+XZW/bHNo3pR\ntygPtQ6UrligK90GlCrZrl+mffKHfQwACZAg4+OhyJwTWf35S3Nh9ibx7E6/+BfI\nA3MrW1GfXdPXxdCJKtWh\n=MNvn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9c857a6fe1b41862b361439e9cd22abfd46eb116\nparent 20107eda2dafbcc427fb0d61c7944f881e95df4d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1783033482 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783033482 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): improve grep literal guidance and sandbox glob routing (#4168)\n\n* `grep` now warns when a no-match pattern looks like a regex, since the\ntool only matches literal text.\n* The `grep` tool description and parameter docs now state up front that\nthe pattern is literal, with explicit do-nots and a pointer to `execute`\n+ `rg` for genuine regex.\n* Slash-containing globs (e.g. `src/**/*.py`) now work in sandbox\nbackends — previously they silently returned zero results because GNU\n`grep --include` only matches basenames.\n* The `grep` tool description is now reconciled at request time against\nthe backend's actual `execute` capability, so the `rg` fallback line\nappears only when `execute` is available.\n* Three new retrieval evals verify that a model recovers after a\nregex-style grep miss.\n* Default `grep` and `glob` timeouts are halved (grep 30s → 15s, glob\n10s → 5s backend / 20s → 10s middleware) so bad patterns and large trees\nfail faster.\n\n\n---\n\nThe `grep` tool matches *literal* text — `FilesystemBackend` shells out\nto ripgrep with `-F`, and the in-memory backends do a plain substring\ncheck. Models routinely reach for regex anyway (`|` alternation, `.*`,\nescapes like `\\.`), which is matched verbatim and silently returns \"No\nmatches found\" even when the content exists. This PR adds two\ncomplementary, non-breaking mitigations: a sharper tool description that\nsets expectations before the call, and a post-call hint that steers the\nmodel back to literal searches after a miss.\n\nIt also fixes a sandbox backend bug where slash-containing globs\nsilently returned nothing, makes the grep description self-adjust to the\nbackend's `execute` capability at request time, and halves the default\nwall-clock timeouts so that a pathological pattern or a huge tree fails\nfaster.\n\n### User-facing behavior changes\n\n* The `grep` tool description now leads with \"LITERAL text pattern\nacross files (NOT regex)\" and lists explicit do-nots: no `|`\nalternation, no `.*` wildcards, no `\\.` escapes. When the `execute` tool\nis active for the backend, it also points to `execute` with `rg` for\ngenuine regex needs; that line is dropped automatically when `execute`\nis unavailable, so the description never suggests a tool the model can't\ncall.\n+ Example: a model that previously called `grep(pattern=\"foo|bar\")` and\ngot \"No matches found\" should now read the tool description and run two\nseparate calls — `grep(pattern=\"foo\")` and `grep(pattern=\"bar\")` —\ninstead.\n* When `grep` returns no matches *and* the pattern carries strong regex\nsignals, the tool response now appends a one-line hint:\n  ```\nNote: grep matches literal text, not regex, so characters like `|`,\n`.*`, and `\\.` are searched verbatim. Search for the literal text you\nneed instead; for `|` alternation, run a separate search per\nalternative.\n  ```\nThe hint stays backend-agnostic (it never names the `execute` tool,\nwhich is not present in every configuration) and only appears on a\ngenuine no-match result. If the pattern happens to match literally (e.g.\na file contains `a = b|c`), or if matches existed but were all removed\nby read permissions, no hint is shown.\n* The `glob` parameter description on `GrepSchema` now clarifies that it\nis an in-tool file filter (not a call to the separate `glob` tool),\nspells out the matching semantics (a pattern without `/` matches the\nfile name at any depth; a pattern containing `/` matches the\nsearch-root-relative path, e.g. `src/**/*.py`), and notes that brace\nexpansion (e.g. `*.{ts,tsx}`) is not supported on all backends — the\nwcmatch-backed backends expand braces, but the Context Hub backend\ntreats them literally, so running a separate search per extension is the\nreliable choice.\n* The `output_mode` parameter description now spells out the exact\noutput shape for each mode instead of a terse one-liner:\n`files_with_matches` returns newline-separated paths, `content` returns\nmatching lines grouped by file under a `<path>:` header with indented\n`<line_number>: <line text>` lines (no surrounding context), and `count`\nreturns one `<path>: <match_count>` line per file.\n* Sandbox backends (`BaseSandbox`) now route slash-containing globs\nthrough an in-process Python glob instead of GNU `grep --include`.\nPreviously, a pattern like `src/**/*.py` was passed to `grep\n--include=src/**/*.py`, which only matches basenames and silently\nreturned zero results. The new `_GREP_PATH_GLOB_TEMPLATE` resolves the\nglob relative to the search root, reads matching files directly, and\nemits the same `path\\0line_num:text` record structure that\n`_parse_grep_output` already consumes, so the rest of the pipeline is\nunchanged. Basename-only globs (no `/`) continue through GNU `grep` for\nspeed.\n* The `grep` tool description is now a *placeholder* that is reconciled\nat request time. `_create_grep_tool` provisions the description assuming\n`execute` is available (so the `rg` fallback line is present).\n`_filter_unsupported_tools_and_apply_prompt` then checks whether\n`execute` is actually active for the backend and swaps in the\nwithout-`execute` variant via `_with_filtered_grep_description` when it\nisn't. The static description on `self.tools` is only provisional until\na request runs. The unsupported-tools logic was extracted into\n`_unsupported_tools_and_execution_state` and `_tool_name` helpers to\nsupport this.\n* Default filesystem tool timeouts are halved:\n  - `grep` sync phase: 30s → 15s\n- `grep` async wrapper: 65s → 35s (wraps two sync phases plus headroom)\n  - `glob` backend walk: 10s → 5s\n  - `glob` middleware deadline: 20s → 10s\n\nThe layering invariants are preserved: the backend glob budget stays\nbelow the middleware deadline (5s < 10s), and the async grep timeout\nstays above two sync phases (35s > 30s). `read_file` has no timeout\n(single direct read, no search or tree walk) and is unchanged.\n\n<details>\n<summary>How regex detection works</summary>\n\nDetection is deliberately conservative so common literal code searches\ndon't trigger false hints. The heuristic flags:\n\n- `|` — alternation, the most common regex reflex\n- `.*` or `.+` — wildcard quantifiers\n- Escaped metacharacters or character classes: `\\.` , `\\w`, `\\d`, `\\s`,\n`\\b`, etc.\n\nBare `.`, `(`, `)`, `[`, `]`, `?`, `^`, `$` are intentionally *not*\nflagged because they appear routinely in literal code searches:\n\n```\ndef __init__(self):    # ( ) : are literal\nself.tools              # . is literal\narr[0]                  # [ ] are literal\n```\n\n</details>\n\n### Motivation\n\nA silent \"No matches found\" for a regex-style pattern is a common\nfailure mode: the content exists, the model just asked for it the wrong\nway and gets no signal that the tool doesn't speak regex. The tool\ndescription fix addresses the problem before the call by making the\nliteral-only contract unmistakable. The hint addresses it after the call\nby catching the model when it still reaches for regex, steering it\ntoward separate literal searches instead of burning calls on regex\nvariants. (The `rg` escape hatch lives in the always-visible tool\ndescription rather than the hint, so the hint stays useful even on\nbackends without an `execute` tool.)\n\nThe sandbox glob fix addresses a quieter but equally confusible failure:\na model that passes `glob=\"src/**/*.py\"` to `grep` on a sandbox backend\ngot an empty result with no indication that the pattern was the problem\n— the files existed and the pattern was valid, but GNU `grep --include`\nonly matches basenames. The in-process glob route makes slash-containing\npatterns work as documented.\n\nThe dynamic description swap ensures the `rg` fallback line never\nappears for a backend that can't serve `execute`, preventing the model\nfrom being directed to a tool it can't call.\n\nThe timeout reduction addresses latency: the original values (30s grep,\n20s glob) were chosen independently based on each operation's cost\nprofile. Halving them lets the model receive a \"narrow your search\"\nsignal sooner, reducing wasted wall-clock time on pathological patterns\nor huge directory trees.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-02T23:04:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b1dbf5e66ac81a9fd95abf6987ba058bb14a5edf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b1dbf5e66ac81a9fd95abf6987ba058bb14a5edf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b1dbf5e66ac81a9fd95abf6987ba058bb14a5edf/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","st