wers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccurme/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"feab6e0b3762aa42fa458af16d0a3e8d04d8b075","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/feab6e0b3762aa42fa458af16d0a3e8d04d8b075","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/feab6e0b3762aa42fa458af16d0a3e8d04d8b075"}]},{"sha":"feab6e0b3762aa42fa458af16d0a3e8d04d8b075","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZlYWI2ZTBiMzc2MmFhNDJmYTQ1OGFmMTZkMGEzZThkMDRkOGIwNzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-02T06:59:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-02T06:59:21Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): unify `grep` include-glob semantics across backends (#3936)\n\nCloses #3922\n\n---\n\nThe same `grep(..., glob=...)` call returned different files depending\non the backend and whether ripgrep was installed. The in-memory\n`StateBackend`/`StoreBackend` path applied the glob to only the\nbasename, so directory patterns like `src/**/*.py` and even `**/*.py`\nsilently matched nothing. The `FilesystemBackend` Python fallback\napplied the glob to the root-relative path, so slashless patterns like\n`*.py` missed nested files. Since `StateBackend` is the default in\n`create_deep_agent` and the tool docs advertise recursive globs, agents\ncould wrongly conclude files do not exist.\n\nThis introduces a single shared matcher, `compile_grep_include_glob`,\nthat mirrors ripgrep's include-glob behavior: a pattern without a `/`\nmatches the basename at any depth (`*.py` matches `/src/app/main.py`),\nwhile a pattern containing a `/` matches the path relative to the grep\nsearch root with `**` support (`src/**/*.py` matches\n`/src/app/main.py`). It is used by both `grep_matches_from_files` and\nthe `FilesystemBackend` Python fallback; the ripgrep code path is\nunchanged. No public APIs, result schemas, or literal-search semantics\nchange.\n\nRegression tests cover the `src/**/*.py`, `**/*.py`, `*.py`, and `*.md`\nmatrix plus search-root relativity for both the in-memory and\n(ripgrep-stubbed) Python fallback paths.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7588fab31193b3fb8aa18de5f1b26d9bbffb5c78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7588fab31193b3fb8aa18de5f1b26d9bbffb5c78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/feab6e0b3762aa42fa458af16d0a3e8d04d8b075","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRgxJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/58QAC7LmlFqWgb8/tgvaortP/01\naB25GSGbIilt/weF+3kqwZ6PqF4bmxkDaEotIwRWnvbb8dwCw2OoYKuhVdJPldau\n+2tp5uNGw+8lQTppVSUb+zOv/7ufQPNErDPbBZ0ClOmCnmNNY+z2GxY8nA0Xggqx\nHZp8Yc+5T7bU62Z+Ebd/0Xkdo5t4gCSEUMIKJlUUvA5o6RyCbLlKc9ARBWeWsscp\nvOKXLMniooDOjHUDJgnpnVZiPBAog4baIDu3AOnBPjPXpbMm2IzKxcQeVYUJ/3DH\nWyBYudy3mPvRqrPZ/qePbiRn4RpJ1WioV++LAsAnxPZJ8zrgmSIIQGjwGVCaXdeP\nmpTjwJjAsIf3DcrZGXZkGtK835kKwEpvPM4EyV5KrpUq3U3hV90Vl99JerCvNDyV\nL0JGXIvxNofuoPAf6y5bidv5DfhGibxDkIdYlwrEKPIF1hp6EfrgMGB2sSAHEZKp\n0y5SJm7bFL1rxInXhJWH1B5ACC4lErf1FE8EVeko9XonlWwfJU9QnVpZKef+bKjK\nAiD7pTq3j5d5RYIGS9Lowjmsv9imHBqC1G7s1fG45DmgS5AEGoKWkvGqSMqsh7Jh\nm9pSUpD6jetDo0E+m+k3hu9W4YYQgmCRyq9ZKFGU4cod+JTqdLpSHGxOialsN22L\nDe3P76FU7lNE9s+Jk3X1\n=wJWC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7588fab31193b3fb8aa18de5f1b26d9bbffb5c78\nparent b0d92c0f38ca0aa037b56e26b2b0d322cdd07856\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782975561 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782975561 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): unify `grep` include-glob semantics across backends (#3936)\n\nCloses #3922\n\n---\n\nThe same `grep(..., glob=...)` call returned different files depending\non the backend and whether ripgrep was installed. The in-memory\n`StateBackend`/`StoreBackend` path applied the glob to only the\nbasename, so directory patterns like `src/**/*.py` and even `**/*.py`\nsilently matched nothing. The `FilesystemBackend` Python fallback\napplied the glob to the root-relative path, so slashless patterns like\n`*.py` missed nested files. Since `StateBackend` is the default in\n`create_deep_agent` and the tool docs advertise recursive globs, agents\ncould wrongly conclude files do not exist.\n\nThis introduces a single shared matcher, `compile_grep_include_glob`,\nthat mirrors ripgrep's include-glob behavior: a pattern without a `/`\nmatches the basename at any depth (`*.py` matches `/src/app/main.py`),\nwhile a pattern containing a `/` matches the path relative to the grep\nsearch root with `**` support (`src/**/*.py` matches\n`/src/app/main.py`). It is used by both `grep_matches_from_files` and\nthe `FilesystemBackend` Python fallback; the ripgrep code path is\nunchanged. No public APIs, result schemas, or literal-search semantics\nchange.\n\nRegression tests cover the `src/**/*.py`, `**/*.py`, `*.py`, and `*.md`\nmatrix plus search-root relativity for both the in-memory and\n(ripgrep-stubbed) Python fallback paths.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-02T06:59:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/feab6e0b3762aa42fa458af16d0a3e8d04d8b075","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/feab6e0b3762aa42fa458af16d0a3e8d04d8b075","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/feab6e0b3762aa42fa458af16d0a3e8d04d8b075/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b0d92c0f38ca0aa037b56e26b2b0d322cdd07856","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b0d92c0f38ca0aa037b56e26b2b0d322cdd07856","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b0d92c0f38ca0aa037b56e26b2b0d322cdd07856"}]},{"sha":"b0d92c0f38ca0aa037b56e26b2b0d322cdd07856","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGIwZDkyYzBmMzhjYTBhYTAzN2I1NmUyNmIyYjBkMzIyY2RkMDc4NTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Kavish Kartha","email":"33845687+kavishkartha05@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-07-02T06:44:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-02T06:44:53Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): move `get_sync()` inside try in `check_async_task` and `cancel_async_task` (#3967)\n\nFixes #3958 \n\n---\n\n`check_async_task` and `cancel_async_task` called `clients.get_sync()`\nbefore their `try/except` blocks, letting `ValueError` escape unhandled\nwhen an async subagent has no URL configured. Moved both calls inside\nthe existing `try/except`, matching the pattern already used in\n`start_async_task` and `update_async_task`.\n\n## Social handles (optional)\n<!-- If you'd like a shoutout on release, add your socials below -->\nTwitter: @kavishkartha31\nLinkedIn: https://linkedin.com/in/kavish-kartha\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"6bb836803674431f6b34538c7ebd24b067cdc874","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6bb836803674431f6b34538c7ebd24b067cdc874"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b0d92c0f38ca0aa037b56e26b2b0d322cdd07856","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRgjlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALdYQAIFl5x04zz1y0i4juK/1Tqqu\n8RRcIDhZfft6EcCrKJM7s9dqlc6Go1lys0Ksf1E18tAd1d7WaqPQSdbvmqBpuOQT\n+ar5BK6WUboB84k45J5DB7WY6Ej8bzsoLusv8vW9CqpD45q/5RsdIoB01E9RXNq9\nXFYAJFuFDUxgCZu7ONDZLic9LE8jl3sVr+1DjmlFl6Dgpe9ZpFMl5chgHkbfRWNq\nzJO0yah/6e3pU4wRFxpZQUL3hoQPEkIBA7IKgq8tZLrgH7JelZoKzBZql7TlNldG\n1wh8DMmYEYoBJOmmiDvH4anE5NJZRbnZaMnCt6SY015qxJdO02r3/EVjQzJEJ1xd\nIohVMK9DrOPA4czSjR55ZqO8rhveTuEPZRcg0fC1suANnZiSMxbPesi8RZjefP7y\nl3hpQICYqKPQMT+kbrIQjMHNQpKUtrZQujg4Zq58Bw1MRZBbooFVv7Hlr76z9Ppw\nMiog7HZz4jD3Vpivb52oI7lH99/OtgQ/Gc84WZd7zxCPrbGaYtsQBlVdYwpUxhPA\nNha3wAVOt1cs2sTWLIRriyKV5OIGJXvNiOvqyNDfnndfJPcNuLrdNn6A9d2eHUPf\nUZDup4/hnea2RpRZKALvdHjDVgSZCrybx6m6nAqSpFBmw2HeTO/C3QiF/o5LrELv\nL7CIZaCfqUvSgJEKfZNV\n=csm6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6bb836803674431f6b34538c7ebd24b067cdc874\nparent d4ba51c46384265b00131fb05429486804103196\nauthor Kavish Kartha <33845687+kavishkartha05@users.noreply.github.com> 1782974693 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782974693 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): move `get_sync()` inside try in `check_async_task` and `cancel_async_task` (#3967)\n\nFixes #3958 \n\n---\n\n`check_async_task` and `cancel_async_task` called `clients.get_sync()`\nbefore their `try/except` blocks, letting `ValueError` escape unhandled\nwhen an async subagent has no URL configured. Moved both calls inside\nthe existing `try/except`, matching the pattern already used in\n`start_async_task` and `update_async_task`.\n\n## Social handles (optional)\n<!-- If you'd like a shoutout on release, add your socials below -->\nTwitter: @kavishkartha31\nLinkedIn: https://linkedin.com/in/kavish-kartha\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-02T06:44:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b0d92c0f38ca0aa037b56e26b2b0d322cdd07856","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b0d92c0f38ca0aa037b56e26b2b0d322cdd07856","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b0d92c0f38ca0aa037b56e26b2b0d322cdd07856/comments","author":{"login":"kavishkartha05","id":33845687,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzODQ1Njg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33845687?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kavishkartha05","html_url":"https://github.com/kavishkartha05","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kavishkartha05/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kavishkartha05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kavishkartha05/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kavishkartha05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kavishkartha05/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kavishkartha05/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kavishkartha05/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kavishkartha05/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kavishkartha05/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web