open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bb852ebe1e43abc608ba27f2a0aa3618ce4e5605","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/bb852ebe1e43abc608ba27f2a0aa3618ce4e5605"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ac386488033303f0657c295d82c7722be78948cc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRZruCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR8cQADyIyJIhs4Ky9w8XHiigwclG\nqz47vDalMtkWw1AgN/WqynCHaTEcJwp2aXfoCOeyApHRM9SqiaVBoHVzVD+OqQBO\nsZmfJ890WH57QFnPt4uRJZSSfpYfpseVj4uQvpIebDvcEfNg/crRhLHN+zOA//ve\nGZRz7TYU6zk/4Bu8GldBQ1fq1EKzkPCEP0KK2vrDq3QcIpprM9lF911ysP2EqmbZ\nrF101McmyValH+Ey5K9wrnyoBbBDk1KD4smzSrY4Nt9y9x0al2AEFj5ineTK+b6Z\nZnc0tEPw+tjfvPTW2aXARKmNCGexiPLrY11coZjszliQM8sSmU/0x6NLMEAZnKw4\nUJ9l/YmXzSMHIn0oaDP65H6BKFBCYSDdyfFyIPbXgqauInS/osLArheVXrfGWDBV\n2CcC9b8EjAek4yMDq9ueit3CA1J6cb8Ne9crMtHk0s+4lNzotfDkAHczWPpQWY0I\n1uddYIW1+1zIDTePae9DDQ9eDjr+tWGBdoAHe9kZyTHzykdxoZLlPVqSXhnpeCKW\nH6UXKxkrVZ/IpC/HKh3V6u+OvRMppo8eOLd/MCZAiBUZa49ROzaJ7Z7JyKogmRS4\nbicyNJb5ccP3d1k34EHKAXNxgCjXQ7xN5ZOV7U7nHEeHtP6/bXgjwWP3ArZXltN6\nfGMNVrCCVjy1lQJe6bYx\n=7rlu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bb852ebe1e43abc608ba27f2a0aa3618ce4e5605\nparent 9870cd9efbf57ccf1c38c423c65227722970461d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782946542 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782946542 -0400\n\nstyle(code): collapse `read_file` output preview by default (#4362)\n\n`read_file` tool calls now collapse their output preview by default in\nthe TUI; expand with click or Ctrl+O to view the file contents.\n\n---\n\nThe `read_file` tool's file path is already shown in the tool header, so\nechoing the file contents inline as an output preview is redundant\nnoise. This collapses `read_file` output by default — showing an expand\naffordance instead — while keeping the full content viewable via\nclick/Ctrl+O.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e968fe6a-3495-16c5-a428-b01012c77c04)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-01T22:55:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ac386488033303f0657c295d82c7722be78948cc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ac386488033303f0657c295d82c7722be78948cc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ac386488033303f0657c295d82c7722be78948cc/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9870cd9efbf57ccf1c38c423c65227722970461d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9870cd9efbf57ccf1c38c423c65227722970461d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9870cd9efbf57ccf1c38c423c65227722970461d"}]},{"sha":"9870cd9efbf57ccf1c38c423c65227722970461d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk4NzBjZDllZmJmNTdjY2YxYzM4YzQyM2M2NTIyNzcyMjk3MDQ2MWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-01T22:36:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-01T22:36:38Z"},"message":"style(code): order `/model` selector by provider availability (#4369)\n\nThe `/model` selector now lists providers you can use (have credentials\nfor) at the top.\n\n---\n\nIn the `/model` selector, the provider groups were rendered in a fixed\ndiscovery order, so a user whose only usable provider (e.g.\n`openai_codex`) sat low in the list had to scroll or search to reach it.\nThis sorts the unfiltered default view so providers the user can\nactually use float to the top, with missing-credential providers above\nnot-installed ones. A search still ranks by fuzzy score, so that path is\nunchanged. The pinned \"Recent\" section stays first.\n\nRequested by @tom21100227.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ad6b5403-7427-49c7-620e-0d070f2f9a40)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"657ee9f8c0f469a9c2e6b95ffcf2e7f8bc147fcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/657ee9f8c0f469a9c2e6b95ffcf2e7f8bc147fcd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9870cd9efbf57ccf1c38c423c65227722970461d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRZZ2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8Z4QAD8TCkQyth8OQQYEHXh8POYi\nYRGoRIkk+MozqKF+dOL3NCg7FAQpbo9v67Bk0tiK/A91TFObdBq7YP9uTTIM4m9Y\ne25ZVior/r8vx1bdtkYVLnUb9e5b8lB1ol+K4vFPVfkTwLkyONmQa+iBNHlQI26M\n6k84YAVa9CpEEtWgon8y3V1gBPRGy0G9ACGjng5poXacFDe7tXCmHshME5xjS6Q7\noTiL3LkL0njtNbFRGX0S83fIi+W/S5S3XMUpGxNGqprYz9vp6G27rXIUrHslVO6o\nsh2gfNHToiu4PXWUkEByCMLVUmFfR0x8m1XrbBK5rBu7iGjsOrN5S6EXe35GFIlf\ns0c0uSASiQaUeGr+lmQh6N6uaSvBcGkErG3mV3SKJVU2dIvzNzbyMRZGjiMoXVge\n5Z0dh/rJJl9fLf8MJjjcpHYAaNe4altn2cWntkvgfdOYC/VRoV+7HJianMpiEwoX\nUfaWPwisssPn9eqjrRlQJWrbS3TZnbcTg8GwLx3UiLio7zvt7EURkWai2fbeVxHl\nPUp4/5Jdcm9lc+OPovYEyN1qs4jXWSg3rTb60JD9rtFwAr4LdM0L5wxNEBM8gUh/\nKHTZvgolOSbvmI2TnFv6w7gCGBl6oIN9jCqFdZI/UO/dwfASYS9aayhx/Wc7ayR1\ncLvnQgGRSzb5lIRl5s3G\n=XBJ/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 657ee9f8c0f469a9c2e6b95ffcf2e7f8bc147fcd\nparent 11f3ea3750f1631b38a45a46110afa7b99cfb508\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782945398 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782945398 -0400\n\nstyle(code): order `/model` selector by provider availability (#4369)\n\nThe `/model` selector now lists providers you can use (have credentials\nfor) at the top.\n\n---\n\nIn the `/model` selector, the provider groups were rendered in a fixed\ndiscovery order, so a user whose only usable provider (e.g.\n`openai_codex`) sat low in the list had to scroll or search to reach it.\nThis sorts the unfiltered default view so providers the user can\nactually use float to the top, with missing-credential providers above\nnot-installed ones. A search still ranks by fuzzy score, so that path is\nunchanged. The pinned \"Recent\" section stays first.\n\nRequested by @tom21100227.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/ad6b5403-7427-49c7-620e-0d070f2f9a40)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-01T22:36:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9870cd9efbf57ccf1c38c423c65227722970461d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9870cd9efbf57ccf1c38c423c65227722970461d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9870cd9efbf57ccf1c38c423c65227722970461d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"11f3ea3750f1631b38a45a46110afa7b99cfb508","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/11f3ea3750f1631b38a45a46110afa7b99cfb508","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/11f3ea3750f1631b38a45a46110afa7b99cfb508"}]},{"sha":"11f3ea3750f1631b38a45a46110afa7b99cfb508","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDExZjNlYTM3NTBmMTYzMWIzOGE0NWE0NjExMGFmYTdiOTljZmI1MDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-01T22:17:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-01T22:17:23Z"},"message":"style(code): delay tool Running timer until 10s elapsed (#4390)\n\nTool-call rows now only show the elapsed-time counter after a tool has\nbeen running for 10 seconds.\n\n---\n\nThe tool-call \"Running...\" status rendered its elapsed-time counter from\nthe first animation tick, so the timer flashed on briefly even for fast\ntools. This gates the `(Ns)` counter behind a 10s threshold\n(`_RUNNING_TIMER_THRESHOLD_SECS`) so it only appears once a tool is\ngenuinely slow; the spinner and \"Running...\" text still show\nimmediately.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/204de007-f224-2ec2-ad79-a941cdbca90a)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8597ed851e313fa03d0cbbb6c13a039a7f61d6f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8597ed851e313fa03d0cbbb6c13a039a7f61d6f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/11f3ea3750f1631b38a45a46110afa7b99cfb508","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRZHzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAskYQAEBH7T+NBbx8QqDJpI50QIQF\nxGdnelMs5noJi23Sn1jLzKvHqXlZFcp2h6C+pCeVlN3rLleQLWXD21dC/y4FVTPt\n3NLlSMn4T8BYRhozeQlSXsDWxgCzGHC/mGg0H9e6/4XbXruyuovmSJMGcfC/H0mZ\nAIWmzis3BFFg/HGvSgznMl/pwei8K94GndX9BsaG4+yZjZTOpi19KSaj6ZN3mJJv\nO7MO4rwh/tPUlh74CpWw3gNgNg+cKua4pXmBIpf40YwwyRqvJ2fVhNmMrAIE22Oe\nwMwXKTwK0/YrI8bApRFt/b6f2Co2Gw7rhWDpunp+6rckrIX3p7ORi58rBkZwTeQD\nThQMsmjOcD0I+lRKG2uBPIDKto+cW58qYt3xFIwzobF5hLKwoC/YuXD8XfrFX65h\nefXwUgRlbgagHyLNun8RYBGmLmz+eX34Uip+QYxvKoqjsg/BAu4C8s6oo6x/XDzG\nWHdUldbFwqO7WXokxVHztkT1KdlSAOM/QWt6spW5uuIUquKqs7Z5GsOqrJyzY236\ni5nOGCiwloD+NeuntvF/VsfKrxzT0dgMl5qRLgJycs8RN+zDioI+cbREiy6U0jP7\nRQS+8rEbc+9VRpXRJDwDnYYnMJGSG8lPwLMNf6y49rHn8j8QbF/ZDomMDKPhOjX9\nyhwZKcx/mBOFcCAEns0z\n=7szf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8597ed851e313fa03d0cbbb6c13a039a7f61d6f3\nparent bbd0f0d1ddc9d22d399a819d7b4363f7997d119e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782944243 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782944243 -0400\n\nstyle(code): delay tool Running timer until 10s elapsed (#4390)\n\nTool-call rows now only show the elapsed-time counter after a tool has\nbeen running for 10 seconds.\n\n---\n\nThe tool-call \"Running...\" status rendered its elapsed-time counter from\nthe first animation tick, so the timer flashed on briefly even for fast\ntools. This gates the `(Ns)` counter behind a 10s threshold\n(`_RUNNING_TIMER_THRESHOLD_SECS`) so it only appears once a tool is\ngenuinely slow; the spinner and \"Running...\" text still show\nimmediately.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/204de007-f224-2ec2-ad79-a941cdbca90a)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-01T22:17:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/11f3ea3750f1631b38a45a46110afa7b99cfb508","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/11f3ea3750f1631b38a45a46110afa7b99cfb508","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/11f3ea3750f1631b38a45a46110afa7b99cfb508/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bbd0f0d1ddc9d22d399a819d7b4363f7997d119e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bbd0f0d1ddc9d22d399a819d7b4363f7997d119e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bbd0f0d1ddc9d22d399a819d7b4363f7997d119e"}]},{"sha":"bbd0f0d1ddc9d22d399a819d7b4363f7997d119e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJiZDBmMGQxZGRjOWQyMmQzOTlhODE5ZDdiNDM2M2Y3OTk3ZDExOWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-01T22:13:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-01T22:13:17Z"},"message":"fix(code): persist resume model state privately (#4400)\n\nDeep Agents Code now records resume model state privately after\nsuccessful model calls, including model params, without exposing the\ninternal `effective_model` runtime context field in LangSmith traces.\n\n```dcode -r 019f1a63-1fca-70a3-90bb-e94458e61f29```\n\n---\n\nModel resume bookkeeping now stays in private checkpoint state instead of being carried through runtime context as `effective_model`. The model middleware records the actual model request that completed, which also avoids persisting a requested override when server-side resolution falls back to the previous model.\n\n## Changes\n- Remove `effective_model` from `CLIContext` so it no longer appears as LangSmith trace metadata.\n- Move `_model_spec` persistence into `ConfigurableModelMiddleware`, emitted after a successful model response using `ExtendedModelResponse` and a private state update.\n- Persist `_model_params` alongside `_model_spec` so resumed sessions restore invocation params such as `temperature` or `max_tokens`.\n- Keep subagent model middleware from writing parent-thread resume metadata.\n- Leave `ResumeStateMiddleware` focused on `_context_tokens`, with model metadata owned by the middleware that resolves the actual request.","tree":{"sha":"b98497521ea319b7090c6caa466a73168a9b0ef3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b98497521ea319b7090c6caa466a73168a9b0ef3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/bbd0f0d1ddc9d22d399a819d7b4363f7997d119e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRZD9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT90QAFVhOldb2leWyMqVCnXCPn4i\nxHO3zDSotxCojcOskcCV2es4ynPzqtsicu4IEwjSW0G4yPdymiQ05LJXQ3nrjZeQ\nKZX5uVfxjeCPqbLVwIMh12ISGGTXYvL8pTZEtjkv8ifeeM42719Po7JrOAT1PI6M\nf/4LqpIfdcKl04WQah8CuvnSBzFPhkk8w51SV25tHP6nQTkNEwRISjn48jRFokeF\nS1EEWB9nRoswVy3M+z/iWDU0y+52OWG0yK52ip9lg0x+43NLA52StJyoJP85sU4O\nbcR2HK+2M2mV11OnV6xTr8kI/bvch7bVRBSksrClA/XWOUScM6LTinsD4SjuaIT9\np9gfOWw0OgOalPeeBCeYuCclPPmzo2lrZ2Gq/Maaog07BgRklgv5+qyIuI4plCEd\n2MWCF7IevyGYwhPQ015JHITSho8mOAzowm/qSSq4PQvhfwSHReyEAk7PSQJ1N3Hb\nZg+qf2dqdIClErxGqhY0qI9Nqd3JD4SYVHc/PXyzLoNp5Wti/PHBHX4LiiFsQNEc\n7tovYBf+rlw0kxtqIFWD4ovbr0E3WKOUacbJm/OuHfoenU+qvId/02omeayuQBpL\nlL42w4T6ICMeyQ+gdJFMfCP8CQWqW8nMdXliGmg5ETOdIEWMjZ5bxRoYzibFm9dl\nBaq9lep51+PSByFV1zkV\n=jXjn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b98497521ea319b7090c6caa466a73168a9b0ef3\nparent 434f29e5cb3d94988e2a4d80b78452bee4b10812\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782943997 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782943997 -0400\n\nfix(code): persist resume model state privately (#4400)\n\nDeep Agents Code now records resume model state privately after\nsuccessful model calls, including model params, without exposing the\ninternal `effective_model` runtime context field in LangSmith traces.\n\n```dcode -r 019f1a63-1fca-70a3-90bb-e94458e61f29```\n\n---\n\nModel resume bookkeeping now stays in private checkpoint state instead of being carried through runtime context as `effective_model`. The model middleware records the actual model request that completed, which also avoids persisting a requested override when server-side resolution falls back to the previous model.\n\n## Changes\n- Remove `effective_model` from `CLIContext` so it no longer appears as LangSmith trace metadata.\n- Move `_model_spec` persistence into `ConfigurableModelMiddleware`, emitted after a successful model response using `ExtendedModelResponse` and a private state update.\n- Persist `_model_params` alongside `_model_spec` so resumed sessions restore invocation params such as `temperature` or `max_tokens`.\n- Keep subagent model middleware from writing parent-thread resume metadata.\n- Leave `ResumeStateMiddleware` focused on `_context_tokens`, with model metadata owned by the middleware that resolves the actual request.","verified_at":"2026-07-01T22:13:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bbd0f0d1ddc9d22d399a819d7b4363f7997d119e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bbd0f0d1ddc9d22d399a819d7b4363f7997d119e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bbd0f0d1ddc9d22d399a819d7b4363f7997d119e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"434f29e5cb3d94988e2a4d80b78452bee4b10812","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/434f29e5cb3d94988e2a4d80b78452bee4b10812","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/434f29e5cb3d94988e2a4d80b78452bee4b10812"}]},{"sha":"434f29e5cb3d94988e2a4d80b78452bee4b10812","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQzNGYyOWU1Y2IzZDk0OTg4ZTJhNGQ4MGI3ODQ1MmJlZTRiMTA4MTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-01T21:20:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-01T21:20:39Z"},"message":"feat(code): toast when opening a clicked URL (#4368)\n\nClicking a URL in the interactive TUI now shows a confirmation toast\nindicating that the link is opening in the default browser.\n\n---\n\nClicking links in the TUI previously opened the browser silently, with\nno in-app feedback. Shared link handling now posts an informational\ntoast on successful opens:\n\n`Opening URL in default browser: <url>`\n\nThe displayed URL is sanitized with `strip_dangerous_unicode` and\nrendered with `markup=False`, matching the existing blocked-URL and\nbrowser-failure notifications.\n\nThis covers both Rich style links and Textual Markdown links, including\nassistant messages, the startup splash LangSmith tracing links, `/auth`\ndocs links, MCP login, thread selector, welcome, and similar modal/link\nsurfaces that share the helper.\n\nThe success toast is enabled by default and can be disabled with either:\n\n```toml\n[ui]\nshow_url_open_toast = false\n```\n\nor:\n\n```bash\nDEEPAGENTS_CODE_SHOW_URL_OPEN_TOAST=0\n```\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0c261ed0-9c77-04cb-35fa-cb8f1c1da3db)\n\nCredit to @tom21100227 for the initial idea\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"16afab551c518b4529c8e9ce4dd9ccb53f237084","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/16afab551c518b4529c8e9ce4dd9ccb53f237084"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/434f29e5cb3d94988e2a4d80b78452bee4b10812","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRYSnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5oEQAJfAeFRk1MRB4/D/JsLmL4ok\nl9fTKK6in5IyueSB+WTljVvP0/sVhiyyr+gROy1AcoL6linKRY7Y1Eu4kM3IrcJU\noMoUcpZXM24uu51Oh25AkEzMhzyjOAUyKOl2XKXm9ODT/m2gk5NfO/Cqe5loTgWl\nwlNuaDZ/ufzJoHIfdXnD24cqv8fTHNXdp2jJ7z+1pQAa9j9rCKKQJW1tziN9JaWL\nEwR15wy294++ccn6YonZ9WxrohoFAvvj2M8GO8YQNHwQRzyWn8y0vkumlPXeb6D5\n9fJfgMcX/yioVg/woE4Bh2QjOietBvkrD1D6YgJwrzNXH53XWR5uiuzsTHqNFklZ\nbv/lT5fDc51yk+ccMF4l8s2CGv/QjDwg23W9S8N5HGtDhX/Zl+KjRtySr/jio8gf\nT4eCtT9Ggb6C6YJsRTjoYIZ0B5s+Do+T0B3XJzQTSU5TOPowxmzFMT6HdcUnV6G6\nFlYeBL/trXXSl1MlZYzjv+dmdYPQ1bv40qF1wT/QiasWs6fSkiakJkCR6Rbe+1qY\npyXfF65orrWUmWB2+4hkGRjSDnbc6qVuIe7UqEbm+Yp44iLDho14Oy1ENRza3BW4\nPFMs3fIbnZQ/AJZTUMlBOZjapEzThLzLo6rNImfHdlkzCUkiz9mIokgFSKpCpYt0\nzaqGr0EiYa7/0pIKs4Vj\n=nEyN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 16afab551c518b4529c8e9ce4dd9ccb53f237084\nparent fa5e8b91d6d3284cf2480777a2b2e79548351da8\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782940839 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782940839 -0400\n\nfeat(code): toast when opening a clicked URL (#4368)\n\nClicking a URL in the interactive TUI now shows a confirmation toast\nindicating that the link is opening in the default browser.\n\n---\n\nClicking links in the TUI previously opened the browser silently, with\nno in-app feedback. Shared link handling now posts an informational\ntoast on successful opens:\n\n`Opening URL in default browser: <url>`\n\nThe displayed URL is sanitized with `strip_dangerous_unicode` and\nrendered with `markup=False`, matching the existing blocked-URL and\nbrowser-failure notifications.\n\nThis covers both Rich style links and Textual Markdown links, including\nassistant messages, the startup splash LangSmith tracing links, `/auth`\ndocs links, MCP login, thread selector, welcome, and similar modal/link\nsurfaces that share the helper.\n\nThe success toast is enabled by default and can be disabled with either:\n\n```toml\n[ui]\nshow_url_open_toast = false\n```\n\nor:\n\n```bash\nDEEPAGENTS_CODE_SHOW_URL_OPEN_TOAST=0\n```\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/0c261ed0-9c77-04cb-35fa-cb8f1c1da3db)\n\nCredit to @tom21100227 for the initial idea\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-07-01T21:20:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/434f29e5cb3d94988e2a4d80b78452bee4b10812","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/434f29e5cb3d94988e2a4d80b78452bee4b10812","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/434f29e5cb3d94988e2a4d80b78452bee4b10812/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/m