,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d6692a7c713490f170b17510d613e02ee37574ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d6692a7c713490f170b17510d613e02ee37574ab","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d6692a7c713490f170b17510d613e02ee37574ab"}]},{"sha":"d6692a7c713490f170b17510d613e02ee37574ab","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ2NjkyYTdjNzEzNDkwZjE3MGIxNzUxMGQ2MTNlMDJlZTM3NTc0YWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-01T07:18:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-01T07:18:04Z"},"message":"feat(code,sdk): add rubric iteration controls (#4405)\n\nCloses #4404\n\nDeep Agents Code now uses clearer acceptance-criteria grading messages,\nlets the rubric grader inspect offloaded tool-result evidence referenced\nin the transcript, defers the rubric iteration default to the SDK, and\nadds interactive grader controls for goals and rubrics.\n\n---\n\nThis improves the goal and rubric grading UX so the status messages\ndescribe the acceptance criteria check rather than implying the rubric\ntext itself is wrong. When grading fails with `needs_revision`, the UI\nnow says the changes need revision. Iteration numbers are hidden unless\nthe user explicitly configured an iteration cap, keeping the default\n`/goal` and `/rubric` flow less noisy.\n\nDeep Agents Code no longer sets its own default rubric iteration cap. If\nthe user does not pass `--rubric-max-iterations`, dcode omits\n`max_iterations` and lets `RubricMiddleware` use the SDK default.\nExplicit `--rubric-max-iterations` values are still forwarded, and the\nSDK now accepts any positive cap instead of enforcing the previous hard\nupper bound.\n\nThe rubric grader also gets a narrow `read_file` tool that can only\ninspect `/large_tool_results/` paths explicitly referenced in the\ntranscript. This gives the grader a way to verify offloaded evidence\nwithout exposing broader filesystem access or waiting for an SDK-level\ntranscript reconstruction change.\n\nThe TUI now exposes `/rubric max-iterations <N|clear>` and `/goal\nmax-iterations <N|clear>` for interactive sessions. Changing the value\nrestarts the app-owned LangGraph server so the construction-time\n`RubricMiddleware` setting takes effect. `/goal model\n[provider:model|clear]` and `/goal max-iterations` are goal-first entry\npoints for the same shared grader settings surfaced by `/rubric model`\nand `/rubric max-iterations`.","tree":{"sha":"a1311ac5155fd3557ac74f5d945741e4e851085f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a1311ac5155fd3557ac74f5d945741e4e851085f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d6692a7c713490f170b17510d613e02ee37574ab","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRL8sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACEAQABiOEVjv4xHaJBmI744kM/dV\nINFROw+NSYFoo9fTmP0sbvHgx0+lhG0t37dd+rvE1olSJ2RmXLMpE5Hi9uZ7LcmP\nuIWpEmGffQdyQURddUx6irSEj3xXrUWkNMkWrVC14FCnolPBmg+zcElcTS1WJE79\n9quVTC9Hksy2wFytgyRAGjaGdOCl5PtXrXuT3CjoZMlx9ZdsPIZQ9/VoAVLpPbkg\nrhI5+26k30F+KWVmX/KDg5dY0C0vwwgtEzScndVdGZf2QoahBLKEsTFWJLnqROW1\nxwPOgHLv/xkVAYI0KThtORv0reDaz0Xxbs56qwNbCMMXFzo71fH90m4vJlleJOJR\nhKlb19Aveu9zpOMCUIpYacMEWN9gMNprJLOrOxyVP2dDVMyiuJJQN/zBnnZBsSTx\nVw0tbEILlsWR2+/+BeKJbkIQRJmSHwuA4dc/4QPUl06Kludf77R8qJQ9UCgVrDS0\nKx/8Ru6VG2lq1Y/92YREVJLKJHyhSArk9HiLSY+Hxi5jgQUUzibsTsYQu9lccNLY\nViOH2X2CWJ/bV2In0474bqdP/zvEMnALTUE5XsiwNNB+tMk1Syksvo7TrQTX7mpZ\nHSWyhln2VO1JvSPR0aGMpgHlXuc72+Qu7kIwTujjkWGFml6bPKLZ/qlurbN/5V+2\n7VK+bU+ELFP/LU+uityI\n=AX9E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a1311ac5155fd3557ac74f5d945741e4e851085f\nparent a51c8d2b1723d143439a1466f5a49a52c442bdfc\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782890284 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782890284 -0400\n\nfeat(code,sdk): add rubric iteration controls (#4405)\n\nCloses #4404\n\nDeep Agents Code now uses clearer acceptance-criteria grading messages,\nlets the rubric grader inspect offloaded tool-result evidence referenced\nin the transcript, defers the rubric iteration default to the SDK, and\nadds interactive grader controls for goals and rubrics.\n\n---\n\nThis improves the goal and rubric grading UX so the status messages\ndescribe the acceptance criteria check rather than implying the rubric\ntext itself is wrong. When grading fails with `needs_revision`, the UI\nnow says the changes need revision. Iteration numbers are hidden unless\nthe user explicitly configured an iteration cap, keeping the default\n`/goal` and `/rubric` flow less noisy.\n\nDeep Agents Code no longer sets its own default rubric iteration cap. If\nthe user does not pass `--rubric-max-iterations`, dcode omits\n`max_iterations` and lets `RubricMiddleware` use the SDK default.\nExplicit `--rubric-max-iterations` values are still forwarded, and the\nSDK now accepts any positive cap instead of enforcing the previous hard\nupper bound.\n\nThe rubric grader also gets a narrow `read_file` tool that can only\ninspect `/large_tool_results/` paths explicitly referenced in the\ntranscript. This gives the grader a way to verify offloaded evidence\nwithout exposing broader filesystem access or waiting for an SDK-level\ntranscript reconstruction change.\n\nThe TUI now exposes `/rubric max-iterations <N|clear>` and `/goal\nmax-iterations <N|clear>` for interactive sessions. Changing the value\nrestarts the app-owned LangGraph server so the construction-time\n`RubricMiddleware` setting takes effect. `/goal model\n[provider:model|clear]` and `/goal max-iterations` are goal-first entry\npoints for the same shared grader settings surfaced by `/rubric model`\nand `/rubric max-iterations`.","verified_at":"2026-07-01T07:18:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d6692a7c713490f170b17510d613e02ee37574ab","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d6692a7c713490f170b17510d613e02ee37574ab","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d6692a7c713490f170b17510d613e02ee37574ab/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a51c8d2b1723d143439a1466f5a49a52c442bdfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a51c8d2b1723d143439a1466f5a49a52c442bdfc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a51c8d2b1723d143439a1466f5a49a52c442bdfc"}]},{"sha":"a51c8d2b1723d143439a1466f5a49a52c442bdfc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE1MWM4ZDJiMTcyM2QxNDM0MzlhMTQ2NmY1YTQ5YTUyYzQ0MmJkZmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-07-01T04:15:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-01T04:15:09Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): emit terminal rubric iteration status (#4406)\n\n`RubricMiddleware` now emits `max_iterations_reached` in terminal rubric\nevents when the iteration cap is exhausted, instead of emitting a final\n`needs_revision` event that will not loop.\n\n---\n\n`RubricMiddleware` currently emits the raw grader verdict before it\nconverts an exhausted `needs_revision` into `max_iterations_reached`.\nThat means stream-event consumers can render another normal revision\nrequest even though the middleware has already decided to stop.\n\nThis changes the ordering so the middleware computes the terminal cap\nstatus first, then emits and records the same `max_iterations_reached`\nresult through all observability surfaces: private state,\n`_rubric_evaluations`, `on_evaluation`, stream events, and the warning\nlog.","tree":{"sha":"d777115d4e75b52a321f86d8eff7728667cd9ac7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d777115d4e75b52a321f86d8eff7728667cd9ac7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a51c8d2b1723d143439a1466f5a49a52c442bdfc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqRJRNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5lAQAFWvro+3AVMvQnrdYp6/pVpZ\nl28eW5Yi/VN575IoKtxVwngtLxejU6GhbROYHK4DRQG8Cu8Kyn1BK2jPgp56cT27\nxJ38yQwNEFPe+h/oh2kSLOLsxvMq+EZMhyFWKJrRozHghIrbCE3AmhHtqVo+V4pF\nLaGRg8gKkTaPuHruE3+R3fgrimqbtxQw4weAWc/ThLHegEaurI0k+jhU6Mk+Mhxr\norDH3crDmVh/a7Fv/t7arrY25fYc+to9Md80oPrHOMOeqQmlmV2BmTDD/HH/wv53\nDr7gKBrybXb7u0VYlcN/HJot1SOcd1jeo0AnlAHFFCLa3oWw4au9nLJYdZAJPhXH\nmZfHFTiNfkEhGJfvjmLew8q92zZqzEvFvds4XUzuE70MiUY+16DDz5vEMaFrJQaK\nvaMg34I8dNAp4u/P9V1ZCzantNhlOt0wuC1ZdoZNSmcK0ZnyqxkMxwEG/tUSJXn9\niBC2bvlMEvmtuv/s8y7YGOLejiWFvKTnjqzcDyEKDhB8Q+t0BgxHy21jBRkcViXv\nSAu4/wO3hD9u6zxDQwxZlMz+/DJyS/XqZ4k5Iv2HWjm4XnJTy231Z5rJ+VEKh0jA\nsKzO7JlSRiyJKDuq5lOyt0AsIiEj4qc/DxSihuedZiSHy/DWPB147pwS+imK+psw\nHLGFqiUNfbvuyuacX2tl\n=nzar\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d777115d4e75b52a321f86d8eff7728667cd9ac7\nparent 42aeec1ecd407d45805585567ce0b9d0c8a0f8d7\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782879309 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782879309 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): emit terminal rubric iteration status (#4406)\n\n`RubricMiddleware` now emits `max_iterations_reached` in terminal rubric\nevents when the iteration cap is exhausted, instead of emitting a final\n`needs_revision` event that will not loop.\n\n---\n\n`RubricMiddleware` currently emits the raw grader verdict before it\nconverts an exhausted `needs_revision` into `max_iterations_reached`.\nThat means stream-event consumers can render another normal revision\nrequest even though the middleware has already decided to stop.\n\nThis changes the ordering so the middleware computes the terminal cap\nstatus first, then emits and records the same `max_iterations_reached`\nresult through all observability surfaces: private state,\n`_rubric_evaluations`, `on_evaluation`, stream events, and the warning\nlog.","verified_at":"2026-07-01T04:15:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a51c8d2b1723d143439a1466f5a49a52c442bdfc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a51c8d2b1723d143439a1466f5a49a52c442bdfc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a51c8d2b1723d143439a1466f5a49a52c442bdfc/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"42aeec1ecd407d45805585567ce0b9d0c8a0f8d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/42aeec1ecd407d45805585567ce0b9d0c8a0f8d7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/42aeec1ecd407d45805585567ce0b9d0c8a0f8d7"}]}]